rent_review_manual.md:28:   - Prompt change: add visible non-river obstacle islands inside the river so the mover must detour or be blocked by internal obstacles rather than only by outer corridor width.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/review/332f06d7_parent_review_manual.md:40:| 332f06d7 | D11 | 0 | 带分叉通道 | 通过 |\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/review/332f06d7_parent_review_manual.md:41:| 332f06d7 | D11 | 2 | 带障碍物通道 | 通过 |\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/review/de809cff_parent_review.md:8:| de809cff | D1 | 0 | 凹痕变为对侧色十字形而非3x3方块 | 12/12 | ✓ |\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/review/de809cff_parent_review.md:25:## D1/0 凹痕变为对侧色十字形而非3x3方块\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/review/332f06d7_parent_review.md:30:| 332f06d7 | D10 | 1 | 阻塞时标记通道 | 12/12 | ✓ |\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/review/332f06d7_parent_review.md:33:| 332f06d7 | D11 | 0 | 带分叉通道 | 12/12 | ⚠ |\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/review/332f06d7_parent_review.md:34:| 332f06d7 | D11 | 1 | 环形通道 | 12/12 | ✓ |\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/review/332f06d7_parent_review.md:35:| 332f06d7 | D11 | 2 | 带障碍物通道 | 12/12 | ⚠ |\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/review/332f06d7_parent_review.md:37:| 332f06d7 | D12 | 2 | 多色通道分段 | 12/12 | ✓ |\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/review/332f06d7_parent_review.md:38:| 332f06d7 | D13 | 1 | 方块尺寸由通道编码 | 12/12 | ✓ |\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/review/332f06d7_parent_review.md:41:| 332f06d7 | D15 | 1 | 单向通道可达性 | 12/12 | ✓ |\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/review/332f06d7_parent_review.md:289:## D10/1 阻塞时标记通道\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/review/332f06d7_parent_review.md:322:## D11/0 带分叉通道\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/review/332f06d7_parent_review.md:333:## D11/1 环形通道\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/review/332f06d7_parent_review.md:344:## D11/2 带障碍物通道\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/review/332f06d7_parent_review.md:366:## D12/2 多色通道分段\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/review/332f06d7_parent_review.md:377:## D13/1 方块尺寸由通道编码\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/review/332f06d7_parent_review.md:410:## D15/1 单向通道可达性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/review/b10624e5_prompt_doc_summary.json:12:    \"change_line\": \"锚块形状匹配而非颜色匹配 — 锚块不再统一为方形，而是有不同形状（L形、T形、十字形等），源和目标通过锚块形状而非颜色配对。缩放因子可由锚块面积比或外接矩形比决定。解题者需要先进行形状分类再匹配。\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/29/code.py:32:#   让蓝水先占据粗糙台阶和右侧盆地，再把红水放进去。于是红水虽然起点更低，却更晚遇到通道。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/29/code.py:41:# - 几何结构只使用一个很窄的主通道和一个右侧接收盆地，再通过镜像和蓝水高度/宽度的小变化产生样例，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/29/code.py:66:# - 整个场景只保留一个上层导流台、一个下层发射带、一个粗糙肩部和一个右侧接收盆地，避免多通道叠加。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2d0172a1/D5/1/code.py:3:# Change: 色块在输出中规范化为单个前景像素点 → 色块输出为 3x3 十字形\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2d0172a1/D9/0/code.py:26:#   In the variant, the outer frame becomes visibly roomy while the inner frame stays tight.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2d0172a1/D9/0/code.py:46:# - Visual observability: depth-2 trees are emphasized so humans can compare roomy outer frames\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/45/code.py:74:# - 生成器还保证至少一部分水离开源高台并进入底盆，否则这两个新增通道都不够明显。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/1/code.py:3:# Name: 角标记框架+十字形色块\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c416de3/16/code.py:39:  with radius 2 never overlap each other or the connector corridor. Connectors use\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/1/code.py:53:#   - Regions are at least 5x5, which leaves enough room for a visible spiral\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/3/code.py:41:#    - The original diagonal code assumes \"open side corridor\" is part of legality. D2/0 breaks\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/11/code.py:339:    - If blocked from below, it may move diagonally downward through an open side corridor; if both diagonals are open, choose the left one.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/3/code.py:22:#    原题在每个墙围成的房间里读取“边界深度 -> 颜色”的调色板，然后按切比雪夫深度\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/3/code.py:25:#    - D4/1：房间里额外出现的多像素色块是阻挡物，波前不能穿过它们。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/3/code.py:26:#    小例子：一个 8x8 房间里，左上/右上/左下有三个单像素种子，中部偏右有一个 2x3\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/3/code.py:43:#    生成器仍通过递归矩形切分得到 3-6 个房间。种子只放在模板锚点上，阻挡块只放在\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/3/code.py:44:#    房间内部、距边界至少 1 格的位置，不与墙、其他阻挡物或种子重叠。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/3/code.py:49:#    每个房间至多一个阻挡块，种子位置从少量模板中选取，区域数量也受限，避免一张图\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/3/code.py:264:    Expand colored seeds through wall-bounded rooms while interior blocker patches stop the waves.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/3/code.py:267:    - One wall color partitions the grid into several 4-connected rooms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/3/code.py:268:    - Inside each room, most cells share a base color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/3/code.py:272:    - In each room, launch a simultaneous 4-neighbor BFS from all single-pixel seeds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/3/code.py:275:    - Blocker cells themselves remain unchanged, and any free cell unreachable from every seed stays in the room's base color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/3/code.py:493:    room_cr = (r0 + r1) / 2.0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/3/code.py:494:    room_cc = (c0 + c1) / 2.0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/3/code.py:497:    return abs(cand_cr - room_cr) + abs(cand_cc - room_cc)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/9/code.py:340:    roomy = [rc for rc in candidates if rc[0] * rc[1] > int(n_cavities)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/9/code.py:341:    pool = roomy if roomy else candidates\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/41/code.py:67:#       guide corridors and final ray segments do not interfere with each other\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/41/code.py:73:#     guides, sources, travel corridors, and blocker cells are chosen from in-bounds lattice lines\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/41/code.py:78:#     repeated \"guide -> blue run -> empty corridor -> collision wall\" motifs make the multi-guide rule inferable from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/7/code.py:45:#   only extends the marker chain along a diagonal that has enough in-bounds room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/42/code.py:50:#    - `_simulate()` 允许多个活动分支，但默认它们不会在狭窄通道内彼此抢占；生成器用分叉后左右分盆来保证。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/35/code.py:29:    corridor before it reaches the deeper pockets that gravity would have filled first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/35/code.py:50:  corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/35/code.py:66:  different edges, and each opens into the same basin corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/35/code.py:73:  corridor where the fronts merge, and a bottom basin network. No auxiliary markers or hidden\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/35/code.py:394:      corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/51/code.py:53:# - 输出里总会有至少 1 格水没有沉到最低盆地，而是停在更高的台面/通道；与“如果继续多轮它还会下去”\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/36/code.py:123:        assert rr >= 0 and int(g[rr, c]) == BG, \"not enough headroom to place settled water\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/5/code.py:454:    assert count >= 2, \"generator always needs room for one rotated and one flipped query\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/22/code.py:3:# Name: 角落图例指示输出样式+填充矩形框架+十字形色块\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:13:#      while discarding the empty headroom and the upper side source shelf.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/27/code.py:9:# - The generator is output-first and reserves the full hidden route corridor so other triples do not occupy dash gaps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/13/code.py:33:#    puzzle still reads as \"independent rooms\". To keep the new rule legible, it\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/13/code.py:38:#    Samples are rejected unless at least one region has room for a distance-2\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/13/code.py:39:#    ring, so the skip pattern is not hidden inside tiny rooms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/13/code.py:55:#    A human can compare input markers near the middle of rooms with outputs that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/13/code.py:59:#    from room boundaries or from numeric color ids.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/44/code.py:28:#    - The two changes reinforce each other: the larger grid makes room for more cups, and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/44/code.py:29:#      communicating-vessel rule turns that extra room into a genuinely global equalization task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/19/code.py:24:#      room for only 2-3 basins, so the solver would only need to track one or two overflows. Here,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/14/code.py:11:#       there is room for 1-2 distractors in the fixed top band.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/16/code.py:19:#        wave reaches both side corridors and visibly splits into a left and a right branch;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/16/code.py:55:#    - Internal bars are placed strictly inside the chamber walls, leaving enough corridor cells on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/16/code.py:58:#    - From examples alone, a human can see that the source pocket empties into a suspended maze and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/16/code.py:60:#    - The split/merge behavior is directly visible because the output occupies both side corridors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/16/code.py:219:    Key insight: The answer is controlled by graph distance inside a floating obstacle maze, not by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/17/code.py:58:#    - the empty corridors widen from 1 to 2 to 3 to ... cells;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/17/code.py:69:#      first green span; the generator sizes the board and seed runway to leave room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/11/code.py:9:#    boundary of a filled corridor. In terminal-local coordinates with side=+1, one representative output is:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/11/code.py:246:    Re-anchor each irregular segment around a nearby rectangle, then fill the corridor between them.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/11/code.py:260:    - Paint both that outer reroute path and the entire background corridor between the path and the rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/12/code.py:19:#     是围绕房间边界向内收缩的矩形环带。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/12/code.py:23:#   - 小例子: 顶边房间的顶边上有三个控制像素 A/B/C。原题会把它们误读成边界深度 0 的\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/12/code.py:24:#     线索，最多只留下一个颜色槽；融合后则把 A/B/C 当作三个独立源，房间内部出现从\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/12/code.py:48:#   - 仍用递归矩形切墙，因此每个 free component 都是矩形房间，边缘锚点坐标可直接从 bbox\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/12/code.py:50:#   - 只允许在真正位于整张画布外边界上的房间锚点放控制像素；内部房间没有外边缘，因此\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/12/code.py:56:#   - 输入里所有非墙、非底色线索都贴在画布外缘，人眼可以先观察“这些彩点属于哪块房间”，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/12/code.py:57:#     再看输出中同色波前如何向房间内部推进。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/12/code.py:63:#   - 墙、底色、控制像素三类对象角色分明；输出中的竞争分区也按房间独立展开，不会互相覆盖。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/12/code.py:233:    - Any non-base clues for a region appear on the global grid border cells that belong to that region, not inside the room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/12/code.py:240:    Key insight: The edge clues no longer encode boundary-depth palette slots. They are literal spatial origins, so solving requires attaching each border clue to its room and then following multi-source BFS competition from those marker positions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/29/code.py:3:# Name: 十字形补丁+交替中心色+凹痕沿直线排列\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/16/code.py:48:#    passive half-plane empty, and places blobs only in the corridor between source and stop.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/16/code.py:62:#    - There is enough room before the marker for at least two green stripes, so both the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/15/code.py:73:#     bar, creating a long empty corridor before the wrap, and the same-color singleton is the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/2/code.py:14:#    - 差异因此不是“先 L 再虚线”两件孤立的事，而是 solver 必须先恢复完整 L 形 corridor，之后才能在正确的几何顺序上做隔格采样。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/2/code.py:38:#    - obstacle 被约束在 output_route 内侧，且 reserve 覆盖完整 corridor，减少不同对象在同一区域交叠。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/2/code.py:52:#    - solver 假设 route 的完整 corridor 不被别的 triple 占用；generator 用 output_route 做 reserve 来满足。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/2/code.py:490:    - Keep the full rerouted corridor only as an internal route; the visible output paints just route cells 1, 3, 5, ... in order, so the segment becomes a dashed L-shaped wrap with ceil(L/2) painted cells when the full route has length L.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/17/code.py:56:#      the legend and leaving room for off-path marker placement near endpoints.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/5/code.py:9:#     two red endpoints face each other across a 4-cell blank corridor and remain disconnected.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/5/code.py:10:#   - The same sample also contains a different red-red bridge whose blank corridor is only 2-3\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/5/code.py:11:#     cells long; after recoloring the markers, that short corridor is repaired.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/5/code.py:21:#     to the same line color, but the 4-cell corridor stays blank. Another pair at `(9,2)` and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/5/code.py:22:#     `(9,6)` with a 3-cell corridor is filled completely.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/5/code.py:39:#   - The hanging pair is searched inside a fully clear interior corridor; its two components, the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/5/code.py:41:#   - Short-bridge interiors, yellow rays, and hanging corridors are mutually blocked so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/5/code.py:90:    - Red markers replace missing turn/endpoint cells; some red pairs bound a short corridor that should close, while others mark genuine internal hanging endpoints separated by a longer corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/5/code.py:742:def _corridor_clear(occupied: set[tuple[int, int]], cells: set[tuple[int, int]]) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/5/code.py:785:            if not _corridor_clear(occupied, reserve):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/1/code.py:3:# Name: 十字形补丁+4连通邻域判定\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/16/code.py:46:#     - keep only one dominant branched color so the tree topology is legible instead of maze-like\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/16/code.py:64:#    The snake is generated inside an interior corridor that leaves at least two background rows between\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/12/code.py:53:# - New combo assumption: there is enough free room beside the segment center to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/32/code.py:15:#     dominoes clamp the missing corridor from both sides on the same axis;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/32/code.py:26:#     selected. It picks the currently shortest clamped corridor, recolors that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/32/code.py:36:#   the bracket relation readable and prevents giant ambiguous corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/32/code.py:56:#   target and no crossings inside the removed corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/32/code.py:67:#   - repaired corridors are bracketed by two red bars;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/32/code.py:92:#   corridors start fully blank and never overlap yellow old arms or crossings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/32/code.py:593:    - Red dominoes sit in pairs around a blank straight corridor; yellow dominoes sit on the first two cells of an intended new ray from a pivot.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/32/code.py:597:    - Repeatedly find the currently shortest red-domino pair that clamps a blank corridor on that same axis, recolor both dominoes plus the cells between them, and then recompute the remaining candidates on the updated line state.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/37/code.py:50:#    horizontal ray, and the dependent vertical ray occupy clear corridors. Wall\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/17/code.py:513:    - Red singletons sit inside broken line corridors; yellow singletons, when present, still sit beside endpoints that must flip to the marked side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/5/code.py:333:    - The obstacles form an ordered corridor in front of each bar. Recover the segment length and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/22/code.py:9:#     two facing same-color corners in one row/column with a blank corridor of length\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/22/code.py:47:#   - Every generated instance contains at least one short blank corridor bounded by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/22/code.py:48:#     two facing corners of the same color; that corridor is restored in the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/22/code.py:52:#   - The mandatory gap is a single straight corridor, not a pile-up of overlapping\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/20/code.py:43:#   room for multiple colors and crossings while making the width-2 effect\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/25/code.py:491:    # Keep multi-companion lines dominant, but always leave room for simple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/32/code.py:77:# Keep enough headroom for the tall 3-row source layouts so branch coverage\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/30/code.py:51:#     - allow diagonal geometry, but restrict it to straight 45-degree rays rather than arbitrary 8-neighbor mazes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/8/code.py:78:#    corridor, and no cell is overwritten by several different colors in the final\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/6/code.py:608:      exit direction; if the path runs out of room, it truncates at the boundary/blocker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/38/code.py:3:# Name: 十字形补丁+形状编码方向+冲突teal标记\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/_final_summary_20260517.json:5:    \"name\": \"十字形补丁+4连通邻域判定\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/_final_summary_20260517.json:214:    \"name\": \"十字形补丁+边界裁剪+矩形区域\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/_final_summary_20260517.json:297:    \"name\": \"十字形补丁+交替中心色+凹痕沿直线排列\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/_final_summary_20260517.json:392:    \"name\": \"十字形补丁+形状编码方向+冲突teal标记\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/12/code.py:21:#   - The generator always builds at least one such marker-clamped corridor, and at\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/12/code.py:39:#     cell, and their interior corridor contains no crossings or yellow artifacts.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/12/code.py:42:#   - Yellow markers and extra red markers are blocked away from the clamp corridor so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/12/code.py:45:#   - In every generated example there is an obvious red-red corridor whose interior is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/12/code.py:342:    - Red markers sit at both ends of a missing straight corridor; yellow markers sit just beyond a line endpoint and indicate a rerouted arm.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/24/code.py:48:#      base puzzle instead of becoming a dense maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/24/code.py:71:#      again (or the transposed version). Other lines avoid the relay corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/24/code.py:91:#      valid companion. Generator placement reserves the relay corridor so nothing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/24/code.py:460:        raise ValueError(\"No legal step that avoids the relay corridor\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/21/code.py:3:# Name: 十字形补丁+边界裁剪+矩形区域\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:479:    row_room = (H - (int(seed_r0) + h)) if dr == 1 else int(seed_r0)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:480:    col_room = (W - (int(seed_c0) + w)) if dc == 1 else int(seed_c0)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:481:    return 1 + int(min(row_room, col_room))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/9/code.py:47:#    - The generator reserves the entire ray corridor, including skipped blank slots,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/9/code.py:60:#    - Reserved blank corridors keep the empty gaps genuinely empty instead of being\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/9/code.py:603:    \"\"\"Reject plus placements that would sit directly on or beside an existing ray corridor.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/20/code.py:228:                f\"Line {li} ({'row' if by_row else 'col'}) companion must leave room to extend: \"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/19/code.py:29:# - D6/2 changes the endpoint: repetition stops at the next frame on the same corridor,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/19/code.py:42:# - Opposite directions on the same corridor use parallel lanes. This prevents ray overlap\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/19/code.py:72:# - The same frame-to-frame stopping interaction appears on multiple corridors in the output,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/19/code.py:329:    \"\"\"Repeat a tile away from its source until the next frame on that corridor.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/19/code.py:386:    - Stop the repetition when the corridor reaches the next frame, and never overwrite frame pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/19/code.py:648:    # instead of biasing toward the longest corridor. This improves branch coverage across\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/1/code.py:132:    - Generated instances place the marker on a top corner so the downward flow has room to develop, though the solver still accepts any unique corner marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D1/0/code.py:3:# Change: 每个黑色凹痕的3x3邻域多数前景色为A时，凹痕变为3x3的前景色B补丁，中心为teal(8)... → 凹痕变为对侧色十字形而非3x3方块\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/23/code.py:35:#    - The block count is tightened to 3-4. This is the smallest change that makes room for 2-3 motifs per block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/5/code.py:31:#      [seed][blank][copy][blank][copy] and then it stops, even if more room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/5/code.py:58:#    - The generator reserves the entire tile-slot corridor from the seed to the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/22/code.py:21:#   expansion visible room to grow while keeping the rule simple: exactly one matched 3x3 stencil\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/19/code.py:26:#   line per grid.  That keeps the rule visible while avoiding an unreadable maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/19/code.py:326:def _orth_room(edge: str, line: int, H: int, W: int) -> int:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/19/code.py:337:    return sorted(lines, key=lambda line: _orth_room(edge, line, H, W))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/34/code.py:65:#    Reserving whole chunk corridors prevents overlapping partial tails.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/16/code.py:26:#          carve long narrow chambers rather than roughly square rooms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/16/code.py:78:#     - Strip dimensions make the effect read as a long dual-color corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:3:# Name: 通道宽度约束洪填+迷宫墙壁\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:23:#    - This combo replaces that layout with one connected blue maze wall\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:24:#      network. The open space is a tree of rooms joined by doorways. Some\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:26:#    - Example trace: marker at bottom-left enters the maze vestibule. Under\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:28:#      it reaches every room. Under the fused rule, reachability is computed by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:31:#      the inner wall of the width-reachable sub-maze, and blue decorations in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:35:#    - The maze is still simple enough to parse visually: one connected wall\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:36:#      component, orthogonal rooms, and a small number of narrow chokepoints.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:37:#    - The generator uses only 2 room-grid sizes (2x2, 2x3, 3x2, 3x3) and only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:40:#    - At least one entire room-subtree is plain-reachable but width-blocked,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:48:#      narrow doorway would be mistaken for a real passage and the maze would\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:52:#      decorations as isolated interior blobs that never 4-touch the maze wall,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:56:#    - The maze is rendered from non-overlapping rectangular rooms and one-cell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:57:#      wall bands; all coordinates are derived from the room lattice, so there\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:62:#    - Hidden decorations are placed only on interior room cells of blocked\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:70:#    - Because the blocked region is an entire maze branch rather than a tiny\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:75:#      maze wall, one magenta marker, and orange inner-border paint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:76:#    - Decorations live at room interiors, away from walls and doorways, so they\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:77:#      do not visually merge with the structural maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:88:#    - All structural walls belong to one border-touching 4-connected maze\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:267:    Paint the inner wall of the maze region reachable from the corner marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:270:    - Azure is the dominant background, blue pixels form one connected maze-wall\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:272:    - The maze consists of rooms and corridors; some doors are two cells wide,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:274:    - Small interior blue blobs may appear as decorations inside maze rooms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:277:    - Reconstruct the structural maze wall from border-touching blue components,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:283:      side of the maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:284:    - Paint orange on every reachable background cell that lies on the maze's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:288:    Key insight: The maze geometry alone is not enough; you must evaluate door\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:289:    width. Rooms behind a one-cell chokepoint belong to the plain maze, but not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:295:def _room_top_left(room: tuple[int, int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:296:    rr, cc = room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:300:def _room_center(room: tuple[int, int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:301:    r0, c0 = _room_top_left(room)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:305:def _room_inner_spots(room: tuple[int, int]) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:306:    r0, c0 = _room_top_left(room)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:314:def _room_neighbors(room: tuple[int, int], rows: int, cols: int) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:315:    rr, cc = room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:329:        unvisited = [nb for nb in _room_neighbors(cur, rows, cols) if nb not in parent]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:417:    ar, ac = _room_top_left(a)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:418:    br, bc = _room_top_left(b)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:430:    room_rows: int,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:431:    room_cols: int,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:436:    h = room_rows * STEP + 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:437:    w = room_cols * STEP + 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:440:    for rr in range(room_rows):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:441:        for cc in range(room_cols):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:442:            r0, c0 = _room_top_left((rr, cc))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:455:def _reachable_rooms(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:482:    blocked_rooms: list[tuple[int, int]],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:486:    count = min(len(blocked_rooms), rng.randint(*HIDDEN_DECOR_RANGE))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:487:    for room in rng.sample(blocked_rooms, count):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:488:        r, c = _room_center(room)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:496:    reachable_rooms: list[tuple[int, int]],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:497:    marker_room: tuple[int, int],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:504:    candidates = [room for room in reachable_rooms if room != marker_room]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:506:    for room in candidates:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:507:        for r, c in rng.sample(_room_inner_spots(room), len(_room_inner_spots(room))):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:531:    room_rows = rng.choice(ROOM_ROWS_CHOICES)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:532:    room_cols = rng.choice(ROOM_COLS_CHOICES)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:533:    h = room_rows * STEP + 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:534:    w = room_cols * STEP + 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:536:    marker_room = (room_rows - 1, 0)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:538:    parent = _build_tree(room_rows, room_cols, marker_room, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:540:    blocked_roots = _pick_blocked_roots(parent, children, marker_room, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:544:    subtree = _subtree_sets(children, marker_room)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:545:    blocked_rooms_set: set[tuple[int, int]] = set()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:547:        blocked_rooms_set |= subtree[node]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:548:    reachable_rooms_set = _reachable_rooms(marker_room, children, blocked_root_set)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:550:    structural = _render_structural(room_rows, room_cols, parent, blocked_root_set, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:557:    hidden = _place_hidden_decor(grid, sorted(blocked_rooms_set), rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:560:    _place_visible_decor(grid, sorted(reachable_rooms_set), marker_room, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/10/code.py:369:def _corridor_cells(side: str, r: int, c: int, shape: np.ndarray, anchor: tuple[int, int], th: int, tw: int):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/10/code.py:464:            corridor = _corridor_cells(side, r, c, shape, anchor, th, tw)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/10/code.py:465:            if not corridor:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/10/code.py:467:            ok_corridor = True\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/10/code.py:468:            for rr, cc in corridor:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/10/code.py:470:                    ok_corridor = False\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/10/code.py:474:                        ok_corridor = False\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/10/code.py:476:                if not ok_corridor:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/10/code.py:478:            if not ok_corridor:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/10/code.py:482:            for rr, cc in corridor:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/10/code.py:492:                    \"corridor\": corridor,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/10/code.py:562:    global_corridor = [(fr + rr, fc + cc) for rr, cc in hole[\"corridor\"]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/10/code.py:563:    for rr, cc in global_corridor:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/10/code.py:617:                    for rr, cc in global_corridor + outside:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/10/code.py:640:                    for rr, cc in global_corridor + outside:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/4/code.py:27:# - Difference trace on a simple open corridor marker -> A -> B -> C -> D -> E,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/12/code.py:294:    need_room_after: bool,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/12/code.py:297:    reserve = 2 if need_room_after else 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/12/code.py:310:    need_room_after: bool,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/12/code.py:313:    reserve = 2 if need_room_after else 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/16/code.py:21:#    room than 3x3, so the tile geometry is enlarged to 8x8 slots.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/13/code.py:15:#    - Example trace on a small room: if the bottom-left marker can reach an\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/13/code.py:16:#      azure corridor plus one isolated interior blue blob, then the output paints\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/13/code.py:17:#      both the corridor and that blob azure, while the structural wall and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/6/code.py:15:#      in a 14x13 grid, then the reachable set is the room interior plus the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/6/code.py:17:#      still paints orange on that room-side inner boundary, but the final output\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/6/code.py:21:#      is the output size?\" now hinge on the same room interpretation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/6/code.py:26:#      always-reachable exterior, which would destroy the crop. So the room is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/6/code.py:48:#      unreachable wall rows/cols above/right of the room are intentionally\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/6/code.py:65:#    - In 2-3 examples a human can see the same motif repeat: one blue room-like\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/6/code.py:67:#      on the room side, and outputs cropped tightly to that room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/6/code.py:180:    Recover the doorway-entered room, paint its inner lining, then crop to it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/6/code.py:188:    - The marker can enter the room only through the frame's one small opening,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/6/code.py:189:      so the room interior is the marker-reachable side of the true wall.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/6/code.py:196:    - Paint orange on reachable background cells that lie on the room's inner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/14/code.py:65:#      corridor, and always leaves a right-side chamber wide enough to be seen.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/4/code.py:29:#   stable across samples and leaves enough room in a 13x13 quadrant for the motif. Each sample forces exactly one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:26:#    compact bottom-left room covering only 15-35% of the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:27:#    A concrete trace is a 14x16 grid with a 5x5 reachable room in the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:28:#    bottom-left. A thick blue vertical barrier stands just to the room's right,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:29:#    a thick blue horizontal barrier sits just above the room, and extra blue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:32:#    scene, including any visible blue decoration placed inside the room. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:34:#    room boundary; the room interior, the unreachable side, the marker, and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:37:#    A purely thin-line room would satisfy the ratio constraint but would not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:42:#    freedom: room width/height, wall thickness, and the size of top/right wall\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:53:#      faces the small room, so the whole component is recoverable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:55:#      traversable. Visible decorations are placed only in the room interior, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:65:#    small room is always at least 4x4 so it can contain an interior distinct\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:66:#    from the 1-cell ring. Visible decorations are placed only on room-interior\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:74:#    that were visible inside the room disappear in the output. This makes both\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:75:#    the sparse-output rule and the small-room meta change visible without relying\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:79:#    barriers, so the scene reads as a single room plus surrounding walls. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:81:#    decorations are small and confined to the room interior, avoiding clutter on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:87:#    pixels disappear because they are not part of the true room boundary, not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:220:    Keep only the compact room boundary scaffold around the marker-side region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:224:    - Border-touching structural walls, together with the outer frame, isolate a small marker-reachable room near the bottom-left while larger wall masses dominate the unreachable side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:225:    - Decorative blue pixels may appear inside the room or behind the structural barrier, but they do not define the room boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:229:    - Flood again while allowing travel through non-structural blue pixels so decorations do not change the geometry of the reachable room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:230:    - Output only the boundary scaffold: keep structural wall pixels blue and paint orange on reachable background pixels that lie on the room's inner boundary; erase the marker, decorations, reachable interior, and unreachable area to background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:233:    - The crucial distinction is not \"all blue survives\" but \"only boundary-defining blue survives\": the solver must recover the real structural wall component first, then emit a sparse wall-plus-ring mask for the small reachable room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:240:def _build_structural_mask(h: int, w: int, room_h: int, room_w: int, thickness: int, rng: random.Random) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:242:    room_r0 = h - room_h\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:244:    # Base L-shaped barrier that makes the marker-reachable room exactly the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:245:    # bottom-left rectangle [room_r0:h, 0:room_w).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:246:    structural[:, room_w : room_w + thickness] = True\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:247:    structural[room_r0 - thickness : room_r0, : room_w + thickness] = True\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:249:    max_top_h = room_r0 - thickness\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:252:        top_w_min = min(w, room_w + thickness)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:254:        structural[room_r0 - thickness - top_h : room_r0 - thickness, :top_w] = True\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:256:    max_right_w = w - (room_w + thickness)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:261:        structural[r0 : r0 + right_h, room_w + thickness : room_w + thickness + right_w] = True\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:266:def _pick_room_dims(h: int, w: int, thickness: int, rng: random.Random) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:267:    max_room_h = h - thickness - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:268:    max_room_w = w - thickness - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:269:    if max_room_h < ROOM_MIN_DIM or max_room_w < ROOM_MIN_DIM:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:273:        room_h = rng.randint(ROOM_MIN_DIM, max_room_h)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:274:        room_w = rng.randint(ROOM_MIN_DIM, max_room_w)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:275:        reach_ratio = (room_h * room_w) / float(h * w)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:277:            return room_h, room_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:323:    room_dims = _pick_room_dims(h, w, thickness, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:324:    if room_dims is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:326:    room_h, room_w = room_dims\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:328:    structural = _build_structural_mask(h, w, room_h, room_w, thickness, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:336:    room_r0 = h - room_h\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:338:    expected_reach[room_r0:h, :room_w] = True\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/1/code.py:449:def _line_cells_by_room(line_path: list[tuple[int, int]], h: int, w: int) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/1/code.py:543:    line_cells = _line_cells_by_room(line_path, h, w)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/1/code.py:584:    line_cells = _line_cells_by_room(line_path, h, w)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/27/code.py:249:    \"\"\"Sample component bbox dimensions; matched objects get slightly roomier boxes.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/8/code.py:153:    \"\"\"Sample a small rectangle size that leaves room for several separated components.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/29/code.py:32:    shape: clean rectangular rooms with 1-cell-thick colored walls\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/24/code.py:48:#    When there is room for a second deleted object, it contains all 3 hidden targets so the full target\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/18/code.py:45:    That is intentionally simpler than the original irregular-maze generator because the new\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D9/0/code.py:26:#    - To make D9 observable, the generator enforces a left-bottom reachable room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D9/0/code.py:48:#      left and bottom borders and encloses a bottom-left reachable room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/30/code.py:32:#      这样同一个 glyph 同时暴露“方向通道”和“长度/输出色通道”，但真正的长度仍由面积给出。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/43/code.py:24:#    - 小例子：区域内部是一个粗 L 形通道，黄色在左下角。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/43/code.py:26:#         本变体固定“先横后竖”，它会先在底边向右挪到竖通道下方，再沿该列向上堆到顶端。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/43/code.py:50:#    - 特殊区域使用预制的非矩形通道模板；放置前会显式检查墙环、缓冲区和已有对象是否冲突。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/43/code.py:55:#      去某个角，而是沿固定先后次序穿过不规则通道。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/25/code.py:23:# - 第三个杯若存在，则放到清晰通道中，不再制造第二组交互，避免整张图变成多层覆盖谜题。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/26/code.py:26:      - original convex behavior: in a rectangular room with rightward motion, every yellow keeps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/26/code.py:82:    - regions are buffered apart, so colored walls do not fuse into unreadable mazes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/10/code.py:42:    - 单纯把新填腔体内部加入前沿还不够；共享墙体会在 D6 擦除后变成新的通道，因此被擦掉的 boundary 也必须并入前沿。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:11:      - yellow cells still move independently per enclosed room and later yellows still stack\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:18:      - rooms are generated as plain rectangles so the diagonal rebound pattern is visually clean:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:26:      - each room is a sealed colored rectangle with empty interior\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:28:      - take a room whose interior is rows 6..11 and cols 5..10, and a legend direction (+1,+1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:37:        - after REFLECT_STEPS total moves, it can stop mid-room rather than on the far wall\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:46:      - rooms: always 2 rectangular rooms total, so every sample has repeated evidence\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:47:      - yellows: 1-2 per room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:50:      - one room per sample is forced to contain a multi-bounce trace\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:52:      - when there is one legend, two rooms share that wall color and direction, reinforcing the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:58:    - passable-region extraction assumes rooms are enclosed and not connected to the outside.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:61:    - border color lookup assumes one dominant wall color surrounds a room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:62:      Generator assigns exactly one wall color per room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:73:    - each room reserves its walls, interior, and one extra exterior buffer cell before another\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:75:    - room walls are kept strictly inside the 20x20 board\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:83:    - a multi-bounce room is forced in every sample, so examples show more than a trivial single\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:87:    - rectangles keep the room silhouettes simple and readable even when the final yellow lands\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:89:    - walls, legends, and rooms are buffered so same-color structures do not touch accidentally\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:93:    - color still carries just one interpretable relation: legend fill color matches room walls\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:100:    - solver expects every movable room to be a bounded passable component with one wall color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:416:    Move yellow pixels inside sealed rooms according to corner legends, but only along diagonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:417:    paths that can rebound off room walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:420:    - Background is the most common color; yellow movers (4) occupy enclosed empty rooms bounded by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:422:    - Border legends are solid 6x7 rectangles at grid corners whose fill color matches a room's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:428:    - For each bounded passable room, identify its surrounding wall color and use the matching\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:438:      \"the far wall.\" You must track a finite diagonal reflection path inside the room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:498:def _rect_room(r0: int, c0: int, h_int: int, w_int: int) -> tuple[set[tuple[int, int]], set[tuple[int, int]]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:532:def _try_place_room(rng: random.Random, occupied: np.ndarray, spec: dict) -> dict | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:552:        interior, walls = _rect_room(r0, c0, h_int, w_int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:571:def _place_rooms(rng: random.Random, legends: list[dict], legend_occupied: np.ndarray) -> list[dict] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:581:    rooms: list[dict] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:583:        room = _try_place_room(rng, occupied, spec)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:584:        if room is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:586:        rooms.append(room)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:587:        r0, c0, h_int, w_int = room[\"bbox\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:590:    return rooms\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:721:    regions = _place_rooms(rng, legends, legend_occupied)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/9/code.py:70:#    - In TL the detached motif plus blank corridor makes the new gap rule explicit.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/4/code.py:49:#        3. the marker trail corridor is background in the output base and unused by earlier trails.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:8:#    - The source task has enclosed background rooms bounded by colored walls. A border legend with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:20:#      input room A | room B, yellow in room A moving right\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:23:#      round 3+: yellow continues through room B, possibly drilling another separator later\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:26:#        The fused rule keeps iterating, so the same yellow can cross into later rooms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:32:#    - All generated rooms in the drilling structure share one wall color and one direction. This\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:34:#    - Samples still contain 2-3 rooms and 1-2 yellows, so the rule has repeated visual support\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:38:#    - Original assumption: each yellow can be solved from its initial room in one compression pass.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:43:#      a yellow keeps the direction of its initial room even after drilling into another room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:44:#      The generator guarantees compatible layouts by making all drill-connected rooms share one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:47:#      movement is confined to the union of initially enclosed room interiors plus wall cells erased\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:48:#      later. This preserves the \"inside rooms\" semantics and prevents leaking into the unrelated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:53:#    - The room structure is a single chain of axis-aligned rectangular chambers that share separator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:58:#    - Every generated sample forces at least one yellow to leave its starting room by drilling\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:409:    Advance yellow pixels through enclosed rooms according to border-legend directions, while walls can be drilled away over repeated rounds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:412:    - Background cells form one or more enclosed rooms bounded by colored walls; yellow pixels begin inside those rooms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:417:    - Each yellow inherits the direction of the legend matching the wall color of its starting room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:422:    Key insight: the output is not a one-shot slide; it is a drilling process. Initial rooms define each yellow's direction, while erased wall cells enlarge the future travel corridor and can connect rooms that were separate in the input.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:515:    rooms: list[dict] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:533:        rooms.append(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:546:    return rooms, walls\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:560:    rooms: list[dict] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:578:        rooms.append(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:591:    return rooms, walls\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:602:    room_count = rng.choice(ROOM_COUNT_CHOICES)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:603:    lengths = [rng.choice(ROOM_LENGTH_CHOICES) for _ in range(room_count)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:615:            rooms, walls = _paint_horizontal_chain(grid, wall_color, r0, c0, cross, lengths)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:617:            rooms, walls = _paint_vertical_chain(grid, wall_color, r0, c0, cross, lengths)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:619:        for room in rooms:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:620:            room[\"color\"] = wall_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:621:            room[\"dir\"] = direction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:622:            room[\"walls\"] = walls\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:623:        return rooms\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:627:def _validate_topology(grid: np.ndarray, rooms: list[dict]) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:636:    expected = [room[\"interior\"] for room in rooms]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:642:def _upstream_room_index(direction: tuple[int, int], n_rooms: int) -> int:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/