      interior, walls = _rect_room(r0, c0, oh, ow)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/7/code.py:504:        region = _try_place_room(rng, occupied, wall_color, direction)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/7/code.py:544:def _paint_rooms(grid: np.ndarray, regions: list[dict]) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/7/code.py:607:    _paint_rooms(grid, regions)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:29:#       - 一个完全位于网格内部的“房间”形背景区域, 中间某处有1个品红像素\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:30:#       - 房间外沿有1格厚的蓝色闭合墙, 墙不会碰到网格边界\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:31:#       - 墙外是大片背景色, 其中可混入一些蓝色装饰墙; 房间内部深处也可放少量蓝色装饰墙\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:33:#       - 房间内侧沿结构墙刷一圈橙色\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:34:#       - 房间内的装饰墙保留\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:35:#       - 房间外的装饰墙擦成背景\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:38:#       - 变体: 标记在内部, 若还沿用“接触边界的墙才算结构墙”, 则闭合房间墙会被误判为装饰\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:39:#       - 新逻辑: 先从标记洪填得到房间内部 reach0; 再从网格边界洪填得到外部 outside0;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:44:#     - 房间形状允许矩形加1-3个矩形凸出, 保持少量自由度且样例间有重复结构支撑\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:51:#     - 房间区域始终保持在距网格边界至少2格的位置, 这样由其外扩1格得到的结构墙不会碰边\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:52:#     - 结构墙由房间区域的4邻外边界直接生成, 天然与房间不重叠且形成闭环\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:54:#     - 标记只放在房间深处的背景格, 不放在边缘或未来会变橙的位置\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:56:#     - 人类可直接看到: 品红点不在角上, 蓝墙圈在内部闭合, 橙色只沿内部房间边界出现\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:60:#     - 可见装饰墙限制在房间深处, 不挤占橙色环\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:61:#     - 隐藏装饰墙限制在房间外且不贴结构墙, 避免蓝墙层层叠在一起难辨结构\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:72:#     - 新假设3: 结构墙组件同时贴着内部 reach0 与边界外部 outside0; generator 保证房间无洞、\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:74:#     - 新假设4: 标记位于结构墙包围的区域内; generator 只从房间深处选标记\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:144:def _room_walls(region: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:154:    - The marker sits strictly inside the grid, inside a wall-enclosed room rather than on a corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:155:    - Some blue components form the room boundary; other blue bits are decorations either inside the room or outside it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:158:    - Flood-fill from the interior marker across background to recover the room's reachable area.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:160:    - Erase non-structural blue decorations on the exterior side, and paint orange on reachable background cells that lie on the room's inner boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:269:def _room_mask(h: int, w: int, rng: random.Random) -> np.ndarray | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:382:    region = _room_mask(h, w, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D3/3/code.py:386:    structural = _room_walls(region)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:14:    - yellow pixels still move toward the extreme side of their room and stack there\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:16:    - rooms contain internal obstacle color 3, which is part of the room identity but not passable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:17:    - movement is now path-based inside the room rather than repeated one-vector stepping\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:24:    - Concrete look: a rectangular room with colored outer wall contains black floor, green obstacle\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:29:      original_main() treated the room as one 0/4 component and only repeated the legend vector.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:31:      With obstacles present, it would either split the room incorrectly or strand the yellow on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:34:      new main() first finds the whole room as one bounded component of {background, yellow,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:35:      obstacle}. Inside that room it runs a BFS over passable cells with 8-neighbor motion biased\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:54:    - `passable = (g == bg) | (g == mover)` no longer identifies the room, because the room may be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:64:    - The original diagonal check assumed both orthogonal intermediates must be inside the room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:69:    - Obstacles are placed strictly inside rooms and never overwrite walls or legends.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:70:    - Each obstacle barrier spans the room interior top-to-bottom and leaves exactly one diagonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:84:    - Rectangular rooms reduce clutter so the informative pattern is the obstacle gate, not noisy\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:85:      room geometry.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:86:    - At most two rooms are generated, which avoids overcrowding around the 6x7 diagonal legends.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:90:    - Wall colors still only provide legend-to-room matching; they do not encode movement by value.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:95:    - The solver assumes each room is a bounded 4-connected component in the meta-mask {0,3,4};\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:96:      generator builds rooms exactly that way.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:100:      generator only keeps rooms with validated candidate starts.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:320:    Slide yellow pixels inside colored rooms by the direction encoded in corner legends.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:323:    - Black background surrounds one or two enclosed rooms bounded by colored walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:324:    - Each room interior may contain black floor, yellow movers, and green internal obstacles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:326:      room they control.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:329:    - For each bounded room, recover the full room from the meta-mask {background, yellow,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:331:    - Use the legend matching that room's wall color to get a diagonal direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:333:      through the room and stacking with previously settled yellows. Diagonal steps may cut corners:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:337:    - The obstacle barrier can separate the room into chambers that touch only at a diagonal pinch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:348:    room_mask = (g == bg) | (g == MOVER) | (g == OBSTACLE)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:351:    for pts in components_mask(room_mask, connectivity=4):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:355:        room = {(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in pts}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:356:        passable = {p for p in room if int(g[p]) in (bg, MOVER)}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:362:        for r, c in room:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:366:                if (nr, nc) in room:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:447:def _room_wall_cells(r0: int, c0: int, h_out: int, w_out: int) -> set[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:496:def _sample_room(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:501:    n_rooms: int,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:507:        if n_rooms == 1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:530:        walls = _room_wall_cells(r0, c0, h_out, w_out)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:531:        room = passable | obstacles\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:538:            \"room\": room,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:551:    n_rooms = min(MAX_ROOMS, len(legends))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:554:    chosen_legends = chosen_legends[:n_rooms]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:557:        reg = _sample_room(rng, occupied, color, direction, n_rooms)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/42/code.py:635:    expected = [reg[\"room\"] for reg in regions]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:19:    - each movable object is a yellow pixel inside an enclosed colored room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:22:    - room interiors now contain two obstacle roles:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:26:    - instead, it navigates through the room toward the legend direction, detouring around green\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:31:- Right-moving room, simplified row-level picture:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:56:- Each room contains exactly one yellow and one blue stop obstacle. This avoids ambiguous multi-\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:62:   broken. The bounded room is now the meta-component `{bg, yellow, green obstacle, blue stop}`.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:63:   Using only passable cells would split the room at internal obstacles and lose the border color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:65:   broken for the same reason. Region identity and motion state space diverge; room detection must\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:72:   interior obstacle for the wall color controlling the room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:75:   the correct side, and the room still has a valid detouring path.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:86:- Rooms are axis-aligned rectangles with a one-cell exterior buffer, so legends and different rooms\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:88:- Green bars are placed strictly inside the room, leaving at least one gap so passable floor stays\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:90:- Blue stop obstacles are placed strictly inside the room and away from the perimeter so there is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:108:- Rectangular rooms are intentional. The original irregular fences would combine poorly with two\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:110:- There is exactly one blue stop obstacle per room and sparse green structure, so the room interior\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:111:  stays readable instead of becoming a dense maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:112:- Blue does appear in legends as center dots, but only inside border rectangles; inside rooms, a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:117:- No free-form color mapping is introduced. Blue always means \"stop obstacle\" inside rooms and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:125:- Each yellow-bearing room contains at least one reachable blue stop obstacle and exactly one yellow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:335:        raise ValueError(\"combo rooms must contain at least one stop obstacle\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:360:def _room_data_from_grid(g: np.ndarray) -> list[dict]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:364:    room_mask = (g == bg) | (g == MOVER) | (g == OBSTACLE) | (g == STOP_OBSTACLE)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:365:    rooms = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:366:    for pts in components_mask(room_mask, connectivity=4):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:369:        room = {(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in pts}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:370:        movers = [p for p in room if int(g[p]) == MOVER]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:373:        passable = {p for p in room if int(g[p]) in (bg, MOVER)}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:374:        stop_cells = {p for p in room if int(g[p]) == STOP_OBSTACLE}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:376:        for r, c in room:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:380:                if (nr, nc) in room:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:391:        rooms.append(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:393:                \"room\": room,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:401:    return rooms\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:428:    for room in _room_data_from_grid(g):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:429:        passable = room[\"passable\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:430:        movers = room[\"movers\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:431:        dr, dc = room[\"dir\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:445:    Route yellow pixels through enclosed rooms using border legends and stop-obstacle cues.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:449:      the wall color of one or more enclosed rooms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:450:    - Inside a room, yellow pixels move on black floor; green cells are ordinary internal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:455:    - For each bounded room, recover the legend direction from the wall color exactly as in the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:457:    - Treat the whole room `{floor, yellow, green, blue}` as one object for region detection, but\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:459:    - A yellow searches the reachable passable cells in that room and ends at the farthest one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:461:      same room cannot reuse already occupied destinations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:472:    rooms = _room_data_from_grid(g)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:473:    assert rooms, \"at least one bounded legend-controlled room is required\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:475:    for room in rooms:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:476:        movers = room[\"movers\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:479:        dr, dc = room[\"dir\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:482:        new_pts = _path_planned_stop_slide(room[\"passable\"], room[\"stop_cells\"], movers, dr, dc)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:535:def _room_wall_cells(r0: int, c0: int, h_out: int, w_out: int) -> set[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:562:def _room_ranges(r0: int, c0: int, h_out: int, w_out: int) -> tuple[int, int, int, int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:568:def _build_room_objects(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:577:    r1, c1, ri0, ci0 = _room_ranges(r0, c0, h_out, w_out)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:675:def _sample_room(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:720:        built = _build_room_objects(r0, c0, h_out, w_out, dr, dc, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:724:        walls = _room_wall_cells(r0, c0, h_out, w_out)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:725:        room = built[\"passable\"] | built[\"obstacles\"] | {built[\"stop_cell\"]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:733:            \"room\": room,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:758:        reg = _sample_room(rng, occupied, color, color_dir[color], total_regions)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/35/code.py:782:    expected = [reg[\"room\"] for reg in regions]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:62:#    - The entire diagonal corridor to the edge is reserved in `occ_path`, including skipped cells,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:83:#      Guarantee: generator reserves the full corridor and inserts exactly one obstacle on it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:377:    \"\"\"Find a placement whose diagonal corridor visibly demonstrates dash+collision.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/18/code.py:3:# Name: 十字形锚点 + 空心框锚点\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/32/code.py:3:# Name: 宽通道约束+L/T形区域\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/2/code.py:31:#      through the spike and into the cup mouth corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/8/code.py:80:# - Assumption: every source color belongs to the movable palette and has enough brighter headroom for its\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/1/code.py:24:#      hub-relative position: above/below/left/right corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/1/code.py:26:#      have different contact lengths. Within a corridor, the correct sprite is the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/1/code.py:32:#   combo: the top corridor may contain two same-colored sprites. Position says both\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/1/code.py:38:#   combo matching path = side corridor -> length-rank filter -> side color repaint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/1/code.py:45:# - To make the D2 signal actually matter, 1-3 side corridors also contain a decoy\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/1/code.py:48:# - The hub remains visually simple: one central hollow rectangle plus side corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/1/code.py:55:#   combo, multiple side-corridor candidates can share one color, so component labeling\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/1/code.py:62:# - A new assumption appears in the corridor selection loop: if a component overlaps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/1/code.py:63:#   exactly one side corridor, it belongs to that side's candidate pool. The generator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/1/code.py:65:#   corridors, with extra padding so components do not merge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/1/code.py:69:#   detach and scatter sprites back into side corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/1/code.py:71:#   hub, true sprites, and same-corridor decoys never overlap or touch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/1/code.py:97:# - Generated samples should contain at least one side corridor with a wrong-length\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/1/code.py:103:# - Solver assumption: each outside component lies in at most one side corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/1/code.py:104:#   Generator guarantee: corridor-specific placement helper enforces this.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/1/code.py:112:    Attach detached sprites to a central hollow rectangle by side corridor + length rank.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/1/code.py:115:    - Position gives the candidate side corridor: above/below/left/right the hub.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/1/code.py:117:      different contact lengths. Within a corridor, keep only candidates whose contact\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/22/code.py:65:#   The generator reserves whole ray corridors away from stray pixels, prevents bbox overlap, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/22/code.py:653:    \"\"\"Optionally place one isolated stray pixel away from bboxes and full ray corridors.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/8/code.py:44:#      - Visible difference: the completed output is a band or corridor centered on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/6/code.py:66:#     - Stray pixels are excluded from all cup bboxes and all reserved waterfall corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/6/code.py:84:#       disjoint output corridors, so the solver can paint in any order after the erase phase.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/6/code.py:492:    \"\"\"Optionally add one isolated pixel away from cup bboxes and waterfall corridors.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D13/1/code.py:14:#      halo of structural walls, so open border corridors stay azure unless they\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D13/1/code.py:17:#      colored the left edge corridor and the cells beside the wall; the new output\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:18:  - Use a rectangular room whose direction is, for example, right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:24:  - With 4 different lanes and distances [1, 4, 2, 5], the room output becomes a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:41:  - The generator uses 1-2 legend colors and one room per color, so there is repeated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:52:  - components_mask(passable, 4) still assumes each active room is an enclosed bg/yellow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:55:    color per region. Each room wall is monochrome, so the assumption is exact.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:67:  - Each room is placed as a non-overlapping rectangle with an extra buffer around it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:74:  - The input shows several yellow seeds inside the same walled room, already suggesting that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:78:  - Because bar length varies within a room, a human can infer that distance matters rather\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:84:  - The generator forces at least two distinct bar lengths per room, preventing degenerate\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:222:    - Border legends are filled rectangles whose dominant fill color matches a room's wall color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:223:    - Each enclosed room contains 3-5 yellow pixels on clear lanes inside a monochrome wall boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:226:    - For each enclosed room, infer its wall color and read the corresponding legend direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:361:        room_h = interior_h + 2\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:362:        room_w = interior_w + 2\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:370:                \"room_h\": room_h,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:371:                \"room_w\": room_w,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:372:                \"area\": room_h * room_w,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:379:def _candidate_origins(room_h: int, room_w: int) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:381:    for r0 in range(1, GRID_H - room_h):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:382:        for c0 in range(1, GRID_W - room_w):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:387:def _fits_reserved(occupied: np.ndarray, r0: int, c0: int, room_h: int, room_w: int) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:389:    r_hi = min(GRID_H, r0 + room_h + ROOM_BUFFER)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:391:    c_hi = min(GRID_W, c0 + room_w + ROOM_BUFFER)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:395:def _reserve_room(occupied: np.ndarray, r0: int, c0: int, room_h: int, room_w: int) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:397:    r_hi = min(GRID_H, r0 + room_h + ROOM_BUFFER)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:399:    c_hi = min(GRID_W, c0 + room_w + ROOM_BUFFER)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:403:def _paint_room(grid: np.ndarray, plan: dict) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:405:    room_h = plan[\"room_h\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:406:    room_w = plan[\"room_w\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:408:    grid[r0, c0 : c0 + room_w] = color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:409:    grid[r0 + room_h - 1, c0 : c0 + room_w] = color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:410:    grid[r0 : r0 + room_h, c0] = color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:411:    grid[r0 : r0 + room_h, c0 + room_w - 1] = color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:415:    # Prefer a one-cell gap between active lanes when the room is wide/tall enough so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:478:        raise ValueError(\"need at least two distinct distances per room\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:491:        candidates = _candidate_origins(spec[\"room_h\"], spec[\"room_w\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:495:            if _fits_reserved(occupied, r0, c0, spec[\"room_h\"], spec[\"room_w\"]):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:502:        _reserve_room(occupied, chosen[0], chosen[1], spec[\"room_h\"], spec[\"room_w\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/40/code.py:540:        _paint_room(grid, plan)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/4/code.py:11:#      the same axis. This makes the path re-enter the spike and the cup's mouth corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/4/code.py:274:      spike and mouth corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D13/2/code.py:39:#     - If a reachable corridor starts at the left grid edge, the old rule colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/7/code.py:29:#    - The bar has one vertical corridor in columns 10..14.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/7/code.py:31:#      little way downward inside the corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/7/code.py:35:#    - If A2 and B2 become edge-adjacent inside the corridor, both chains stop.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/7/code.py:43:#      stable reduces pairing ambiguity and makes the shared corridor easy to see.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/7/code.py:64:#      on the correct side, and enter the corridor without already reaching the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/7/code.py:78:#    - The bar visibly contains one complete pass-through corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/7/code.py:80:#      corridor from opposite mouths and meeting inside one strip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/7/code.py:86:#    - Only one through-channel is used, so the shared-corridor story is easy to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/7/code.py:88:#    - Decoys stay smaller and never merge with the used corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/7/code.py:94:#    - The rule is inferred entirely from geometry: one shared corridor, fixed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db0c5428/16/code.py:3:# Name: 十字形阵列+无空洞\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/37/code.py:82:  - Three large slots keep sprites separated and leave room for one vertical and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:14:    - Yellow pixels slide inside enclosed rooms and stack against the far wall.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:21:    - A-colored rooms use actual_A = disp_A.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:22:    - B-colored rooms use actual_B = sign(disp_A - disp_B).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:23:    - A mixed room has a single enclosed interior but its wall ring visibly contains both\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:24:      legend fill colors. That room uses mixed_dir = sign(actual_A + actual_B).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:29:    - The mixed room uses sign((0,1) + (-1,1)) = (-1, 1) = up-right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:32:        1. Count adjacent wall colors for a room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:38:        3. Inspect which legend wall colors appear around each room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:43:    - B-only rooms no longer follow B's shown arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:44:    - The mixed room depends on both modifications at once because one summand is itself decoded\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:48:  - The generator always provides three evidence room types in the same grid:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:49:      1. one A-only room,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:50:      2. one B-only room,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:51:      3. one mixed A+B room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:55:      - mixed_dir is non-zero and differs from both pure-room directions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:60:    - \"one wall color per room\" is false for the mixed room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:61:    - \"one legend directly determines one room direction\" is false for B and also false for the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:62:      mixed room, whose motion depends on both legends.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:67:    - Border analysis must now collect the set of legend wall colors around a room instead of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:75:    - The only non-background wall colors adjacent to room interiors are the two legend fill colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:76:    - If a room sees both legend colors, their vector sum is non-zero.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:82:  - Every room is a closed rectangle, so its interior is guaranteed to be one bounded component.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:83:  - The mixed room wall ring is colored after the room geometry is fixed; top/left segments use\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:87:  - The A-only room anchors the normal meaning of a legend arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:88:  - The B-only room shows that B's displayed arrow is not the real motion cue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:89:  - The mixed room shows that a two-color wall is a separate instruction class rather than a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:91:  - Because these three room types appear together, a solver can compare them within one example\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:96:  - The mixed room uses a clean top-left versus bottom-right color split, so the two wall colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:98:  - Fixed room slots avoid accidental tangles that would make boundary ownership hard to parse.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:102:  - The new burden is structural: a room may be linked to one legend color or to both.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:108:      Compare the true output against a wrong interpreter that keeps the mixed-room addition but\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:112:      the mixed room back to its majority wall color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:118:  - main() assumes room borders expose only legend fill colors, not stray structural colors;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:119:    generate_input() enforces this by using exactly those colors for room walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:120:  - main() assumes the mixed room really contains both wall colors; generate_input() enforces this\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:341:    Slide yellow pixels inside enclosed rooms, but decode the room direction through a fused\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:345:    - The background is black and yellow pixels sit in closed rooms bounded by colored wall rings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:347:      used for the room walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:348:    - Some rooms are bordered by a single legend color, while one room is visibly bordered by both\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:355:    - A single-color room uses that legend's true direction, while a two-color room uses the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:357:    - All yellow pixels in a room slide as far as possible in that resolved direction and stack.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:360:    The wall colors tell you whether a room listens to one legend or to both, and one of those\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:474:def _paint_room_walls(grid: np.ndarray, region: dict, legends_by_role: dict[str, dict]) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:680:    # Mixed room also depends on B's decoded direction, so count it for decode impact too.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/39/code.py:697:        _paint_room_walls(grid, region, legends_by_role)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/5/code.py:12:#         back through the spike and the central mouth corridor just like the D1 reflection variant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/5/code.py:45:#    - The obstacle can sit inside the same cup's mouth corridor. Therefore \"any non-bg pixel\" is too\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/5/code.py:51:#    - The dedicated obstacle cell is chosen on the reflected mouth-side corridor, never on the cup\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/5/code.py:60:#    - Only one special obstacle is added per cup, on the ray corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/5/code.py:500:    \"\"\"Build one cup, place an internal blocker on the reflected corridor, and commit it.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/17/code.py:63:#   Guarantee: base colors are assigned from legend slots with room for depth 0..len(chain)-1.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/12/code.py:30:#    - The full ray corridor is reserved in `occ_path`, including the intentional blank cells, so no\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/12/code.py:38:#      which keeps the launch corridor easy to read.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/12/code.py:47:#      Guarantee: generator reserves the whole corridor and paints only the odd-offset output cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/12/code.py:48:#    - Assumption: each showcased cup has enough room to reveal the combo visually.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db0c5428/10/code.py:3:# Name: 角像素编码中心+十字形空洞\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:13:    - Yellow pixels still slide and stack against the far wall inside each enclosed room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:24:    - In the source task or in the pure arrow-shape variant, color-5 rooms would slide down.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:25:    - In this combo, color-5 rooms instead slide in sign((0,1) - (1,0)) = (-1, 1), i.e. up-right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:66:  - Right-colored rooms visibly disobey their own displayed arrow and instead follow the vector\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:71:  - Only two legends appear, both separated from rooms by reserved space.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:85:  - A sample is accepted only if at least one cell inside a second-color room differs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:362:    Slide yellow pixels inside enclosed rooms using arrow legends plus a derived second instruction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:365:    - The background is the most common color. Colored wall loops enclose passable rooms containing yellow pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:367:    - The left and right legends correspond to two distinct wall colors appearing on the rooms below.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:374:    Key insight: Color still links each legend to its rooms, but the motion is a two-stage inference:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/28/code.py:480:    \"\"\"Build one cup, reserve its thick path corridor, and commit it to the canvases.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/35/code.py:55:  - The generator uses three roomy slot regions so sprite bundles stay disjoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:25:#   1. Position gives the corridor: a component above / below / left / right of the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:27:#   2. Within that corridor, contact-edge length rank decides which candidate is the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:34:#   says \"both belong to the top corridor\", then prefers the one whose valid top-side\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:45:#   * one horizontal-corridor decoy from the short class, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:46:#   * one vertical-corridor decoy from the long class.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:47:#   So position alone is insufficient whenever a corridor contains two candidates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:57:#   multiple same-colored candidates into the same side corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:63:#   (hub + attached true sprites), then scatters detached copies into side corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:64:# - Each detached patch is placed by an explicit corridor-aware search with padding,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:66:#   exactly one side corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:67:# - Decoys are never attached in the output, but they are placed in the same corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:75:#   * some corridors contain two same-colored candidates, and only the one from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:80:# - The hub is kept near the center to leave balanced side corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:95:# - Every generated sample should have at least one vertical corridor containing both a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:97:#   candidate in each corridor\" solver should therefore disagree with the combo solver\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:101:# - Solver assumption: a relevant detached component lies entirely in one side corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:103:#   Generator guarantee: corridor search enforces exactly that.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:104:# - Solver assumption: in each side corridor, at least one candidate has the correct\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:108:#   corridor as the true sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:494:    Attach detached sprites to a hollow 4x6 rectangle by side corridor and length tier.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:497:    - Position relative to the hub decides the candidate side corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:500:    - If a corridor contains multiple candidates, long sides choose the longer valid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:641:    # Keep the hub near the center to leave balanced space for multi-candidate corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:678:            # Place the larger patch first to reduce corridor-packing failures.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/32/code.py:692:    # Optional corner distractor: different color and outside all side corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:10:     - Border legends are filled rectangles whose dominant fill color matches a room wall color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:11:     - Interior rooms are irregular fenced blobs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:14:     - All rooms are strict axis-aligned rectangles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:15:     - Every room wall uses the same color, so color matching is gone.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:16:     - Instead, room wall thickness is either 1 or 2, and each thickness matches the border legend\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:18:     - Example: a thin-walled room (1-cell wall) may use a 5x5 legend with 1-cell fill margin and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:19:       move right, while a thick-walled room (2-cell wall) uses a 7x7 legend with 2-cell margin\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:20:       and moves up. Both rooms can share the same wall/fill color, so thickness is the only cue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:23:     - The fused solver must detect a room rectangle, measure its wall thickness, and map that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:32:     rooms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:33:   - The generator may place multiple rooms per thickness, but it always guarantees at least one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:34:     thin room and one thick room in the same grid, so the contrast is explicit in every example.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:39:   - Original region processing inferred a room's controlling legend from adjacent wall colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:47:   - Stack order still matters when multiple yellows share a room, so reverse placement follows the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:52:   - Each room reserves its full outer rectangle plus a 1-cell moat, so rooms never overlap,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:58:   - Humans can directly compare \"thin room vs thick room\" because room geometry is rectangular and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:67:   - Legends stay in corners; rooms stay in the open field with background moats between them.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:68:   - No distractor markings are added inside rooms, so thickness and movement remain easy to read.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:74:   - Assumption: every yellow-containing room has thickness 1 or 2 and that thickness appears in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:76:     produces those two room types.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:259:def _infer_room_thickness(g: np.ndarray, inner_bbox: tuple[int, int, int, int], bg: int, mover: int) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:302:        inferred = _infer_room_thickness(g, (int(r0), int(c0), int(r1), int(c1)), bg, mover)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:327:    Slide yellows inside rectangular rooms using thickness-matched border legends.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:331:    - All room walls and both legend fills use the same non-black color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:332:    - Each enclosed room is a strict axis-aligned rectangle whose wall thickness is either 1 or 2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:339:    - For every enclosed rectangular room, measure whether its wall is 1 cell or 2 cells thick.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:340:    - Match the room to the legend with the same thickness, then slide all yellows in that room as\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:345:      decisive cue is thickness: thin rooms follow the thin-frame legend, and thick rooms follow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:355:def _room_sets(region: dict[str, object]) -> tuple[set[tuple[int, int]], set[tuple[int, int]]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:393:def _sample_room(rng: random.Random, occupied: np.ndarray, thickness: int) -> dict[str, object] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:423:        room = {\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:428:        return room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:432:def _place_rooms(rng: random.Random, legend_occupied: np.ndarray) -> list[dict[str, object]] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:434:    rooms: list[dict[str, object]] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:443:        room = _sample_room(rng, occupied, thickness)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:444:        if room is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:446:        rooms.append(room)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:447:        outer_r0, outer_c0, outer_r1, outer_c1 = room[\"outer_bbox\"]  # type: ignore[misc]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:454:    return rooms\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:457:def _paint_rooms(grid: np.ndarray, rooms: list[dict[str, object]], wall_color: int) -> list[dict[str, object]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:459:    for room in rooms:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:460:        inner, walls = _room_sets(room)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:463:        enriched = dict(room)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:501:def _place_yellows(rng: random.Random, rooms: list[dict[str, object]], thickness_to_dir: dict[int, tuple[int, int]],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:503:    for room in rooms:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:504:        region_set = room[\"inner\"]  # type: ignore[assignment]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:505:        thickness = int(room[\"thickness\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:559:    room_count = 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:568:        inferred = _infer_room_thickness(g, (int(r0), int(c0), int(r1), int(c1)), bg, 4)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:572:        room_count += 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:579:        \"room_count\": room_count,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:580:        \"thin_rooms\": thick1,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:581:        \"thick_rooms\": thick2,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:595:    rooms = _place_rooms(rng, legend_occupied)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:596:    if rooms is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:598:    rooms = _paint_rooms(grid, rooms, wall_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:600:    if not _place_yellows(rng, rooms, thickness_to_dir, grid):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/44/code.py:608:    if metrics[\"thin_rooms\"] == 0 or metrics[\"thick_rooms\"] == 0:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/20/code.py:782:        room = {\"top\": bar_r0, \"bottom\": H - 1 - bar_r1}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/20/code.py:789:        room = {\"left\": bar_c0, \"right\": W - 1 - bar_c1}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/20/code.py:790:    return orientation, bar_color, (bar_r0, bar_c0, bar_r1, bar_c1), room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/20/code.py:797:def _pick_used_windows(rng, orientation, room, chain_lens, strip_width, span_len, legend):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/20/code.py:808:        valid_sides = [side for side in sides if room[side] >= chain_len * 2 + 3 and slots[side]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:15:      - 原题是全局横条带布局: 偶数行是彩色条, 奇数行是通道, 所有粒子都在左边界并固定向右。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:16:      - solver 的真正物理规则很局部: 粒子在可通行格上直行; 前方若撞到彩色墙, 就检查左右/上下两个垂直候选里是否存在“被同色墙夹住”的通道格; 若唯一存在则拐弯。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:26:      - 在上层通道直行到 `x1` 时, 前方 `x1+1` 被同色墙封住, 所以下拐进中间缺口。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:27:      - 下到下层通道后继续前进, 再被 `x2-1` 的同色墙挡住, 于是向上拐回上层。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:36:    - 原 `_has_corridor` 只把 `{BG, PARTICLE}` 视作可走; 融合后箭头像素必须是可通行的, 否则粒子一出发就撞上标记。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:38:    - 原 `main` 通过“左边入口在 col 2/3”筛真通道; 融合后不再依赖全局条带入口, 因为四个局部组件经过旋转后不共享这一几何朝向。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:45:    - 每条真实路径只放 1 个粒子, 所以不会发生多个粒子竞争同一通道或终点冲突。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:53:    - fake corridor 在这个融合版里被弱化掉, 因为真正的核心变化是多边入口和 3 转以上路径; 继续保留大量假走廊只会降低可读性。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:60:    - solver 假设所有拐弯点在“当前方向的两个垂直候选”里至多有一个合法通道。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:86:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:118:            if 0 <= tr < h and 0 <= tc < w and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:193:    \"\"\"Move magenta edge particles by following explicit arrows through spiral corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:210:      the candidate next cell. Rotating the same 3-turn corridor template to different edges does not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/42/code.py:3:# Name: 十字形锚点 + 连接方向由锚点决定\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/16/code.py:24:#      original: two differently colored fenced rooms might use two different arrows, and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/16/code.py:26:#      combo: one corner legend controls four same-colored rooms; all yellows move in parallel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/16/code.py:27:#      along the same direction; then the board is cropped down to just the cluster of rooms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/16/code.py:34:#    - We keep one shared direction across all rooms. This repeated evidence is important:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/16/code.py:46:#    - Crop support cannot depend only on yellow destinations; empty rooms or rooms whose yellow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/16/code.py:55:#      components rather than one merged same-color maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/16/code.py:59:#      all rooms use the same wall color and all yellows move in the same direction, while the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/16/code.py:60:#      output frame is always the tight room-cluster crop instead of the original canvas.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/16/code.py:67:#    - The crop includes full wall rings, preserving the identity of each room after legends and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/16/code.py:73:#    - The meaningful changes are \"one legend controls many same-colored rooms\" and \"output is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/16/code.py:74:#      cropped to the room cluster\"; both are directly visible in the pixel grids.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/16/code.py:238:    Slide yellow pixels inside multiple same-colored rooms, then return a tight crop.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/16/code.py:242:      room walls share one color and there are 3-5 separate rooms using that same wall color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/16/code.py:249:    - Since all rooms use the same wall color, every yellow pixel in every room slides in the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/16/code.py:250:      same direction and stacks against the far wall of its own room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/16/code.py:255:    - Color matching becomes globally shared: the one legend direction applies to all rooms of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/18/code.py:7:#    - Base task: a magenta particle starts at (r, 0), follows same-color corridors,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/18/code.py:12:#      but the moment it enters the target it stops, even if the corridor continues.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/18/code.py:32:#    - Original corridor checks treated any non-bg/non-particle as a wall color. In\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/18/code.py:33:#      the fused task TARGET must not count as a wall, so `_has_corridor` excludes it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/18/code.py:41:#    - Input shows several isolated target-colored dots embedded in true corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/18/code.py:45:#    - Restricting targets to odd corridor rows keeps them legible as dots inside open\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/18/code.py:87:    \"\"\"Return the first valid horizontal corridor cell for row r, if any.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/18/code.py:114:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/18/code.py:158:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/18/code.py:214:    - Col 0 is filled with particles; real corridors are bg cells between same-color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/18/code.py:218:    - A valid particle enters the first real corridor on its row and follows the base\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/18/code.py:220:      color, turn 90 degrees into the unique perpendicular same-color corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/18/code.py:222:      immediately, even if the corridor would continue further.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/18/code.py:280:    \"\"\"Reserve a 3-column window for a vertical corridor and return the wall column.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/24/code.py:350:    \"\"\"Bias larger motif counts toward roomier panels so all count branches appear regularly.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D10/1/code.py:24:#   old rule on a corridor marker->A->B->C:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D10/1/code.py:27:#   new rule on the same corridor:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db0c5428/4/code.py:60:#      3-cell margin. That leaves room for the whole 15x15 expanded region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/9/code.py:386:def _room_patch(mask: np.ndarray, wall_color: int) -> tuple[np.ndarray, set[tuple[int, int]], set[tuple[int, int]]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/9/code.py:388:    room = np.full((ih + 2, iw + 2), int(wall_color), dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/9/code.py:389:    inner = room[1 : 1 + ih, 1 : 1 + iw]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/9/code.py:392:    occupied_local = {(r, c) for r in range(room.shape[0]) for c in range(room.shape[1]) if int(room[r, c]) != 0}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/9/code.py:393:    return room, region_local, occupied_local\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/9/code.py:413:def _room_positions(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/9/code.py:416:    room_shape: tuple[int, int],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/9/code.py:418:    room_occupied_local: set[tuple[int, int]],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/9/code.py:421:    rh, rw = room_shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/9/code.py:429:            room_cells = _shift_cells(room_occupied_local, r0, c0)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/9/code.py:430:            if _touches_patch(room_cells, patch_cells):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/9/code.py:432:            room_center_r = r0 + (rh - 1) / 2.0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/9/code.py:433:            room_center_c = c0 + (rw - 1) / 2.0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/9/code.py:434:            dist = abs(room_center_r - patch_center_r) + abs(room_center_c - patch_center_c)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/9/code.py:487:    room, region_local, room_occupied_local = _room_patch(mask, wall_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/9/code.py:488:    positions = _room_positions(size, size, room.shape, patch_cells, room_occupied_local, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/9/code.py:492:    room_mask = room != 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/9/code.py:493:    grid_slice = grid[rr : rr + room.shape[0], rc : rc + room.shape[1]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/9/code.py:494:    grid_slice[room_mask] = room[room_mask]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:9:#   colored blocker is directly ahead and exactly one perpendicular same-color corridor exists.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:11:#   terminal corridor containing the final BG cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:12:# - D17/1 changes the input construction: each movable real corridor gets its own unique color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:14:#   corridor; it is never reused by a different movable corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:16:#   blocker, turns upward into a vertical color-4 corridor, and stops near the top edge. Originally\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:18:#   other movable corridor uses 4, that endpoint color uniquely identifies the finished corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:21:# - The fused task keeps the original corridor-tracing mechanics, fake corridors, edge stops, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:23:#   independent movable corridors do not accidentally share a bar color through the shared-row\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:30:#   that: the solver must also return the final travel direction so the endpoint corridor color can\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:34:#   may share its color only with bar rows that are part of the same logical corridor; independent\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:36:# - The solver now assumes the endpoint sits on a unique real corridor, so `_corridor_color()` reads\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:42:#   corridors they would be forced to share a color, violating D17/1.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:46:#   qualify as movable real-corridor starts.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:50:#   corridor bars and different moved particles usually end in different colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:51:# - Because each movable corridor color is unique in that example, a human can infer that the final\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:52:#   color is not arbitrary recoloring: it is determined by the corridor the particle ends in.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:56:#   local corridor color, which is visually simpler than overlaying a fixed magenta token.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:58:#   hard to tell whether repeated colors indicate one corridor or many.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:62:#   flanking the final segment, and D17/1 ensures that this color identifies one movable corridor in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:112:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:128:def _corridor_color(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> int:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:129:    \"\"\"Return the bar-pair color of the real corridor containing the endpoint cell.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:150:    assert len(set(candidates)) == 1, \"final position is not on a unique real corridor\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:155:    \"\"\"Find the first valid real-corridor entrance for row r, or None.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:192:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:202:    \"\"\"Return moved particle traces as (start_row, end_r, end_c, corridor_color, end_dir).\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:214:        traces.append((r, end_r, end_c, _corridor_color(g, end_r, end_c, end_dir), end_dir))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:219:    \"\"\"Move particles along uniquely colored corridors and recolor them at their final corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:224:    - Real movable corridors are bg cells flanked by same-color bars; fake rows use mismatched bars.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:227:    - Each particle that has a valid real-corridor entrance moves right through bg cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:228:    - When blocked by a colored cell, it turns 90 degrees into the unique perpendicular corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:231:      terminal corridor instead of staying magenta.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:234:    - The endpoint color is read from the corridor that contains the particle's final position, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:235:      in this combo each movable corridor color is unique, so the output color identifies which\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:236:      corridor the particle ended in.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:251:            out[end_r, end_c] = _corridor_color(g, end_r, end_c, end_dir)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:257:    \"\"\"Reserve a 3-column window for a vertical corridor and return the wall column.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:273:    \"\"\"Choose non-adjacent channel indices for independent real corridors.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:294:    \"\"\"Assign a color to each bar row while keeping real corridors unique and fake corridors fake.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:339:def _plan_real_corridors(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:342:    \"\"\"Assign straight or L-turn behavior to each real corridor.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:418:    \"\"\"Render the planned real-corridor turns onto the grid.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/25/code.py:470:    plans = _plan_real_corridors(real_indices, bar_start, H, W)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/10/code.py:34:      room under the original per-pixel rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:16:   - 网格仍是原题的条纹布局：偶数行是彩色条，奇数行是水平通道，竖直转接靠\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:22:       2. 障碍颜色：一旦粒子已经进入迷宫，后续所有拐弯都只看正前方挡块颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:30:       * 它沿竖直通道上行，遇到颜色 9 的挡块，再被强制从上转右，进入一条蓝色\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:60:   - 竖直通道仍然通过预留 3 列窗口分配，避免多个转弯结构互相覆盖。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:118:def _corridor_color(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> int | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:119:    \"\"\"Return the corridor-pair color visible at (r, c), else None.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:157:    \"\"\"First horizontal corridor on row r that matches the source color.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:160:        color = _corridor_color(grid, r, c, \"right\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:170:def _first_real_corridor_color(grid: np.ndarray, r: int) -> int | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:174:        color = _corridor_color(grid, r, c, \"right\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:203:            step_color = _corridor_color(grid, nr, nc, direction)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:216:            turn_color = _corridor_color(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:260:            if _corridor_color(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir) is not None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:322:        color = _first_real_corridor_color(grid, r)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:374:    \"\"\"Move source-colored particles through cue-directed corridors and paint corridor trails.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:377:    - bg=7. Odd rows in col 0 contain source particles colored from the corridor palette.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:378:    - Even rows are colored bars. Real horizontal corridors are BG cells between same-color bars.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:382:    - A source may start only if the first real horizontal corridor on its row has the same color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:384:      90 degrees according to the cue color, provided that the chosen side exposes a corridor cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:385:    - The output paints every visited travel cell with the current corridor color; the final cell is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:390:      and corridor color paints the trail, so the output trail records the sequence of corridor segments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:717:        corridor_color = candidate_color.get(r) or _first_real_corridor_color(g, r)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:718:        if corridor_color is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:722:            source_color[r] = corridor_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/26/code.py:724:            alt = _other_palette_color(real_colors, corridor_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/17/code.py:41:#      extensions have room and the local 3x3 windows remain clean.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/4/code.py:664:        room = {\"top\": bar_r0, \"bottom\": H - 1 - bar_r1}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/4/code.py:671:        room = {\"left\": bar_c0, \"right\": W - 1 - bar_c1}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/4/code.py:672:    return orientation, thickness, bar_color, (bar_r0, bar_c0, bar_r1, bar_c1), room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/4/code.py:679:def _pick_used_windows(rng, orientation, room, chain_lens, strip_width, span_len):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/4/code.py:690:                if room[side] < chain_len * 2 + 3 or len(slots[side]) < 3:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/4/code.py:706:        valid_sides = [side for side in sides if room[side] >= chain_len * 2 + 3 and len(slots[side]) >= 3]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/4/code.py:886:    orientation, _thickness, bar_color, bar_bounds, room = _bar_setup(rng, H, W)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/4/code.py:896:    picked = _pick_used_windows(rng, orientation, room, chain_lens, strip_width, span_len)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/31/code.py:3:# Name: 固定手性+交叉口强制转弯+螺旋走廊\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/31/code.py:38:#        corridors\"; combo turning is \"at a one-sided open intersection, turn in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/31/code.py:45:#      ordinary L-corridor. Each real path therefore performs exactly four\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/31/code.py:56:#      intended active rows still have a same-color corridor entrance at col 2-3.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/31/code.py:79:#    - Column choices satisfy `bar_start+3 <= x2 < x3 < x1 <= W-4`, leaving room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/31/code.py:129:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/31/code.py:130:    \"\"\"Original-task corridor predicate, kept for degeneration checks.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/31/code.py:311:            if _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/31/code.py:320:    \"\"\"Move magenta particles along clockwise spiral corridors with forced T-junction turns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:10:The original task had one enclosed room per region, a direction legend, and straight sliding\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:11:through open floor. This combo changes both the motion model and the room interior:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:13:  - each room contains an internal obstacle core\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:18:  - Original: a yellow inside a room with a right-pointing legend keeps stepping east until it\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:21:    side of the blue center block (clockwise) or the left side (counterclockwise). Inside the room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:25:  - Difference: the destination depends on contour order around a room-with-obstacle, not on a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:46:    preserve the room object. That fails once obstacles occupy the interior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:50:    direction. The combo instead needs a linearized cycle derived from the room contour.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:53:room is exactly `obstacle_core ∪ 1-cell shell`, so the room contour equals the yellow movement\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:60:  - define the room as `core ∪ shell`\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:61:  - define the colored wall as the 4-neighbor exterior of the room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:63:each completed room prevents ambiguous contacts between different regions. The generator rejects\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:98:    the obstacle genuinely changes the path rather than merely existing inside the room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:345:    Slide yellow pixels inside obstacle-filled rooms along the ordered boundary shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:355:    - For each bounded room, find its wall color and the matching legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:358:    - Trace the room's outer contour, cut it at the contour cell closest to the legend corner, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:364:    - Obstacles change the room contour itself, so the true movement path is the shell created by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:374:    room_mask = (g == bg) | (g == MOVER) | (g == OBSTACLE)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:377:    for pts in components_mask(room_mask, connectivity=4):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:381:        room = {(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in pts}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:387:        for r, c in room:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:391:                if (nr, nc) in room:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:406:            for p in _ordered_boundary_track(room, corner, clockwise, h, w)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:451:def _room_wall_cells(room: set[tuple[int, int]], h: int, w: int) -> set[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:453:    for r, c in room:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:455:            if 0 <= nr < h and 0 <= nc < w and (nr, nc) not in room:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:461:    walls = _room_wall_cells(blob, h, w)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:510:def _shape_has_simple_shell(room: set[tuple[int, int]], corner: str, clockwise: bool, h: int, w: int) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:511:    boundary = _boundary_cells(room)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:512:    core = room - boundary\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:523:        track = _ordered_boundary_track(room, corner, clockwise, h, w)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:549:        room = _grow_blob(canvas, (int(sr), int(sc)), target_size, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:550:        if room is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:553:            filled = _fill_holes(room, h, w)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:554:            if filled == room:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:556:            room = filled\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:557:        if any(not canvas[r, c] for r, c in room):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:560:        walls = _room_wall_cells(room, h, w)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:561:        boundary = _boundary_cells(room)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:562:        core = room - boundary\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:565:        if any(r in (0, h - 1) or c in (0, w - 1) for r, c in room | walls):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:567:        if any(occupied[r, c] for r, c in room | walls):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:569:        if not _shape_has_simple_shell(room, corner, clockwise, h, w):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:572:        track = _ordered_boundary_track(room, corner, clockwise, h, w)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:575:            \"room\": room,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:645:        room = grown[\"room\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:654:                \"room\": room,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:660:        reserve = room | walls\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:686:    expected = [reg[\"room\"] for reg in regions]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/_final_summary_20260517.json:203:    \"name\": \"十字形锚点 + 空心框锚点\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/_final_summary_20260517.json:481:    \"name\": \"十字形锚点 + 连接方向由锚点决定\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/27/code.py:42:#        legal perpendicular corridor exists or stops one cell earlier. Both A and B leave full\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/27/code.py:47:#      rows, plus a few additional ordinary real corridors. This keeps the new rule obvious\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/27/code.py:54:#    - Original _has_corridor accepted PARTICLE as traversable; that breaks sequential blocking,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/27/code.py:55:#      so the combo version allows only BG corridor cells on the working grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/27/code.py:69:#    - The generator reuses the original L/U corridor builders, which already enforce non-\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/27/code.py:87:#    - Trails occupy corridor background cells only and do not overwrite colored bars, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/27/code.py:104:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/27/code.py:140:            if _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/27/code.py:151:    \"\"\"Return the first same-color corridor entrance for row r, or None.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/27/code.py:165:    \"\"\"Check whether row r is a genuine movable corridor in the base grid.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/27/code.py:239:    - Even rows carry colored bars; odd rows are candidate corridor rows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/27/code.py:240:    - A real corridor is a bg route flanked by same-color bars, with optional L/U turns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/19/code.py:18:    - yellow (4): travels its full available corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/19/code.py:19:    - orange (7): travels half of its available corridor, using floor(free_steps / 2)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/19/code.py:60:    - orange is only accepted when it has a strictly partial move, and pink is only accepted when it has room available but still stays put\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/19/code.py:64:    - orange travel uses a precomputed budget from its wall-determined direction and static corridor length; the generator avoids layouts where another moving pixel would need to redefine that budget to remain interpretable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/19/code.py:408:        \"pink_room_but_static\": PINK in by_color and by_color[PINK][\"free_steps\"] >= 2 and pink_in == pink_out,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/19/code.py:426:    - Yellow then spends its entire free corridor in that direction, orange spends half of that corridor, and pink stays where it is.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/19/code.py:429:    Key insight: Direction is no longer a property of the whole region; it is chosen independently per mover from the nearest wall color, while the mover's own color separately encodes how much of that direction-specific corridor it is allowed to use.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/19/code.py:643:        and metrics[\"pink_room_but_static\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/23/code.py:73:#    Only one chain is used, which avoids clutter while leaving enough room for the boundary-touch\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/16/code.py:243:        corridors: list[list[tuple[int, int]]] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/16/code.py:257:                corridors.append(cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/16/code.py:258:        if not corridors:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/16/code.py:261:        n_ext = int(rng.integers(1, min(2, len(corridors)) + 1))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/16/code.py:262:        chosen_ids = rng.choice(len(corridors), size=n_ext, replace=False)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/16/code.py:265:            corridor = corridors[int(idx)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/16/code.py:266:            max_len = min(3, len(corridor))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/16/code.py:268:            cells = corridor[:ext_len]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:27:# - D10/2 后: 真假不再看颜色，而看通道宽度。真走廊宽 1 格，假走廊宽 2 格。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:32:#   这里上下并不在同一列重合，所以旧 solver 会看漏；但人类能看出它们围着同一条 1 格窄通道。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:38:#   融合逻辑在 mid[1] 成功，因为上/下 bar 在半径 1 内都可见，且中间通道宽度仍是 1 格。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:55:# - 原 _has_corridor(水平方向) 假设上下 bar 必须在同一列精确出现；融合后失效，改为“半径 1 内可见 bar 支撑”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:56:# - 原 _has_corridor(竖直方向) 假设左右必须同色；融合后颜色无语义，改为“左右都为彩色即可”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:123:def _has_true_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:124:    \"\"\"True iff (r,c) is inside a real narrow corridor under the fused rule.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:138:    \"\"\"Trace one particle using the fused corridor predicate.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:153:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_true_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:163:    \"\"\"Move magenta particles through broken narrow corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:168:    - Real corridors are 1-row channels between adjacent bar rows; fake corridors are 2-row gaps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:173:      1-cell-wide corridor. Horizontal corridor recognition tolerates 1-cell rail gaps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:191:            if _has_true_corridor(g, r, c, \"right\"):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:215:def _exact_width_has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:216:    \"\"\"Width-based corridor test without D8-style gap tolerance.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:244:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _exact_width_has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:263:            if _exact_width_has_corridor(g, r, c, \"right\"):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:474:        \"true_corridors\": 0,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:475:        \"fake_corridors\": 0,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:493:            metrics[\"true_corridors\"] += 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/8/code.py:499:            metrics[\"fake_corridors\"] += 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db0c5428/22/code.py:66:#      room on the bottom/right so the 15x15 output never clips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/24/code.py:7:# - The source task still uses striped same-color bar pairs as corridors and launches\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/24/code.py:9:#   each completed segment erases the wall pair flanking every traveled corridor cell,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/24/code.py:51:# - No rule depends on absolute color ids. Colors only mark corridor membership; the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/24/code.py:52:#   transformation depends on corridor structure, travel order, and whether wall pairs\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/24/code.py:73:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/24/code.py:89:def _corridor_walls(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/24/code.py:122:            walls = _corridor_walls(grid, r, c, direction)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/24/code.py:131:                if _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/24/code.py:137:        walls = _corridor_walls(grid, r, c, direction)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/24/code.py:144:    \"\"\"Return source-task seed rows whose left entrance is a valid real corridor.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/24/code.py:235:    \"\"\"Run the erase-and-relaunch corridor combo.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/24/code.py:240:      horizontal corridors plus L/U-turn gadgets exactly as in the source task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/24/code.py:244:    - After that segment finishes, each traveled corridor cell erases its two same-color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/24/code.py:247:      of the terminal corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/24/code.py:253:      pass leaves visible holes in the corridor walls, and those missing wall pairs are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/4/code.py:67:#   them into side corridors by geometry.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/4/code.py:72:#   each intended sprite lies in exactly one side corridor and overlaps the hub's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/4/code.py:78:#   2. detach and scatter rotated copies into side-specific corridors,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/4/code.py:79:#   3. optionally add a distractor into a corner corridor that matches no side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/4/code.py:95:# - True sprites live only in side corridors; distractors live only in corners.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/4/code.py:116:#   in its corridor. Generator places exactly one true sprite per active side and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/4/code.py:117:#   corner distractors outside those corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:31:    - The movable empty space is no longer two isolated rooms. It is one enclosed serial system:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:32:      a large chamber and a small chamber are linked by a tiny elbow corridor, so a yellow can\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:33:      leave the first room and continue inside the second.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:42:    - A yellow starts near the left side of A. Under the source task it would stay inside one room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:45:    - Under this combo it first moves right across A, passes through the elbow corridor, then\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:63:    `components_mask(passable, connectivity=4)` used to mean \"one enclosed component == one room\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:88:  - Humans can see one large room and one small room joined by a single black doorway, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:90:  - The larger room always acts first because the legends are paired by room size, not wall color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:329:        corridor = set(comp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:331:            corridor -= cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:332:        if not (1 <= len(corridor) <= CONNECTOR_LEN):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:334:        corridor_comps = _subset_components(corridor)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:335:        if len(corridor_comps) != 1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:361:                    if (nr, nc) in corridor:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:371:                \"corridor\": corridor,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:386:    corridor = system[\"corridor\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:394:        if cur in corridor:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:411:        if nxt in corridor:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:477:      and a smaller chamber linked by a tiny elbow corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:595:    corridor = [(c1[0] + k * small_dir[0], c1[1] + k * small_dir[1]) for k in range(CONNECTOR_LEN)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:596:    c_entry = corridor[-1]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:610:    corridor_set = set(corridor)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:611:    big_ring -= corridor_set\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:612:    small_ring -= corridor_set\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:613:    if corridor_set & big_cells or corridor_set & small_cells:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:622:    all_used = big_cells | small_cells | big_ring | small_ring | corridor_set\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:629:    for cell in corridor_set:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:631:            if nbr in corridor_set or nbr in big_cells or nbr in small_cells:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:647:        \"corridor\": corridor_set,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:711:    expected = set(layout[\"big\"][\"cells\"]) | set(layout[\"small\"][\"cells\"]) | set(layout[\"corridor\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:774:        \"corridor_len\": len(systems[0][\"corridor\"]),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:9:#   The original task had a 1-cell launch buffer at col 1 and then a corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:13:#   supported corridor cell at col 4.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:16:#   corridor cell, cols 8-10 might be another orange gap, and cols 11+ restore\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:17:#   the corridor. Original logic would cross both the launch gap and the later\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:35:#   (b) requires the first supported real corridor cell to be exactly at col 4,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:38:#   corridor cell; the generator preserves that by never carving width features\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:41:#   The generator paints cols 1-3 as background only after all corridor and fake\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:44:#   overlap with vertical turn structures and guarantees enough horizontal room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:52:#   The scene remains the original striped corridor world. The only added visual\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:75:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:105:            if _has_corridor(grid, nr, nc, direction):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:116:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:143:    return _has_corridor(grid, r, CORRIDOR_START, \"right\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:162:    \"\"\"Move magenta particles through shifted corridors with bounded gap crossing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:166:    - Colored bars on even rows start at col 4 and form real/fake corridors on odd rows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:172:      perpendicular supported corridor, if one exists. Otherwise it stops.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:176:      real particles must survive that exact gap to enter the corridor, but\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/12/code.py:57:#   sprites, and have a trail corridor that avoids the anchor, foreign sprites, and other trails.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/12/code.py:734:    edge_room = min(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/12/code.py:740:    max_radius = float(edge_room - 0.6)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:3:# Name: 障碍色转向+交叉口信号灯\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:16:   - 保留原题的条纹几何：偶数行是彩条，奇数行是水平通道，col 0 全是粒子，col 1 保持背景。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:22:       2. 信号灯层：如果前方一步是特殊信号像素，则它先决定“此交叉口是直行还是转弯”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:23:            * 8 = 在该交叉口转弯\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:24:            * 9 = 在该交叉口直行\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:33:                  ... BG [8] ... 则在 8 这个交叉口直接转入唯一侧支，后面的挡块即使存在也不触发。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:34:   - 差异因此是显式可见的：同样是 T 字交叉口，8/9 决定“转不转”；而 2/3 决定“若转，则朝哪边转”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:41:       * 8/9: 交叉口信号语义\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:49:   - 原 _has_corridor 假设通道中心只能是 BG/PARTICLE；D9 融合后信号像素本身也必须可视为可通行，否则粒子会把信号灯当墙。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:52:   - 新增假设 1：若信号色为 8，则信号交叉口必须存在可转入的合法侧支。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:60:   - 所有竖直结构统一按 3 列窗口预留，避免不同交叉口的竖直通道彼此贴边重叠。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:61:   - 挡块转弯使用原题式几何：挡块在 `c_v`，真正竖直通道在 `c_v-1`，上下都先开一个可选入口，再只向被选择方向继续延展。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:62:   - 信号交叉口使用更直接的 D9 式几何：信号像素就在奇数行通道单元，只有一个上下入口被打开，因此“转弯”是唯一可执行动作。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:70:   - 样例里至少有一条粒子路径先经过 9 再撞到 2/3，因此人类能看到“先看信号决定是否进交叉口，再看挡块颜色决定向哪边转”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:76:   - 每个真实通道只放 0-2 个关键事件，且关键列有全局间隔，避免整张图出现密集交织的十字路口。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:81:       * 8/9 控制“是否在交叉口转”\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:86:   - `_choose_signal_turn()` 假设信号交叉口若有多个候选方向，则前方挡块色可消歧；generator 当前主要生成唯一侧支，所以这个回退分支只是容错。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:88:   - 对于双开口挡块，solver 会只检查颜色指定的一侧是否为合法走廊；generator 保证该侧至少有一步合法 corridor。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:116:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:154:        if 0 <= nr < H and 0 <= nc < W and _has_corridor(grid, nr, nc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:204:        if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:213:    \"\"\"Move magenta particles through striped corridors with fused local instructions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:218:    - Blocker cue colors 2/3 can appear ahead of a corridor to encode relative turn direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:226:      particle turns counter-clockwise or clockwise, provided the target side is a legal corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:614:        if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, chosen):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/1/code.py:639:        if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, chosen):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/13/code.py:26:#    - Example corridor with legend direction right:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/13/code.py:27:#      input yellow at the right wall -> try right -> bounce to left -> cross the room ->\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/13/code.py:33:#    - Keep the original legend machinery, wall colors, and enclosed-room topology.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/13/code.py:42:#    - Border-color lookup by adjacent wall majority still works because each room keeps one wall\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/13/code.py:51:#    - Region growth still reserves interior, walls, and a one-cell wall buffer, so rooms do not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/13/code.py:54:#      reflection simulator keeps all final positions inside the same room with distinct endpoints.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/13/code.py:58:#      output yellows detach and land mid-room after rebounds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/13/code.py:64:#    - The only moving objects remain the yellow pixels, and they stay inside clean enclosed rooms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/13/code.py:65:#    - Empty rooms are allowed, but populated rooms are filtered to show a clear detach-and-scatter\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/13/code.py:382:    - Border legends are solid rectangles on the outer frame; their fill color matches a room-wall color, and their center/indicator dots encode an initial direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/13/code.py:386:    - Each yellow attempts to move with that direction for a fixed number of steps, reflecting off walls whenever the next step would leave the room; already-settled yellow endpoints still block later yellows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:7:#   The striped corridor geometry stays the same as the base task: even rows\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:11:#   source has a corridor-palette color, and it may move only through corridors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:13:#   cell is painted in the output with the current corridor color. Because the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:14:#   admissible corridor color must equal the particle color, the same visible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:17:#   In the base task, a source on row 5 entered the first real corridor on that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:19:#   source at (5, 0) is red and the first real corridor is blue, the row does\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:20:#   not move at all. If another row has a red source and red corridor bars, that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:38:#   2. Original corridor tests only required \"same non-bg bars\". That is no\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:40:#      color, or a red source could enter a blue corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:42:#      an active corridor color so vertical gap cells remain paintable even when\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:49:#   are assigned only after corridor geometry is fixed, so source coloring cannot\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:50:#   create overlaps or break turn sealing. Vertical corridor columns are still\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:53:#   The leftmost colored sources are isolated from the maze by background col 1,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:54:#   so humans can compare source color with nearby corridor-bar color directly.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:55:#   Trails reuse existing corridor colors instead of adding a new marker layer,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:64:#   3. Real multi-turn paths keep one consistent corridor color along the whole\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:83:def _corridor_color(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:86:    \"\"\"Return the corridor color for a legal cell, else None.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:106:    \"\"\"Find the first legal same-color horizontal corridor entrance.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:109:        color = _corridor_color(grid, r, c, \"right\", particle_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:136:            step_color = _corridor_color(grid, nr, nc, direction, particle_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:148:            turn_color = _corridor_color(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir, particle_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:199:    \"\"\"Move color-grouped particles and paint their matching-corridor trails.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:203:      col 1 stays background. Even rows carry corridor bars.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:204:    - Real corridors are same-color bar pairs around a 1-cell path; fake rows\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:208:    - A source can enter or turn only into corridors whose flanking bar color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:210:    - Every visited travel cell is painted with the current corridor color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:216:      corridor and it becomes the trail color, so matched rows both move and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:275:    \"\"\"Reserve a 3-column window for a vertical corridor and return the wall col.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:485:    \"\"\"Choose a source color different from the corridor color on that row.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:500:        corridor_color = None\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:507:                corridor_color = above\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:510:        if entrance_col is None or corridor_color is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:512:        bar_above = next((c for c in range(width) if int(g[row - 1, c]) == corridor_color), width)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:513:        bar_below = next((c for c in range(width) if int(g[row + 1, c]) == corridor_color), width)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:515:            candidates.append((i, row, corridor_color))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/3/code.py:536:    if len({corridor_color for _, _, corridor_color in real_candidates}) < _MIN_MOVED_COLOR_GROUPS:\n/home/li