 valid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/35/code.py:46:  2. one colored decoration pixel in a neighboring fake corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/35/code.py:56:- `_has_corridor()` can no longer treat only `{BG, PARTICLE}` as traversable,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/35/code.py:58:- The original `_trace()` assumed that \"blocked + valid side corridor\" implies\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/35/code.py:65:  the combo, a control pixel may sit on the source corridor, so entrance\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/35/code.py:83:  local difference between them is which neighboring fake corridor carries the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/35/code.py:101:- The palette is kept to exactly 6 colors: 3 corridor colors plus background,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/35/code.py:147:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/35/code.py:163:def _corridor_color(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> int | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/35/code.py:164:    \"\"\"Color of the bar pair that makes (r,c) a valid corridor cell.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/35/code.py:182:    \"\"\"True if row r is locally a fake corridor at column c.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/35/code.py:203:        color = _corridor_color(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/35/code.py:244:            if 0 <= tr < h and 0 <= tc < w and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/35/code.py:280:    \"\"\"Move magenta particles using control-gated, hint-resolved corridor turns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/35/code.py:293:      corridor color with the decoration pixel in the adjacent fake channel on that side.\n/home