ome/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/32/code.py:353:      perpendicular corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/32/code.py:354:    - Every traveled corridor cell erases its flanking same-color wall pair to BG.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/32/code.py:359:    - The erased walls are not just an output trail. They mutate the corridor network\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/12/code.py:38:#   into a maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/27/code.py:38:#    This reserves room for one-cell obstacle detours and the translated shadow copy.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/17/code.py:25:#     - 原 `_has_corridor(..., left/right)` 假设墙就在相邻行；融合后必须改成最近墙搜索，否则三格宽水平走廊完全失效。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/17/code.py:118:def _is_horizontal_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/17/code.py:123:def _is_vertical_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/17/code.py:128:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/17/code.py:132:        return _is_horizontal_corridor(grid, r, c)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/17/code.py:133:    return _is_vertical_corridor(grid, r, c)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/17/code.py:153:            if _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/17/code.py:173:        if not _is_horizontal_corridor(grid, r, c):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/17/code.py:188:    \"\"\"Move magenta particles through irregularly spaced three-cell corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/17/code.py:192:    - Consecutive bar rows are separated by 1-3 background rows; only some 3-row bands are true same-color corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/17/code.py:198:    - When a colored blocker is directly ahead, it turns 90 degrees only if one adjacent cell belongs to a 3-column-wide vertical corridor with matching side walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/17/code.py:233:def _legacy_has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/17/code.py:263:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _legacy_has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/33/code.py:65:#    - The source square is placed with comfortable margins and with room above,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/8/code.py:60:#      non-singleton foreign group on a line corridor = obstacle group, bent output\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/8/code.py:379:#    foreign-color group on a line corridor is an obstacle set; blocked edges bend around\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D5/1/code.py:44:#      scattered positions and accepts only those whose trail corridor is clear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/24/code.py:32:     the corridors among those frames rather than in a dedicated right strip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/24/code.py:39:  Two red sprites sit near the upper one in the central corridor, and one red sprite sits\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/24/code.py:63:  move into the frame corridors. The combo solver switches to an exact hollow-rectangle test:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/24/code.py:81:  every full frame rectangle, so sprites appear in corridors among frames and never inside\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/24/code.py:90:  are mixed into the between-frame corridors instead of isolated on the far right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/24/code.py:102:- The corridor-only placement keeps the frame cluster readable even in the denser 2x3 layout.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/24/code.py:107:- Every sample places sprites left of the rightmost frame edge inside the frame-union corridors,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/24/code.py:206:    Remove corridor sprites and display per-frame tallies inside the frames.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/24/code.py:212:    - Small monochrome sprites are scattered in the background corridors around the frames.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/24/code.py:297:    \"\"\"Choose a total that is visually rich but still easy to pack into corridors.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/24/code.py:442:    \"\"\"Allow only corridor cells inside the overall frame arrangement.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/24/code.py:522:    \"\"\"Place a distractor sprite anywhere feasible in the corridor canvas.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/1/code.py:382:        room = axis - sz - OBS_BOTH_GAP\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/1/code.py:383:        if room < 2 * lo:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/1/code.py:385:        a = random.randint(lo, min(hi_cap, room - lo))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/1/code.py:386:        b = _rand_thickness(lo, min(hi_cap, room - a))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/24/code.py:24:#    generator always creates at least three interacting shapes in one corridor, with at\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/24/code.py:55:#    The interaction is confined to one central corridor: one early blocker, one middle\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:28:#    - Horizontal real corridors are recognized only when the two bar rows have\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:35:#    - A horizontal corridor cell is still valid if each bar row shows the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:37:#      rail crack as part of one corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:47:#      dashed corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:58:#    - We keep only straight corridors and L-turns in the generator. That keeps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:63:#    - Original horizontal corridor test assumed exact same-column overlap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:64:#      Broken rails violate that, so `_has_corridor()` must switch to local\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:67:#      a real corridor. Here many real rows have no exact overlap anywhere, so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:85:#      cracks do not destroy corridor identity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:86:#    - Within those same dashed corridors, some wider rail absences are crossed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:107:# - `_iter_active_rows()` assumes the first visible bars of a real corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:137:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:138:    \"\"\"True if (r,c) belongs to a corridor under the fused rule.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:171:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:192:            if _has_corridor(grid, nr, nc, direction):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:203:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:214:    \"\"\"Yield particle rows that have a valid real-corridor entrance.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:221:            if _has_corridor(grid, r, c, \"right\"):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:249:    \"\"\"Move magenta particles through broken rail corridors with a width cap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:254:    - Real horizontal corridors are same-colored rail pairs, but the rails may\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:261:      blocker forces a 90-degree turn into the unique supported corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:266:    - Same-colored dashed rails still define one corridor, but only short joint\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:277:def _legacy_has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:307:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _legacy_has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/62593bfd/20/code.py:453:        raise ValueError(\"not enough room for diagonal pair\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/3/code.py:229:        room = axis - sz - OBS_BOTH_GAP\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/3/code.py:230:        if room < 2 * lo:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/3/code.py:232:        a = random.randint(lo, min(hi_cap, room - lo))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/3/code.py:233:        b = _rand_thickness(lo, min(hi_cap, room - a))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:24:    - 保持原题的条纹骨架: 偶数行为横条, 奇数行为水平通道, 第0列全是粒子, 第1列全是背景.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:46:    - 单格阻挡块只放在当前为 BG 的通道格, 并尽量避开同色邻居, 使其保持“孤立块”外观.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:50:    - 人类可直接观察到: 有些粒子停在普通通道中途, 但另一些粒子会停在“异色夹口”的拐弯入口上.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:53:    - 仍保持规则的横条+通道版式, 只在少量通道位置加入单格块和少量假入口.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:69:def _corridor_flanks(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:83:def _corridor_kind(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> str:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:84:    \"\"\"Classify a passable cell as a real corridor, fake corridor, or neither.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:85:    flanks = _corridor_flanks(grid, r, c, direction)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:94:def _has_real_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:95:    return _corridor_kind(grid, r, c, direction) == \"real\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:106:        if _corridor_kind(grid, r, c, \"right\") != \"real\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:155:            if stop_on_fake and _corridor_kind(grid, r, c, direction) == \"fake\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:180:            kind = _corridor_kind(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:252:    \"\"\"Move particles through striped corridors with fake-trap mouths and blocker-driven turns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:257:    - Real corridors are flanked by same-color bars; fake corridors are flanked by different colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:258:    - Some channels contain isolated colored blocker cells that act as obstacles inside the corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:261:    - A particle starts on a row whose entrance is a real horizontal corridor and moves right through bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:262:    - After each move, if the particle is now inside a fake corridor cell relative to its travel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:265:      corridor mouth lets it turn and continue. If the unique available mouth is fake, the particle\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:270:      attempt. The final behavior depends on whether the forced mouth is a true same-color corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:271:      or a fake mismatched corridor that functions as a trap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/11/code.py:70:#    - later beams terminate when they approach previously painted teal corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/11/code.py:77:#    dense maze. Decoy rectangles stay away from the active lanes to avoid ambiguous\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/40/code.py:34:#   corridors are channels flanked by same-color bars.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/40/code.py:55:# - A separate straight real corridor contains a short horizontal gap of width\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/40/code.py:74:# - Entrance detection still assumes the first real corridor starts at col 2 or\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/40/code.py:76:# - Turn targets are still required to be supported real corridor cells. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/40/code.py:77:#   generator guarantees both fork turn cells satisfy `_has_corridor(...)`.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/40/code.py:85:#   exist and the visually longer side has room for a truncating gap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/40/code.py:99:# - Gap markings are localized erasures on otherwise regular corridors, so they\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/40/code.py:103:# - Colors still only indicate corridor matching vs mismatch. No ordering or\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/40/code.py:111:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/40/code.py:128:    \"\"\"Return the first valid real-corridor entrance column for row r.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/40/code.py:153:        if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/40/code.py:187:            next_run = 0 if _has_corridor(grid, nr, nc, direction) else unsupported_run + 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/40/code.py:265:    \"\"\"Move particles through striped corridors with length-aware ambiguous turns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/40/code.py:270:    - Real corridors are bg cells flanked by same-color bars; fake corridors use\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/40/code.py:278:      directions. If both are valid real corridors, it chooses the branch with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/7/code.py:28:#   they are confined to the background corridors between the four frames.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/7/code.py:30:#   Top-left frame = width 7, red, with 2 matching red sprites in the corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/7/code.py:31:#   Top-right frame = width 11, blue, with 4 matching blue sprites in the corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/7/code.py:58:# - Sprites are then placed on a separate placement canvas that only exposes corridor cells:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/7/code.py:85:# - Sprites are restricted to inter-frame corridors, not a detached right-side panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/7/code.py:153:    - Small monochrome sprites appear only in the background corridors between those frames.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/7/code.py:291:        room = axis - sz - OBS_BOTH_GAP\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/7/code.py:292:        if room < 2 * lo:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/7/code.py:294:        a = random.randint(lo, min(hi_cap, room - lo))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/7/code.py:295:        b = _rand_thickness(lo, min(hi_cap, room - a))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/17/code.py:42:      only in the corridors between those frame rectangles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/17/code.py:46:      corridor and one blue sprite is placed near the lower-right corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/17/code.py:61:  - Frames shrink from width 11 to width 9 so the 2x2 layout plus visible corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/17/code.py:81:    corridors \"between frames\" and prevents accidental placement inside a hollow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/17/code.py:96:  - The generator keeps all sprites in corridor background, not inside frames and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/17/code.py:217:    - Small monochrome sprites sit in the corridors between frame rectangles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/39/code.py:23:#   - The settled color is not magenta: it is the color of the terminal corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/39/code.py:28:#       rightmost free cell. The solver writes that cell with T's corridor color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/39/code.py:44:#   - Original `_has_corridor` accepted PARTICLE as traversable. That breaks the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/39/code.py:50:#     The combo must recover the terminal corridor color from the current work grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/39/code.py:70:#     corridor color rather than staying magenta.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/39/code.py:73:#     both settled cells take the target corridor color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/39/code.py:77:#     cells inside