r(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/13/code.py:256:    \"\"\"Move particles through striped corridors with palette-first ambiguous turns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/13/code.py:267:    - If both turns are valid, compare the two corridor colors against the corner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/32/code.py:372:        room = axis - sz - OBS_BOTH_GAP\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/32/code.py:373:        if room < 2 * lo:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/32/code.py:375:        a = random.randint(lo, min(hi_cap, room - lo))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/32/code.py:376:        b = _rand_thickness(lo, min(hi_cap, room - a))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:29:  degrees only when a perpendicular same-color corridor is available.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:33:- Keep the exact same motion rule and the same real/fake corridor distinction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:36:  2. For every occupied corridor cell, the two colored wall cells that define that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:37:     local corridor are erased to BG.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:49:  occupied corridor cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:52:  pairs flanking those same occupied corridor cells. The walked corridor therefore\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:58:  corridors and turn only at legal junctions\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:69:- `_has_corridor()` still assumes traversable cells are BG or PARTICLE in the input.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:77:  corridors whose bars begin at column 2 or 3. The generator still guarantees this.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:84:- The generator keeps the original corridor grammar: striped rows, same-color real\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:90:  `_corridor_walls()`, so it cannot go out of bounds or delete arbitrary structure.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:94:- Across a few examples, a human can see that visited corridors are not merely\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:100:  the channel and the corresponding corridor bars disappear\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:104:- The two effects live on complementary cell sets: trail on corridor path cells,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:106:- Unvisited corridors remain fully intact, so the output preserves clear contrast\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:108:- The existing generator spacing for vertical corridors avoids dense overlapping\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:116:  determined by visible corridor occupancy.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:122:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:123:    \"\"\"True if (r,c) is a passable cell flanked by same-color corridor bars.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:138:def _corridor_walls(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:160:    \"\"\"Return the first genuine horizontal corridor entrance for row r, else None.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:192:    \"\"\"Trace from (r,c) and return visited non-start cells plus corridor wall cells.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:206:            walls = _corridor_walls(grid, r, c, direction)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:215:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:223:        walls = _corridor_walls(grid, r, c, direction)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:267:    \"\"\"Move magenta particles and replace traversed corridors with a fused trail result.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:271:    - Column 0 is filled with particles; true horizontal corridors live on odd rows\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:273:    - Some real corridors include legal vertical turn corridors; fake corridors use\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:281:    - Every traversed corridor cell also erases its two flanking corridor-bar cells to BG.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:286:      traced route is rendered: the path itself becomes magenta while the corridor rails\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/2/code.py:329:    \"\"\"Reserve a 3-column window for a vertical corridor and return the wall column.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/32/code.py:10:#    我把可见模式收紧为两类，正好对应题意里的“十字形 vs 单点”：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/62593bfd/13/code.py:92:#    - Assumption: there is enough horizontal room for packed sides.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/17/code.py:19:#      corridors, so repeated growth can visibly thicken several blocks and cause\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/17/code.py:30:#      create a maze-like center, but still visually separable in the input.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/17/code.py:43:#      Broken: growth must be able to block corridors, so it overwrites teal trail\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/23/code.py:29:- A magenta particle starts in column 0, follows same-color corridors through orange\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/23/code.py:31:  perpendicular same-color corridor, and the output keeps only the terminal magenta\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/23/code.py:54:- Extra particles stay on separate straight corridors, giving repeated evidence that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/23/code.py:67:- Original entrance filtering still matters: only rows whose first real corridor starts\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/23/code.py:71:  corridor exists.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/23/code.py:81:- Extra particles are placed on disjoint real corridors outside the protected band, so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/23/code.py:95:- All trails stay inside 1-cell corridors and never repaint the colored bars.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/23/code.py:109:- Active particles only appear on rows with valid real-corridor entrances.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/23/code.py:117:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/23/code.py:136:    \"\"\"Return the first real-corridor entrance column for row r, or None.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/23/code.py:159:    \"\"\"Single-step proposal from the static corridor geometry.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/23/code.py:171:        if _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/23/code.py:299:    - Even rows are colored bars; odd rows are horizontal corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/23/code.py:300:    - Real corridors are same-color bar pairs that may connect through vertical shafts.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/23/code.py:305:      cell, it may turn 90 degrees into the unique perpendicular same-color corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/20/code.py:57:# - \"The board is roomy enough for 2-3 objects\" is false; the generator must enlarge\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/16/code.py:16:#    corridor. The combo changes two parts together.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/16/code.py:19:#    - Input side (D20/2): instead of at most one L/U detour, each real corridor is a 2-channel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/16/code.py:35:#    - The entrance scan assumes the first real corridor begins at col 2 or 3 and that fake /\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/16/code.py:50:#    corridors in the input. The rule depends only on visibly matching flank colors, not on hidden\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/16/code.py:79:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/16/code.py:96:    \"\"\"Return the left-side corridor entrance for row r, if it exists at col 2 or 3.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/16/code.py:128:            if 0 <= tr < h and 0 <= tc < w and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/16/code.py:159:    \"\"\"Move particles through multi-turn same-color corridors and mark only the corners.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/16/code.py:163:    - Even rows are colored bar rows; odd rows are corridor rows or empty rows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/16/code.py:167:    - A valid particle row is one whose first corridor entrance is a background cell flanked by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/16/code.py:170:      direction, it turns 90 degrees into the unique perpendicular same-color corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/16/code.py:177:      from the corridor geometry rather than copying a visible trail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/15/code.py:50:#      Here cross-beam overlap would create order-dependent mixed-color corridors. The generator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/15/code.py:67:#      messy shared corridors with conflicting colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/15/code.py:362:        room = axis - sz - OBS_BOTH_GAP\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/15/code.py:363:        if room < 2 * lo:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/15/code.py:365:        a = random.randint(lo, min(hi_cap, room - lo))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/15/code.py:366:        b = _rand_thickness(lo, min(hi_cap, room - a))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:25:      - 仍然使用原题的条纹布局: 偶数行为横条行, 奇数行为水平通道行, 第0列全是粒子, 第1列全是背景.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:27:      - 新增对象是“走廊内孤立阻挡块”: 放在真实水平通道里, 自身是单格彩色像素, 视觉上区别于长条.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:33:        - 粒子在真实水平通道内向右走.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:35:        - 异色通道只是背景噪声, 即使经过相关区域附近也不会因为“假”而停.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:37:        - 粒子在真实水平通道里先撞到一个单格阻挡块, 这一步复用原题的“前方有彩色格就尝试转弯”.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:51:    - 转向判定仍只接受真走廊; 假走廊是终点而不是合法转向目标, 所以 _has_corridor 不能放宽.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:53:    - assert 依赖“同一时刻至多一个合法垂直/水平转向”; generator 通过非相邻真实通道与vcol窗口保留来保证.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:55:    - 活动真实通道优先选成彼此不相邻, 这样 trap_turn 总能朝相邻 fake channel 开口, 不会污染另一条活动入口.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:60:    - 人类能直接看到“单格块挡住了水平通道”.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:77:    \"\"\"Return the first valid real-corridor entrance column for row r.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:101:def _corridor_flanks(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:115:def _corridor_kind(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> str:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:117:    flanks = _corridor_flanks(grid, r, c, direction)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:126:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:127:    \"\"\"True iff (r,c) is a real corridor cell flanked by same-color walls.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:128:    return _corridor_kind(grid, r, c, direction) == \"real\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:158:            kind = _corridor_kind(grid, r, c, direction)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:168:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:185:        kind = _corridor_kind(grid, r, c, direction)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:198:    \"\"\"Move magenta particles through real corridors with blockers and fake-corridor traps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:203:      (real corridors), others mismatch (fake corridors).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:204:    - Real horizontal corridors may contain isolated colored blocker cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:207:    - A particle starts from each odd row whose left entrance is a real horizontal corridor and moves right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:209:      an obstacle; when blocked, the particle may turn 90 degrees only into a perpendicular real corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:211:      current travel direction, it has entered a fake corridor and stops immediately.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:212:    - Otherwise it stops at the grid edge or when a blocker offers no legal real-corridor turn.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:215:    - The fused behavior is local: isolated blockers redirect motion, while fake corridors are terminal. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/9/code.py:217:      corridor mouth, so the particle stops inside a visibly mismatched side channel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:18:#   or dead end\"; one round is \"launch rightward, but stop before entering corridor segment 3\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:20:#   1. the horizontal segment entered from the start cell counts as corridor 1,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:21:#   2. the first perpendicular turn enters corridor 2,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:22:#   3. if another legal turn would enter corridor 3, the particle stops on the current cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:28:#      horizontal row, but this would be corridor 3, so the particle stops there because of D6/2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:34:#   with plain D13/2, the intermediate stop positions are forced by a repeated corridor-limit motif.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:37:# - The corridor limit is fixed at N=2. Using N=1 would erase most turning structure; using larger\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:40:#   corridor cap, plus 1-2 singleton L-turn sources. This keeps repeated evidence while avoiding a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:43:#   lands at the mouth of a target horizontal corridor, so re-launching to the right is visually\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:49:# - Original trace assumed every unique legal turn is always taken. This breaks under the corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:50:#   cap, so the turn step must stop when `corridors_used >= 2` even if a legal turn exists.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:66:# - No hidden metadata is used. The only cues are corridor geometry, repeated interior stop points,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:70:# - The grid remains the original striped corridor drawing. No labels, markers, or recoloring are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:77:# - The only hidden variable a solver must infer is the fixed corridor cap N=2, and that cap is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:83:# - The corridor count resets at the start of each round. The generator relies on this by placing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:106:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:160:    max_corridors: int | None,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:163:    \"\"\"Trace a right-launched particle, optionally capping how many corridors it may enter.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:166:    corridors_used = 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:183:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:189:        if max_corridors is not None and corridors_used >= max_corridors:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:193:        corridors_used += 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:198:            \"corridors_used\": corridors_used,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:208:    max_corridors: int | None,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:220:        end_r, end_c, meta = _trace(g, rr, cc, max_corridors=max_corridors, return_stats=True)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:252:    limited_first, first_stats = _move_once(grid, max_corridors=MAX_CORRIDORS, return_stats=True)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:254:        limited_first, max_corridors=MAX_CORRIDORS, return_stats=True\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:257:        grid, max_corridors=None, return_stats=True\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:290:    \"\"\"Move magenta particles through the corridor network for exactly two capped rounds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:299:      cell and exactly one perpendicular same-color corridor is available.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:300:    - Each launch may enter at most two corridor segments. If a legal turn would enter segment 3,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:307:      two corridor segments, then relaunch those new positions to the right and apply the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:308:      two-corridor cap again.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:310:    first = _move_once(np.array(grid, dtype=int), max_corridors=MAX_CORRIDORS)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:311:    second = _move_once(first, max_corridors=MAX_CORRIDORS)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/22/code.py:342:    \"\"\"Reserve a 3-column window for one vertical corridor.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/16/code.py:59:#   patches have enough room for marker protrusions and body growth.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/62593bfd/6/code.py:319:        raise ValueError(\"no room to create a visible packing shift\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/38/code.py:30:#      corridors are visible; the output is the whole legend-free board.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/38/code.py:77:#    from the original continuous corridors. Requiring both row and column trim\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/3