lated boxes from overlapping a moved corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/29/code.py:79:#    - The generator enforces a clear background corridor, unique adjacent head, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/19/code.py:36:#   The generator keeps marker cells non-overlapping, in bounds, and outside the legend scan corridor. Same-color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/4/code.py:80:- The legend scan corridor is reserved so the first non-bg cells from the bottom\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/4/code.py:104:- The reserved 3-column legend corridor keeps the dense legend visually separate\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/18/code.py:58:   - Each assembly reserves the entire corridor from destination to container.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/5/code.py:52:    - Marker pixels must stay in bounds, avoid the legend footprint, avoid the left-side scan corridor,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/15/code.py:87:#     - The trajectory is visible as a vertical/diagonal band in the empty corridor,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/15/code.py:92:#     - Bars are short and the top area is tall, leaving a wide corridor for trails.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/15/code.py:97:#     - Assumption: there is enough free room to the right for every forced shift.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/26/code.py:43:#   color, then paste the moved container on top. What remains visible is a stepped diagonal corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/26/code.py:48:#   Combo task: move NW by 3, recolor the same 3 grey cells, paint the vacated diagonal swept corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/26/code.py:85:#   row and column both change, the box leaves a maroon diagonal corridor, and a full contact turns the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/26/code.py:107:# - The trail rule assumes intermediate corridor cells are free of unrelated objects; the packed local\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/13/code.py:58:#     - Every placed input pixel must stay in-bounds and avoid the legend scan corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/27/code.py:46:#    - Reverse reconstruction needs more than `steps` extra room on the trailing side:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/27/code.py:632:    room_h = 26 - base_h\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/27/code.py:633:    room_w = 26 - base_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/27/code.py:634:    if room_h < min_extra_h or room_w < min_extra_w:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/27/code.py:637:    extra_h = random.randint(min_extra_h, min(8, room_h))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/27/code.py:638:    extra_w = random.randint(min_extra_w, min(8, room_w))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/23/code.py:83:#    decomposable and prevents the maze from turning into an unreadable thicket.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/35/code.py:9:#     a 4-color checkerboard would leave too little room for readable sprites, markers, and borders.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/23/code.py:55:#      generator still reserves the scan corridor at and left of the legend column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/23/code.py:454:    \"\"\"Protect the lower-left legend scan corridor.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/24/code.py:17:  2. `D7/2`: static obstacle blocks (color 8) sit in the corridor and stop a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/24/code.py:26:  second. Its input corridor is clear, but after A has moved, B's next step\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/24/code.py:57:- Input objects are separated by background; B's input corridor is clear, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/24/code.py:58:  the A obstacle is placed only in A's corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/24/code.py:102:  generator keeps each mover's corridor isolated so no second valid mate exists.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/22/code.py:50:#    corridor, and non-overlapping at the pixel level. Every non-block legend\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/11/code.py:25:  are left empty as bg corridors. Those corridors are separated from neighboring slots by 1-2\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/11/code.py:27:  lattice, so both the seams and the empty corridors stay visible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/11/code.py:45:The extra empty corridors are the minimum structure that makes D14 visible without adding too many\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/11/code.py:68:  visible frames occupy all non-corridor rows x cols slot intersections, so they never overlap\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/11/code.py:70:  sprites occupy distinct corridor slots and are centered with a 1-pixel bg moat inside each slot\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/11/code.py:72:  the lattice is embedded with only a small outer margin, so the internal corridors stay salient\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/11/code.py:77:Humans can see one rectangular frame arrangement plus one or more bg corridors threading through\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/11/code.py:79:output keeps the same lattice shape, but the small squares disappear from the corridors and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/11/code.py:97:  sprites are centered in frame-sized corridor slots with a 1-pixel inset:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/11/code.py:180:    - Smaller square sprites are centered inside those empty corridor slots, so they lie inside the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D3/0/code.py:45:#    - The generator reserves the entire ray corridor, including skipped slots, so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/26/code.py:24:#      the rightmost funnel fills first and occupies a wide corridor near the right edge;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/26/code.py:57:#      and placed fully in-bounds with enough room toward the opening edge for radiation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D9/1/code.py:29:#     - If neither side corridor is open, only the prefix A ... P is drawn.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D9/1/code.py:38:#       route becomes (4,2)->(4,4)->(3,4)->(3,8)->(4,8) if that corridor is clear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D9/1/code.py:39:#       If both upward and downward corridors are blocked, keep only (4,2)->(4,4).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D9/1/code.py:48:#       which keeps routing readable and avoids maze-like ambiguity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D9/1/code.py:72:#     - They sit inside a potential line corridor, so the detour is locally legible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/31/code.py:61:#    after the same fill/radiate action. The radiating corridor always continues through the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D2/1/code.py:27:#    send the beam back along the same corridor. Example: a north-going beam that hits a right-bar\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D2/1/code.py:53:#    beam, so the painted output remains legible instead of turning into a dense maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D2/1/code.py:329:        room = axis - sz - OBS_BOTH_GAP\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D2/1/code.py:330:        if room < 2 * lo:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D2/1/code.py:332:        a = random.randint(lo, min(hi_cap, room - lo))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D2/1/code.py:333:        b = _rand_thickness(lo, min(hi_cap, room - a))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/1/code.py:19:#      cel