rior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/38/code.py:79:  merging with the open corridor;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/38/code.py:109:    generator always adds a 1-2 cell border gap plus inward corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/38/code.py:404:    - Each frame has its own color, a 1-2 pixel border opening on one side, and possibly a thin bg corridor entering from that opening. Smaller square sprites of size `frame_size - 2` sit elsewhere and may contain bg hole components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/38/code.py:408:    - For each frame, count only non-frame-color components that are fully enclosed inside the full square patch; the border opening and any boundary-connected corridor do not count as holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/40/code.py:73:#   - after that turn, both outgoing corridors remain background for at least 2 cells;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D3/3/code.py:346:        room = axis - sz - OBS_BOTH_GAP\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D3/3/code.py:347:        if room < 2 * lo:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D3/3/code.py:349:        a = random.randint(lo, min(hi_cap, room - lo))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D3/3/code.py:350:        b = _rand_thickness(lo, min(hi_cap, room - a))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/40/code.py:32:#       9x9 or 10x10 frames because the 8-connectivity effect needs enough interior room for separated 2x2 blocks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/2/code.py:24:#        corridor, B stops as soon as its next step would overlap A's moved box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/39/code.py:72:- A 30x30 canvas is used so there is always room for the scattered 6x6 sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/39/code.py:45:#   disjoint straight corridors and remove collision machinery entirely.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/