endpoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/25/code.py:84:#   later top routes truncate inside previously painted corridors. This gives\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/25/code.py:90:#   would clutter narrow wire corridors. Collisions happen on already-painted\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/30/code.py:21:#      among many grid-like patterns, but here it deterministically means 2 stacked rooms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/30/code.py:22:#    - Difference: room counting no longer needs wall reconstruction or overlap reasoning. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/30/code.py:27:#      3-5 frames with different room counts and varied widths/heights to preserve a nontrivial sort.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/30/code.py:28:#    - Equal room counts would become visually ambiguous because the original overlap-based tiebreak\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/30/code.py:38:#      We therefore sort by room count and use top-left reading order only as a deterministic fallback.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/30/code.py:128:def _room_count_for_color(grid: np.ndarray, color: int) -> tuple[int, tuple[int, int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/30/code.py:141:    rooms = len(full_rows) - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/30/code.py:142:    assert rooms == _count_enclosed_regions(mask)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/30/code.py:143:    return int(rooms), box\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/30/code.py:148:    Turn each intact horizontally partitioned frame into a left-aligned color bar whose length equals its room count.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/30/code.py:157:    - This count is the number of rooms, equivalently the number of full-width wall rows minus one.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/30/code.py:158:    - Sort fra