riginal corridor exit\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/26/code.py:26:#    - In the playfield, the blue network is not a single forced bend-only corridor. At each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/26/code.py:44:#    - The mover size is fixed to 3x3. That gives 1..8 visible symbol pixels, enough room to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/31/code.py:3:# Name: 直线射线+边缘停止+稀疏窄通道\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/31/code.py:30:  - green background, blue winding corridor, black n x n mover, red n x n destination,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/31/code.py:31:  - solve by BFS over all feasible n x n placements inside the blue corridor,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/31/code.py:44:  - Old corridor-following logic with edge-stop would BFS through the turn and could prefer the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/31/code.py:116:- To prove the fusion is not just \"edge-stop on any corridor\", every generated sample includes a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/4/code.py:25:   - horizontal travel cares about corridor height >= h\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/4/code.py:26:   - vertical travel cares about corridor width >= w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/4/code.py:32:- A single blue zig-zag corridor follows five segments:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/4/code.py:40:- Original task would use one scalar n and ask whether every corridor cross\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/4/code.py:96:- The corridor itself shows different horizontal-vs-vertical thickness.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/4/code.py:105:- Gates are cut from the same corridor instead of adding extra markers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/27/code.py:67:- The generator paints a rectangular base corridor and then adds side pockets for each gate.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/27/code.py:84:- The main corridor stays horizontal before the final global symmetry transform; pockets alternate\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/27/code.py:407:    corridor_start = x_shift + 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/27/code.py:408:    grid[base_r : base_r + n, corridor_start:G] = _RIVER\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/27/code.py:411:        x0 = corridor_start + idx * chamber_len\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/27/code.py:414:    mover_r, mover_c = base_r, corridor_start\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D13/2/code.py:270:def _orth_room(edge: str, line: int, H: int, W: int) -> int:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D13/2/code.py:281:    return sorted(lines, key=lambda line: _orth_room(edge, line, H, W))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D13/2/code.py:295:    room = _orth_room(edge, line, H, W)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D13/2/code.py:296:    max_step = min(_STEP_RANGE[1], room, (line_len - 2) // 2)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/5/code.py:79:#    - The scene is a sparse orthogonal fork rather than a dense maze. Pockets are only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6ffbe589/D7/1/code.py:31:#   exactly two long cue corridors on the opposite sides, enough for up to three cues without overlap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6ffbe589/D7/1/code.py:33:#   Side-specific corridors avoid diagonal placements and keep cues visually separate from the board.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6ffbe589/D7/1/code.py:413:    \"\"\"Pick a corner anchor and return the two side corridors available for cues.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/8/code.py:19:   - Original: a solid black n×n square slides through blue n-wide corridor windows toward a solid red n×n square.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/8/code.py:22:     the same rotated L shape, and the frame opens toward the corridor only along the side where that L touches the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/8/code.py:37:     template. The same orientation is reused consistently by mover, corridor sweep, and docking cavity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/8/code.py:58:   - The blue corridor is rendered as the union of translated copies of the same L shape, so every intended anchor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/8/code.py:60:   - The docking frame is painted only after the corridor exists, and only if its whole (n+2)×(n+2) patch contains\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/8/code.py:68:     2. the corridor width matters relative to that exact L silhouette;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/8/code.py:87:     Because the corridor and dock cavity are L-specific, many samples should yield a different reachable target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/7/code.py:47:#    - Structures are spaced with padding, and distractors stay off the ray corridors, so the black\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/28/code.py:26:#      parts of the corridor visibly wider without changing the canonical spiral order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/28/code.py:43:#    - The visible change is strong: the river is a regular spiral, not a random corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/28/code.py:47:#      make the corridor look non-uniform without creating clutter or secondary objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/24/code.py:18:   the pipe is no longer a single corridor. It is a small network with a branch and a loop,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/34/code.py:444:    corridor_colors = {_WIDE, _NARROW}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/34/code.py:451:            elif all(grid[r, c] in corridor_colors | {_BG} for r in range(pr) for c in range(pc, pc + n) if c < W):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/34/code.py:458:                grid[r, c] in corridor_colors | {_BG}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/34/code.py:468:            elif all(grid[r, c] in corridor_colors | {_BG} for r in range(pr, pr + n) for c in range(pc) if r < H):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/34/code.py:475:                grid[r, c] in corridor_colors | {_BG}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:23:     stays inside the blue corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:42:       leading into a bottom-left L cavity. The mover can only dock if both the corridor is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D5/0/code.py:142:    - The final destination is controlled by visible waterline markers, not by purely local geometric stability. Extra water can bypass empty headroom in an earlier basin and appear in a later basin.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D5/0/code.py:229:        assert min_line <= max_line, \"need at least one row of empty headroom above the marked water\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D5/0/code.py:287:        assert any(int(b[\"line\"]) > min(np.where(output_grid[:, int(b[\"left\"])] != BG)[0][0], np.where(output_grid[:, int(b[\"right\"])] != BG)[0][0]) for b in basins), \"need visible headroom above at least one filled basin\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/36/code.py:11:#     river: still a single winding corridor, but now green instead of blue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/36/code.py:12:#     two_squares: same-sized solid n×n squares placed on the corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/36/code.py:39:#       while the corridor is always green on a blue field. The solver must infer both the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/36/code.py:67:#     no extra markers are added; the grid remains a clean blue field plus one green corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/36/code.py:71:#     The corridor/background inversion is inferable from large-area corners vs narrow strip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/10/code.py:14:#      keeps the source sprite, keeps the legend, and adds a blue corridor that visibly runs from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/10/code.py:32:#    - This guarantees non-overlap, in-bounds placement, and clear empty corridors where trails can be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/10/code.py:39:#    - There are no branching mazes or dense overlays. Each color gets a dedicated horizontal lane,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/10/code.py:48:#      outside the frame; the generator reserves that corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/1/code.py:9:#    - 融合后，蓝色不再代表“任意可拐弯通道”，而是若干对角线 n×n 放置状态的并集。黑块从起点沿唯一的\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/1/code.py:14:#    - 这与原题的差异是决定性地把“位置”改成了“位置 + 对角方向”，并把“通道自己允许拐弯”改成了“镜面显式触发反射”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D5/2/code.py:23:#   原题输入若在右上角直接画 10 个蓝点，它们会沿右侧通道落入两个相邻盆地；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/2/code.py:20:#     - 同一滑行通道上再放一个更近的错形红诱饵，肉眼能看到“最近的不一定会进入槽里”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/2/code.py:25:#     - 输出时，真匹配块按匹配后的朝向滑入槽内；原始位置和中间通道都变黑；近处错形块与所有其他红块一起被擦除。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/2/code.py:38:#     - 真红块和诱饵都只放在槽口外的背景通道中，不进入结构实体，也不会越界。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/2/code.py:44:#     - 结构之间通常保留 2-3 格缓冲，单个补丁的黑轨迹和红块都局限在一个窄通道内，避免多层覆盖导致难以阅读。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D7/1/code.py:38:#    that leave room for a blank beat between the inner marker and companion,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/3/code.py:16:- the input river is no longer a single corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/3/code.py:45:  enough to express the fusion without turning the grid into a maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/3/code.py:60:- The original code assumed a single corridor, so it never had to reason about multiple routes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/3/code.py:75:- A human sees a branched blue river in the input and a single surviving blue corridor in the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D9/1/code.py:17:#      basin group into two enclosed vertical chambers linked by a one-row-low connector corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D5/0/code.py:46:#     - The full launch corridor to the edge is still reserved in `occ_path`, including future blank\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D5/0/code.py:48:#     - Output paints only the odd-indexed cells of that corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D5/0/code.py:54:#     - No other object is allowed on the launch corridor, including skipped cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D5/0/code.py:60:#     - main() now assumes that if a cup is intended to demonstrate the variant, the corridor has enough\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D5/0/code.py:62:#     - generate_input() guarantees this by requiring at least two odd-offset corridor cells per cup.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D5/0/code.py:330:    and the intermittent ejection corridor is clear.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/22/code.py:32:#     clearly, while leaving enough room for a multi-turn river on a 12-20 grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/22/code.py:45:#     reachable\". That is invalid here because even with a fully wide corridor the mover may stop\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/22/code.py:66:#   - Because the corridor stays fully wide and the destination is reachable, a failure to reach red\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/4/code.py:31:#    - Distinct placeholder colors are limited to 2-4, which leaves room for repeated evidence inside the frame\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/11/code.py:3:# Name: 多目标选择+分支通道\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/11/code.py:11:     corridor. The solver picks the only destination and BFS runs on legal n x n placements.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/11/code.py:12:   - This combo keeps the same slide mechanics, but the blue corridor now visibly branches. There\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/11/code.py:28:     enough to make the branch choice visually obvious without turning the river into a maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/11/code.py:52:     every intended corridor position is guaranteed to be a legal placement before optional choking.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/41/code.py:111:  - black and red are same-sized squares aligned on one straight corridor,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/37/code.py:17:   - The original task painted a blue winding corridor and solved motion by BFS over all feasible n×n placements.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/37/code.py:333:                # Leave enough room for the rest of the path after the forced bounce.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/25/code.py:53:#    - Each quadrant bbox must exist and have room for at least a 3-cell connected piece.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/6/code.py:43:    - 输入放置逻辑沿用原题 output-first：先造蓝色通道，再放 mover / dest。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/6/code.py:45:    - generator 在放置后重算 feasible placement，并要求 solver 输出与内部 oracle 一致，防止重叠、越界或非法通道宽度漏网。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/6/code.py:48:      - 黑色不再“瞬移”，而是沿通道连续留下轨迹。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/6/code.py:50:    - 规则依赖几何可见条件“能否穿过宽度 >= n 的通道”，不依赖颜色编号排序。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/21/code.py:46:# - 结构之间仍保持 padding；distractor 仍禁止落在任何 socket 向外的清晰视线通道上，因此不会误变成 matched。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/21/code.py:62:# - 规则完全由可见几何关系驱动：是否处在某个结构开口的视线通道上，决定它是“滑入”还是“原地保留”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/30/code.py:88:  generator keeps a single winding corridor and a single valid chokepoint so that interpretation is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/42/code.py:22:    - one blue winding corridor on a square grid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/42/code.py:27:    - a five-stage snake corridor whose horizontal stages and vertical stages have\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/42/code.py:52:      visible gate levels exist in one corridor and that only a later gate blocks the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/42/code.py:65:  - The corridor always has exactly five stages and four turns. That is enough to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/42/code.py:66:    show multi-level gating without producing visually chaotic mazes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/42/code.py:89:  - Every painted corridor rectangle is clipped by construction to stay in-bounds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/42/code.py:213:    Slide a solid rectangle through a multi-gate winding corridor on a non-square grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/19/code.py:70:#   distance or by \"first thing on the corridor\". A human can see one sprite being ignored\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/19/code.py:76:# - Structures remain separated, and each ray corridor carries at most one true sprite and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/19/code.py:96:#   original straight-corridor slide model under rotation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/35/code.py:3:# Name: 多体顺序移动+环形通道+一对多目标\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/35/code.py:8:#    原题只有一个 mover 和一个目标，蓝色通道也是单链，所以“走到目标”与“沿唯一通道一直前进”几乎是同一件事。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/35/code.py:13:#    - 蓝色通道是一个矩形环，mover 从左侧支路进入，3 个目标挂在环的其它支路上。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:7:#    - Keep the original scene grammar: green background, one winding corridor, one black n×n mover,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:9:#    - The corridor now uses two blues:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:16:#      - Original task on a physically wide 2×2 corridor with no erased chokepoint: the black square\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:25:#    - Only one extra input degree of freedom is added: corridor color state {dark blue, light blue}.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:30:#    - Original `river = most common remaining color` is no longer valid because the corridor may use two\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:31:#      colors. The fused solver uses explicit corridor semantics instead of a single inferred river color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:33:#      traversable anymore; traversability depends on mover size and corridor shade.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:40:#    - The generator first paints a fully wide, physically valid corridor, then recolors a downstream\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:42:#    - Mover and destination are placed on pre-cleared corridor blocks, same size, non-overlapping.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:53:#    - No overlays or extra symbols are stacked on top of the corridor; the clue is encoded directly in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:54:#      corridor color, so the moved object and the channel remain easy to parse.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:326:    corridor_colors = {_WIDE, _NARROW}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:334:            if all(grid[r, c] in corridor_colors | {_BG} for r in range(pr) for c in range(pc, pc + n) if c < W):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:342:                grid[r, c] in corridor_colors | {_BG}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:353:            if all(grid[r, c] in corridor_colors | {_BG} for r in range(pr, pr + n) for c in range(pc) if r < H):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:361:                grid[r, c] in corridor_colors | {_BG}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/0/code.py:70:#     overlapping layers are avoided: guide, source, travel corridor, and basin walls occupy disjoint cells in input\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/32/code.py:37:  the generator still creates a long winding blue corridor with multiple turns,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/32/code.py:82:- The river is one clean connected corridor; black and red just mark its ends.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/5/code.py:26:#   则是该 2x4 红块移动到结构外侧贴边位置，原位置变回背景，6 格通道保持纯背景，其他干扰红块不动。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/5/code.py:57:#   推理通道里。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/5/code.py:58:# - 没有黑拖尾后，输出更干净；为了防止“终点和原地红块混成一团”，front-ray 约束禁止在终点通道上放置\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/12/code.py:11:#   repaints it either on the opposite edge when the corridor stays at least n wide,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/12/code.py:25:#   boundary exit, a winding corridor, and optional chokepoints. The generator keeps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/12/code.py:41:#   The generator first paints an internal winding corridor, then extends its first\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D8/0/code.py:36:#   使远杯保留 1-3 格后被阻挡。若有第三个杯，则只放在清空通道里，不参与冲突。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:3:# Change: gravity + flow——水像素优先垂直下落，被阻挡时通过唯一开放侧的对角线滑动，支撑后沿水平方向滑向最近可落点... → 通道跟随式流动\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:17:#    - This variant replaces that open-space physics with a pipe-like corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:24:#      Variant: if a 2x2 water plug starts at the end of a corridor that first goes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:30:#      corridors rather than open cups. Solver logic changes from iterative local\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:39:#    - The placement graph is restricted to a single non-branching corridor component\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:44:#      plug reaches the corridor end.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:52:#      a global corridor view and a fixed 2x2 footprint check.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:57:#      in a corridor. The new output check instead preserves \"solid 2x2 plug placed on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:58:#      a legal corridor position.\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:62:#      corridor cells. This avoids accidental open-space motion.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:79:#    - There is only one moving object, one corridor, and 2-3 broad wall color zones.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:85:#      0 is always the corridor interior, and all other colors are equivalent walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:153:def _follow_corridor(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:161:        assert len(comp) >= 2, \"corridor must allow visible movement\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:162:        assert all(d <= 2 for d in deg.values()), \"reachable legal placements must form a simple corridor\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:163:        assert deg[start] == 1, \"source water must start at a corridor endpoint\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:173:        assert len(forward) == 1, f\"ambiguous corridor branch: {forward}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:179:        assert len(path) == len(comp), \"corridor component must be a single non-branching path\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:190:    assert bool(feasible[start]), \"source plug must occupy a legal corridor placement\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:191:    path = _follow_corridor(feasible, start, check_input=check_input)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:207:    Move a compact water plug through a wall-bounded corridor until the corridor ends or narrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:212:    - The source plug starts at one endpoint of the reachable corridor. Downstream sections may bend and may later narrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:216:    - A move is legal only if the full 2x2 footprint fits inside corridor cells (bg or current water).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:217:    - Starting from the source placement, follow the unique sequence of legal 4-neighbor placements along the corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:218:    - Relocate the plug to the last reachable placement before the corridor terminates or becomes too narrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:220:    Key insight: Motion is governed by corridor topology and width, not gravity; the plug can follow turns, but a 1-cell chokepoint blocks it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:235:        assert bool(feasible_out[rr, cc]), \"output plug must stay inside the corridor\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:291:def _carve_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, path: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:342:        _carve_corridor(grid, path)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:385:    raise RuntimeError(\"failed to generate a valid corridor sample\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/17/code.py:28:  - Stuck case: a later corridor segment is narrowed below n, so BFS stops at\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/17/code.py:85:    corridor geometry, not movement semantics.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/17/code.py:124:- Input contains one dominant coherent blue structure, not a noisy maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/13/code.py:58:#    the same corridor and keeps the contrast between target, decoy, structure, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/800d221b/D7/1/code.py:3:# Change: hub固定为3x3实心方块... → hub为十字形\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/800d221b/D7/1/code.py:6:# - The visible difference is the core behavior change from \"hub固定为3x3实心方块\" to \"hub为十字形\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/800d221b/D7/1/code.py:8:# - Variant detail: hub不是方块，而是十字形（+形）结构。改变了hub的视觉特征和边界像素分布，分支的连接方式也相应变化。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/3/code.py:45:- 解题者能直接看到：输入里蓝色块贴在边缘导流仓内；输出里蓝色优先铺开在离出口最近的上层通道和盆口，而不是全部沉到最底部。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/15/code.py:30:     corridor becomes pure blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D10/2/code.py:18:#      horizontal corridor with exactly one bottom opening above the target basin.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:24:#    four square rooms arranged as a 2x2 checkerboard. Each room is monochrome, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:25:#    each room color arrives in the input as multiple disconnected fragments that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:28:#      - fused task: the same red shards are split as a room-specific template,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:33:#    family instead of degenerating into a crop. Four rooms are enough to make the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:41:#      mirrored same-color rooms would become disconnected copies. The combo solver\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:48:#      later merge into a room cluster.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:54:#    input canvas, all room fragments are scattered outside it with Chebyshev padding\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:60:#    the output always turns those shards into four solid room-filling squares in a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:65:#    The scene has only two layers: one anchored scaffold and four scattered room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:71:#    is determined only by visible fragment structure: each room color has a stable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:73:#    room the color must fill.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:127:_ROOM_KEYS = {room: _template_key(parts) for room, parts in _ROOM_TEMPLATE_COORDS.items()}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:128:_KEY_TO_ROOM = {key: room for room, key in _ROOM_KEYS.items()}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:156:def _room_key_from_color(g: np.ndarray, color: int) -> tuple[tuple[int, int, tuple[tuple[int, int], ...]], ...]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:158:    assert len(comps) >= 2, \"each room color must arrive as multiple fragments\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:165:    four-room checkerboard.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:172:      that scaffold, with one fragment-template family per checkerboard room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:175:    - Normalize the scaffold to the output frame and recover the four 2x2 rooms that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:178:    - Place that color into the unique room whose template matches those fragments,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:179:      filling the entire room so the scattered shards become one 4-connected cluster.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:182:    - The checkerboard is expressed by the scaffold's four room positions, while the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:184:      to stay apart anymore. The fragment-template family tells you which room each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:185:      color belongs to, and once a room is identified its final 2x2 cluster is forced.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:194:    room_colors = sorted(set(map(int, np.unique(g))) - {bg, frame_color})\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:195:    assert len(room_colors) == 4, \"expected exactly four non-frame room colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:198:    seen_rooms: set[str] = set()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:199:    for col in room_colors:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:200:        room_key = _room_key_from_color(g, int(col))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:201:        assert room_key in _KEY_TO_ROOM, \"encountered unknown room fragment template\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:202:        room = _KEY_TO_ROOM[room_key]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:203:        assert room not in seen_rooms, \"each room template must be used by exactly one color\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:204:        rs, cs = _ROOM_SLICES[room]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:206:        seen_rooms.add(room)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:208:    assert seen_rooms == set(_ROOM_SLICES), \"all four checkerboard rooms must be assigned\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:209:    for col in room_colors:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/25/code.py:210:     