ew/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/2/code.py:232:    _paint_rect(grid, 7, 6, 3, 4, wall_right, corridor)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/2/code.py:233:    _paint_rect(grid, 8, 4, 2, 3, wall_right, corridor)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/2/code.py:236:    for r, c in sorted(corridor):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/2/code.py:239:        if c + 1 < 10 and (r, c + 1) not in corridor and grid[r, c + 1] == BG and random.random() < 0.18:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/2/code.py:241:        if c - 1 >= 0 and (r, c - 1) not in corridor and grid[r, c - 1] == BG and random.random() < 0.18:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/2/code.py:248:    corridor, source_cells = _build_corridor()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/2/code.py:249:    base = _decorate_solids(corridor, wall_colors[0], wall_colors[1])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/2/code.py:286:    - Solid wall colors never move; only the blue packet is translated along the corridor topology.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/2/code.py:326:    raise RuntimeError(\"failed to generate a valid corridor-following instance\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/38/code.py:18:#    - Input keeps the original river mechanics: a blue winding corridor on green background and one black n x n mover.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/38/code.py:23:#    - The selected color appears on 2-3 same-sized target squares placed in order along the main corridor. Those are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/38/code.py:27:#      corridor, a yellow distractor on a side spur near D. If F is reachable, the output paints every placement from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/38/code.py:29:#      between C and F, the trail runs from A through C and stops at the farthest main-corridor placement before the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/38/code.py:37:#    - The branch structure is limited to short side spurs so the main corridor still visually dominates and the visit\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/38/code.py:53:#    - Selected targets lie on the main corridor in increasing corridor order; distractors are placed only on branch tips\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/38/code.py:57:#    - Chokepoints are inserted only on the main corridor after at least one selected target and before at least one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/38/code.py:61:#      bar, that same color appears on multiple main-corridor targets, and the output black trail consumes exactly that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/38/code.py:62:#      color's corridor prefix while leaving wrong-color branch targets untouched.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/38/code.py:65:#    - The main corridor remains a single winding ribbon; side branches are short and sparse.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/38/code.py:75:# - Selected-color targets are laid out along one main corridor so that the farthest reachable placement from the start\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/26/code.py:28:#   enterable, so a distractor whose green side lies on the natural corridor can\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D1/1/code.py:18:#       central corridor. This keeps the change localized to path simulation, but makes the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D1/1/code.py:145:      cup's mouth corridor. Stop only after every content pixel has been placed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/6/code.py:44:#    corridor. Distractors are placed only on background cells, outside structure bboxes,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/40/code.py:3:# Name: 渐变色轨迹+裁剪通道内部\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:3:# Name: 十字形色块+单轴对称+隐式端口\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D3/0/code.py:210:    - If blocked below, it may slide diagonally down through the unique open side corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D1/2/code.py:77:#     - Stray pixels are kept away from all cup bboxes and from full gravity corridors so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D1/2/code.py:420:    \"\"\"Optionally add an isolated stray pixel, away from all cup regions and gravity corridors.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/12/code.py:46:#    only exact-shape rectangles on the opening side with a clear corridor, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/12/code.py:51:#    corridor from the slot to the decoy. Other distractors avoid structure bboxes,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/12/code.py:71:#      shape, and each valid mover has an all-background corridor to its slot.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/12/code.py:231:        corridor = grid[tr1 + 1:rr0, tc0:tc1 + 1]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/12/code.py:235:        corridor = grid[rr1 + 1:tr0, tc0:tc1 + 1]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/12/code.py:239:        corridor = grid[tr0:tr1 + 1, tc1 + 1:rc0]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/12/code.py:243:        corridor = grid[tr0:tr1 + 1, rc1 + 1:tc0]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/12/code.py:245:    if corridor.size and np.any(corridor != bg):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/12/code.py:383:    - A red component docks only if it is a solid rectangle of that exact shape, sits on the opening side with the same cross-axis span, and has a clear background corridor to the slot.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/20/code.py:3:# Name: 非正方形网格+密集宽通道\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/20/code.py:42:     carve a dense wide corridor system out of it. The motion rule itself stays\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/7/code.py:51:#    room for the 4-cell tall legend on the left edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:24:#     - The corridor is no longer interpreted as an undirected pipe. We reason on the placement\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:42:#       language is clearly \"gravity cave\", not a slightly modified winding corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:410:    room_left = int(tail_c)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:411:    room_right = int(w - (tail_c + n))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:412:    for side, room in [(-1, room_left), (1, room_right)]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:413:        if room < 1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:415:        max_extra = min(int(room), max(1, min(3, n + 1)))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D12/2/code.py:24:#     - 差异：原题只移动水；本变体先改结构，再让原有流体规则利用新通道继续流动。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:3:# Name: 路径像素数距离+迷宫式墙壁\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:29:      3 + 3 = 6；另一枚更远的 maroon 在较宽主通道深处，沿路 5 格每格只贴 1 面墙，总代价只有 5。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:35:    - 迷宫保留单一目标块、单一墙色、单一 token 色；复杂度来自通道几何而不是对象种类膨胀。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:36:    - generator 强制同时出现较宽主通道和狭窄支路，并筛掉“新旧前 k 个来源集合完全相同”的样本，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:41:      保证 reachable 区里确实有不同宽度、不同贴墙程度的通道。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:42:    - 原 main() 只需要至少一个入口；融合后若把所有可达通道都做成等宽直廊，新规则会退化。生成器\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:43:      因此显式做“主通道加宽 + 支路保持狭窄 + 近处死胡同”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:48:    - 迷宫从单个入口接到外部主通道，支路和加宽单元都只在非目标区域内生成，不越界、不覆盖目标块。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:49:    - distractor 只放在与主迷宫 4 不连通的孤立 floor 口袋里，因此不会被误判为可达来源。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:52:      较宽或半开阔的主通道里。输出若优先搬走后者，说明排序标准不是普通 BFS。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:53:    - 由于目标块仍按 row-major 填入，观察者只需比较“哪些 maroon 消失了”，就能对照迷宫几何推断\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:57:    - 迷宫是单层平面结构，没有叠加标记；加宽只表现为局部 corridor 变宽，不会让对象边界混乱。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:61:      作为墙，并构造让这种“贴墙程度”可肉眼比较的通道。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:64:      generator 在采样时显式检查这一点，不满足就重造迷宫。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:121:    assert starts, \"maze must expose at least one passable entry beside the destination\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:144:    assert starts, \"maze must expose at least one passable entry beside the destination\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:427:    - Orange cells are walkable floor, magenta cells are maze walls, and maroon cells sit on floor cells inside the maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:435:    Key insight: In the maze, the winning maroons are not always the fewest steps away; wider passages can beat shorter but tighter dead ends because distance is driven by repeated contact with nearby walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:450:    assert starts, \"destination block must have at least one passable maze entry\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/11/code.py:32:#   long enough corridors to expose the alternating gaps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/11/code.py:40:#   corridor separately from the painted subset. Distractors and later blobs are banned\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/16/code.py:3:# Name: 紧凑裁剪+稀疏窄通道\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/16/code.py:19:      原题输入是整张方形背景图，蓝色通道占比较大，黑色 n×n 方块沿可容纳整个 n×n\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/16/code.py:24:      1. 输入端：通道改成稀疏细线式结构，整张输入里只有 10%-20% 的非背景像素，绝大多数\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/16/code.py:26:      2. 输出端：先按原滑动规则得到整张结果，再把结果裁成“包含整条通道区域的最小矩形”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/16/code.py:32:      与原题相比，解题者现在要同时看出“黑块在窄通道里的移动/受阻规则”和“输出把整条\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/16/code.py:33:      通道外的背景边框全部裁掉”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/16/code.py:36:      - 如果只做裁剪，不约束通道稀疏度，输入和输出差异会弱化成“去掉一点边框”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/16/code.py:38:      - 因此生成器同时强制：输入稀疏、输出必然变小、且通道仍要有 >=3 次转折，避免退化成\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/16/code.py:49:      - BFS 仍然在 n×n 顶点放置网格上进行；D14/0 没有改变物理规则，只是把大部分通道做成\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/16/code.py:64:      3. 输出只保留通道所在的紧凑矩形，而不是原始大画布。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/16/code.py:69:      - 路径被限制为非自接触折线，避免生成大块蓝团导致“哪里是通道、哪里是宽水面”不清。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/39/code.py:59:#   have room before reaching the sprite and never need clipping.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/17/code.py:32:#     The ray stops after three cells even though the depth budget still has room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/17/code.py:71:#   corridors, so distractors do not land on meaningful travel lines.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/17/code.py:86:#   corridor, so they read as separate blobs rather than ambiguous branch points.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c3d4a41/D1/2/code.py:16:#      Here, each input color column is reassigned to the tooth whose remaining headroom matches\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c3d4a41/D1/2/code.py:35:#      output projection column\". That is no longer true and is replaced by a count/headroom bijection.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c3d4a41/D1/2/code.py:52:#      unique tooth headrooms. The generator enforces this by sampling a permutation of [1,2,3,4] for\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c3d4a41/D1/2/code.py:79:    - Do not preserve input colors by absolute column. Instead, match each input color column to the bar projection whose available headroom above the tooth equals that column's colored height.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c3d4a41/D1/2/code.py:165:        headroom = bar_top - interior_top\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c3d4a41/D1/2/code.py:166:        space_to_dst.setdefault(int(headroom), []).append(dst_col)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/15/code.py:37:#    cross older rays, or put stray blue cells in a ray corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:7:#   A canonical corridor sits beside the 3x3 destination block. The first maroon is within\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:293:    - Magenta walls form narrow corridors near the destination.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:294:    - Maroon pixels sit on floor cells outside the block; some are near the opening, others are deeper in the corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/10/code.py:54:#      room to host all legal offset ticks exactly.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:26:#         hall token -> opens right gate -> right-room token -> opens lower gate -> lower-room tokens.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:27:#      This guarantees a visible collect -> wall disappears -> new room opens -> continue pattern.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:46:#    - Dynamic rooms are separated by full wall segments touching the border or other barriers, so the newly opened\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:123:        room_left = DEST_LIMIT - len(collected)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:124:        layer = layer[:room_left]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:180:    - Some maroons sit in rooms that are initially sealed by magenta barriers, while earlier reachable maroons sit next\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:233:    - Trigger T1 opens the right room by crumbling a vertical gate.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:234:    - Trigger T2 in the right room opens the lower room by crumbling a horizontal gate.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:247:    # Keep the lower room open internally.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:252:    # Hall / room floors remain orange by default. Mark fixed and optional maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/21/code.py:55:#    (root / side pair / top pair), so rays mostly occupy separate corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:253:      the move order is no longer “shortest corridor first” or “row-major fill”. The whole transformation is driven by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/19/code.py:47:#      corridors. One child is intentionally suppressed by the DFS step schedule,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/19/code.py:70:#    - The suppressed child is also required to have clear vertical corridors, so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/8/code.py:35:#      valid because markers sit on the ray corridor and orthogonal rays must cross. The solver therefore\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:64:      - with centers at (1,1) and (9,9), a maroon near the upper-left corridor belongs only to the first block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:65:      - a maroon near the lower-right corridor belongs only to the second block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c3d4a41/D4/0/code.py:26:      - If a column has more colored cells than the room below the base, only the visible prefix survives.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c3d4a41/D4/0/code.py:38:        - Bar is anchored high enough to leave room under the base.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/24/code.py:242:                assert int(g[r, c]) == bg, \"fixed-length corridor must be empty in valid inputs\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/24/code.py:517:        corridor_union: set[tuple[int, int]] = set()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/24/code.py:520:            overlap = corridor_union & info[\"all_cells\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/24/code.py:524:            corridor_union |= info[\"all_cells\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/28/code.py:63:#   blob may lie later on the same already-drawn fixed-distance corridor, because\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/28/code.py:65:#   The generator enforces one relevant blob per corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/28/code.py:69:#   active chain hop is guaranteed to lie on the exact corridor the solver will\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/28/code.py:74:#   emission corridor, but they do not draw that corridor in the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/28/code.py:87:# - Ray corridors are short and object spacing is still controlled by the padded\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/28/code.py:96:#   * every intended ray has enough in-bounds room for its full step budget;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/28/code.py:476:    corridor_set = set(full_path) if not include_origin else set()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/28/code.py:506:                tight_blue = corridor_set.intersection(blue) if (steps_limit == 2 and not include_origin) else set()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c3d4a41/D4/1/code.py:36:#    has enough room for the intended pairwise fill.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:40:#   copies, reachable corridors keep their maroons, and blocked regions become clean floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:42:#   Across a few examples, a solver can see a stable contrast: maroons connected to a corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:146:    - The output separates maroons by connectivity, not by raw proximity: corridor-connected maroons survive and also appear inside the block, while wall-isolated maroons disappear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/13/code.py:742:    \"\"\"Bias 3-start samples toward roomier grids so that branch coverage is observable.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D6/2/code.py:17:#   along that ray's outward direction. The output fills the corridor from the gap\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D6/2/code.py:39:#   redirect. In this variant the generator guarantees pairwise disjoint corridors,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D6/2/code.py:176:    - The ray paints the gap and every background cell along that straight corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D1/1/code.py:59:#     - The solver may stop a beam on self-reentry; generation therefore uses roomy layouts that usually\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:8:#    - 原题会把 `floor+maroon` 都当作 BFS 通道，所以一条走廊里的整串栗色会一次性全部变成候选，再按距离从近到远选前 k 个。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:16:#    - 原 solver 的 `passable={floor,9}` 在本题已失效；现在栗色必须从通道集合里移除，否则不会产生“前一个栗色挡住后一个”的现象。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:248:    - A unique red cell marks the middle of a green 3x3 destination block, while maroon pixels sit on narrow floor corridors or in isolated pockets outside it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:3:# Name: 墙壁有通道口+规则矩形框架\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:17:#    three aligned floor strips on one side: inner-frame gap, 1-cell corridor between frames, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:39:#    The nested rectangles keep object roles separated: center target, inner frame, corridor strip, outer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/15/code.py:66:      Sprites are placed with padding between rectangles, enough room on both\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/15/code.py:67:      long sides for emitted rays, and enough room on both short sides for 2-4\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/15/code.py:70:      Markers are isolated single pixels on bg-only short-edge corridors. A\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/37/code.py:52:#      the source chamber, orange floor as corridors, and only two token colors at once.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/37/code.py:62:#      matching reachable tokens. The fixed corridor layout guarantees both.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/37/code.py:203:    - Magenta walls leave corridor openings from each destination into the shared chamber.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/20/code.py:42:#     and column are drawn first and occupy their full free corridors. Color 6 then\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/20/code.py:75:#     marker host corridors clear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/20/code.py:86:#     earlier colors relative to the empty-grid corridors. It must be positive.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/14/code.py:55:#      the full approach corridor is clear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/14/code.py:84:#      split state is idempotent; generator preserves clear corridors so repeated hits\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/0/code.py:15:      - 原题是横向条带布局: 偶数行是彩色横条, 奇数行是背景通道.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/0/code.py:20:      - 顶/底起点只放在真正通向边缘的竖直走廊端点; 右侧起点只放在无转弯的直通道右端, 避免逆向进入时无解.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/0/code.py:28:    - 仍保留 straight/L/U 三种通道类型与 fake corridor, 避免任务退化成纯直线搬运.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/0/code.py:32:    - 原先的“入口检查”假设真实入口在左侧, 所以需要检查条带起点是否在 col <= 3; 变体下不能继续把这个约束绑死在左边, 改为沿粒子朝内方向寻找首个可达 corridor cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/0/code.py:51:    - solver 假设每个边界粒子沿朝内射线都能到达至少一个 passable corridor cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/0/code.py:54:      generator 每条路径最多一个起点, 且转弯列/通道行互异.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/0/code.py:68:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/0/code.py:99:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/0/code.py:108:def _ray_has_corridor_entry(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/0/code.py:109:    \"\"\"Check that an edge particle can actually enter a real corridor when moving inward.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/0/code.py:118:        if _has_corridor(grid, rr, cc, direction):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/0/code.py:137:    valid = [d for d in candidates if _ray_has_corridor_entry(grid, r, c, d)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/0/code.py:197:    \"\"\"Move magenta edge particles along same-color corridors; initial direction is inward from the edge.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/0/code.py:244:    \"\"\"Reserve a 3-column window for a vertical corridor and return the wall column.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/2/code.py:34:#    - Every accepted sample enforces a minimum visible corridor length before the first blocker, so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/2/code.py:45:#      explicitly verify all labeled diagonal corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/2/code.py:50:#    - For every labeled port on every sprite, the diagonal corridor must stay inside bg for a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:62:#     - all semantic cues remain local to the fixed 3x3 target, keeping the wall/corridor scene readable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:172:    - Orange floor cells contain scattered maroon tokens, while magenta walls may block some corridors near the target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:300:    \"\"\"Build wall barrier around dest with corridor openings, extending outward.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c3d4a41/D13/0/code.py:22:#     - 2 to 4 extra grey distractor components are added in the entrance corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c3d4a41/D13/0/code.py:75:#   - distractors stay in a narrow corridor and remain isolated; they do not overlap\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c3d4a41/D13/0/code.py:140:    - The dominant structural color is grey, forming one large right-side frame, one left-side comb-shaped bar, and several tiny extra grey distractor blobs in the corridor between them.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/31/code.py:29:#      repetition for humans to notice the diagonal arrangement, while still leaving room for the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/31/code.py:51:#      `[2, h-3] x [2, w-3]`. This leaves room for the ±2 endpoint offsets while still allowing the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:21:#       因而 12 条射线长度高度不对称，输入看起来像“角落里的观察口”而不是居中的房间。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:27:#     - 融合后同一栗色虽然仍在同一房间内，但不在任何首阻挡直线视野上，所以保留在原位。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:37:#     - 原 solver 允许栗色充当 BFS 通道；在本题里栗色恰恰必须终止视线，否则会退化成“同一射线整串都可见”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:46:#     - 所有“可见源”都放在某条射线的室内地板段上；所有“BFS-only 诱饵”都放在同一房间内但避开全部射线格；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:49:#     - 人类可直接看到两个稳定线索：一是绿色块明显偏在框的一角，四侧空隙长短悬殊；二是有些栗色明明和目标块在同一房间里，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:244:    - The frame is asymmetric: the green block sits near one frame corner, so some outward directions are short and cramped while the opposite directions open into longer corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:252:    - Being in the same room is no longer enough. The magenta frame puts the block in a corner-biased viewing position, so many maroon pixels are flood-fill reachable but still ignored because no straight ray sees them first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:360:    room_cells = {\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:366:    bfs_only_candidates = [cell for cell in room_cells if cell not in lane_union and int(inp[cell]) == FLOOR_COLOR]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:370:    room_spare = TOTAL_MAROON_RANGE[1] - int((inp == MAROON).sum())\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:371:    bfs_only_count = random.randint(1, min(4, len(bfs_only_candidates), max(1, room_spare)))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:28:#       a real horizontal corridor. The particle is not on the grid edge. Its start\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:29:#       direction must be inferred from the local corridor shape: the cell itself is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:30:#       inside a same-color horizontal corridor, and one horizontal side is sealed by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:32:#       visible as the only open continuation of that corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:34:#     - the striped corridor/bar layout stays the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:37:#       corridor cell, plus a same-color blocker immediately behind it\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:39:#       same corridor logic after its internal launch point\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:42:#       1. particle at (5, 0) enters the row-5 corridor and moves right\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:46:#       2. recolor (5, 7) with the row-5 corridor color, sealing the left side\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:47:#       3. because (5, 8) is visibly inside a horizontal corridor and only its right\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:54:#       \"particle in corridor + one side blocked\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:56:#       same visible corridor color already flanking that row\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:60:#       inside the corridor rather than outside the left boundary\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:72:#     - from a few examples, a human can see that particles begin inside corridors,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:74:#     - the same corridor-following rule after launch is preserved, which keeps the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:77:#     - every particle lies on a same-color horizontal corridor cell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:83:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:114:            if 0 <= tr < h and 0 <= tc < w and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:144:            if 0 <= tr < h and 0 <= tc < w and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:156:    \"\"\"Infer the internal particle's initial direction from its local corridor structure.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:161:        if not _has_corridor(grid, r, c, direction):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:172:    \"\"\"Move internal magenta particles along the same corridor network to their final cells.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:486:    \"\"\"Use the same visible corridor color as the start row's flanking bars.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/1/code.py:529:            if not _has_corridor(base, r, c, direction):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:71:#   - Triggers are placed on corridor cells, never on wall or destination cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:72:#   - Unreachable distractors are placed in the opposite sealed corridors. They stay visibly maroon in the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:403:    - Maroon pixels appear in three depth bands: one trigger in the first corridor, one trigger in the second corridor, and several more outside the outer frame; extra distractors can remain trapped in opposite sealed corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7666fa5d/1/code.py:42:  enough room to show all required evidence in one puzzle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/10/code.py:17:#    so markers must move into the corridor between paired sprites. A ray now travels from one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/10/code.py:18:#    active port into that corridor, can hit the opposite sprite, reflect, and ping-pong back.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/10/code.py:26:#    wide corridors, isolated markers, and lane-separated labels so nothing overlaps or merges.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/10/code.py:27:# e) Visual observability comes from repeated pair structure: two corridors, three marker colors,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/10/code.py:32:#    same port repeats across every isomorphic sprite and lights both the corridor and bounce port.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/10/code.py:152:    Read corridor markers as template-port labels, then fire finite reflective ping-pong rays between facing sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/10/code.py:157:    - Sprites are arranged in face-to-face pairs, and isolated single-pixel markers sit inside the corridor in front of some active-edge ports.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/10/code.py:165:    - The marker does not name an absolute location. It identifies one template port inside a face-to-face corridor, and that port must be replayed on every transformed copy while respecting the paired reflective geometry.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:51:#    - Distances come from the visible wall/corridor geometry only; no hidden metadata is used.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:66:#    - The ranking keys depend only on visible geometry: row position, corridor-derived distance,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:72:#    - The destination remains a stable landmark and the corridor walls still separate reachable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:78:#      rows containing multiple reachable maroons require a second observation: closer-in-corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:232:    - Some maroons are flood-fill reachable from the target through floor/maroon corridors; others may be sealed off behind walls as distractors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:240:    - Walls still determine eligibility, but the movement order is no longer purely distance-based and no longer purely scan-order either; you must combine visible row position with local corridor distance inside each row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:19:#   channel rows, and horizontal/vertical corridors are still detected by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:22:#   col 0 now use several colors taken from the corridor palette instead of a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:24:# - A particle may start only if the first reachable horizontal corridor on its\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:26:#   the same way: among perpendicular candidates, only corridors flanked by that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:34:#   row with a red corridor, the same red source does move.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:39:# - The variant is intentionally narrow: corridor geometry, turn shapes, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:42:#   1. at least two real corridor colors,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:43:#   2. at least one movable real corridor whose source color matches,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:44:#   3. at least one other movable real corridor whose source color mismatches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:52:# - Original `_has_corridor()` only checked \"same colored walls\" and did not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:54:#   red source enter a blue corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:63:# - The generator keeps the original corridor-building routines, so geometric\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:66:# - Source colors are assigned after corridor geometry is fixed and only affect\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:74:#   left-edge particle color matches the corridor color actually move.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:76:#   share colors with real corridors elsewhere, so the rule is inferable from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:81:#   colored source column, which is spatially isolated from the corridors by the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:83:# - No new markers or annotations are added inside the corridor field.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:86:# - Particle colors are drawn from the same visible palette as the corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:93:#   movable channels whose source color does not match their corridor color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:95:#   corridor behavior, so the generator rejects it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:100:# - Solver assumption: a legal turn corridor must have wall color equal to the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:102:#   one consistent corridor color along the whole path, exactly like the base\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:124:def _has_corridor(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:161:                if _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir, particle_color):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:171:    \"\"\"Move each odd-row source only through corridors of the same color.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:240:    \"\"\"Reserve a 3-column window for a vertical corridor and return the wall col.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:459:    Returns `(channel_index, row, corridor_color)` tuples using only corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:469:        corridor_color = None\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:476:                corridor_color = above\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:478:        if entrance_col is None or corridor_color is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:480:        bar_above = next((c for c in range(W) if int(g[row - 1, c]) == corridor_color), W)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:481:        bar_below = next((c for c in range(W) if int(g[row + 1, c]) == corridor_color), W)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:483:            candidates.append((i, row, corridor_color))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:501:    candidate_colors = {corridor_color for _, _, corridor_color in candidates}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:515:        corridor_color = bar_color[bar_rows[i]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:517:            particle_color[i] = corridor_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:520:        alt = _choose_alt_color(real_colors, corridor_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/21/code.py:17:#    - Original task: the background is always azure 8, the grid is roomy, sprites are 7-9 by 2,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:23:#    - Original rule: a reachable maroon near one corridor gap is moved into the 3x3 target and its old\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:186:    - Magenta wall segments create corridor gaps and sealed pockets around that target, while maroon tokens sit on floor cells outside the 3x3 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:194:    - The crop hides the distant corridors, so the important evidence is local: maroon inside the 3x3 block means \"selected\", gray means \"reachable and consumed\", and blue means \"blocked out by walls\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:218:    assert starts, \"at least one corridor gap next to the target is required\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/2/code.py:16:#    - The corridor geometry is unchanged from the original task: even rows are colored bars, odd rows are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/2/code.py:38:#    - entrance scan and bar-start validation still hold; they depend on corridor geometry, not on source color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/2/code.py:44:#    - The generator preserves the original corridor builder and keeps bars starting at col 2 or 3, so border\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/2/code.py:51:#      the output introduces magenta at remote corridor endpoints. Across 2-3 examples the human-visible rule is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/2/code.py:52:#      that red marks choose which corridors activate.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/2/code.py:54:#    - Controls stay on the empty border and never overlap corridor bars.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/2/code.py:59:#      used; corridor colors remain purely structural as in the original task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/2/code.py:74:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/2/code.py:106:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/2/code.py:116:    \"\"\"Return the first valid horizontal corridor entrance for row r, or None.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/2/code.py:204:    \"\"\"Reserve a 3-column window for a vertical corridor and return the wall column.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/25/code.py:86:#      overlaps or very thin unreadable corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:40:#    - Walls/corridors are preserved, so the solver still needs reachability and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/19/code.py:20:#    into a corridor between two sprites. A small example is N=7 with labeled rows\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/19/code.py:35:#    - \"Any non-bg blocks a ray\" is no longer true. Markers now sit inside the corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/19/code.py:40:#    The generator keeps both pairs separated vertically, keeps each corridor internal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/19/code.py:45:#    pair shows split two-color bridges with a center gap on odd-width corridors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/19/code.py:48:#    Only one collision corridor exists per row, and there are no perpendicular\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/19/code.py:117:def _corridor_cells(\n/ho