:446:    if not odd_corridors:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/19/code.py:449:    top_corridor = random.choice(odd_corridors)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/19/code.py:450:    bottom_corridor = random.choice(odd_corridors)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/19/code.py:459:    left_margin_top = random.randint(1, W - (top_corridor + 4))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/19/code.py:460:    left_margin_bottom = random.randint(1, W - (bottom_corridor + 4))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/19/code.py:474:        top_corridor,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/19/code.py:482:        bottom_corridor,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/19/code.py:516:        c_right = left_margin_bottom + 1 + bottom_corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D9/1/code.py:2:# Dimension: D9 — 交叉口行为 (obstacle)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D9/1/code.py:4:#         -> 交叉口强制转弯。粒子在水平走廊里遇到“前方仍是背景、但前方格旁边有唯一竖直支路入口”的交叉口时，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D9/1/code.py:29:#     - real corridors are odd rows whose bars above/below share a color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D9/1/code.py:30:#     - fake corridors keep mismatched bar colors and act only as distractors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D9/1/code.py:36:#       next cell has exactly one vertical corridor entry (up or down), then the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D9/1/code.py:55:#     - _has_corridor() still assumes only same-color flanks define a legal turn.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D9/1/code.py:62:#       branch stops before crossing another real horizontal corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D9/1/code.py:88:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D9/1/code.py:122:        if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D9/1/code.py:151:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D9/1/code.py:176:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:19:#   ordering to the same corridor geometry.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:24:#   corridor system, because the center must first reach a gap and then loop\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:28:#   before a farther-left maroon even if its actual corridor path is longer.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:180:    Reachability still depends on corridor connectivity from the center, but priority no longer uses\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:181:    corridor length. A maroon that is geometrically close to one side of the block can outrank another\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/5/code.py:60:#    corridor beyond that side. Because the majority-heavy side is deliberately the wrong side, the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D9/2/code.py:2:# Dimension: D9 — 交叉口行为 (obstacle)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D9/2/code.py:3:# Change: 垂直走廊与水平走廊交叉时，要么两条条完全断开让粒子惯性通过，要么两条条不断让粒子完全阻挡——不存在半通过状态。... → 交叉口信号灯机制\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D9/2/code.py:50:#             particle stops seeing the wall, then tries a perpendicular corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D9/2/code.py:67:# - _has_corridor in the original code assumed the center cell must be BG/PARTICLE.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D9/2/code.py:74:#   the corridor entrance unchanged near the left edge. This prevents signal colors from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D9/2/code.py:112:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/