/code.py:31:#    uses wall-bounded tree corridors with 1-2 openings near the target. This keeps paths unique,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:43:#    cell at a time, each new cell touching exactly one existing corridor cell, so branches never\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:45:#    maroons are placed on isolated floor pockets outside the corridor network.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:51:#    Yellow and teal are confined to narrow corridors outside the destination. Teal overrides yellow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:210:    - Passable openings beside the destination lead into corridor-like floor regions; isolated floor pockets may hold unreachable distractor maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:3:# Name: 沿边界追踪可达性+迷宫式墙壁\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:15:#    Here the block has exactly one opening into a one-cell-wide maze, and the solver must walk that maze\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:17:# 2. Complexity calibration: a full random maze would be visually noisy and harder to validate, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:18:#    generator uses a coarse 5x5 maze lattice mapped to odd cells of the 11x11 canvas. This keeps the maze\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:24:#    the fixed 3x3 destination block, and only carves floor cells where the maze graph explicitly allows it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:43:FILL_K_RANGE = (2, 7)  # leave room for branch distractors so flood-fill would differ\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:133:    assert len(starts) == 1, \"maze must expose exactly one passable opening next to the destination\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:188:    Pull maroon tokens from the left-hand wall-follow route of a maze into the 3x3 block around the red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:192:    - Outside it, magenta walls carve a one-cell-wide orange maze with exactly one opening touching the block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:193:    - Maroon tokens lie on maze corridors; some are on the left-hand route and others hide in side branches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:196:    - Start at the unique corridor cell adjacent to the destination and face away from the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:197:    - Follow the maze using a left-first wall-follow order (left, forward, right, back) until the route exits at the border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:299:    corridor = set()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:302:            corridor.add(_coarse_to_grid(node))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:304:            corridor.add(_edge_cell(a, b))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:305:    corridor.add(_border_exit_cell(main_path[-1]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:307:    for r, c in corridor:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/0/code.py:6:# - Concrete form: keep the original striped corridor system unchanged, but add\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/0/code.py:13:#   corridor geometry, entrance detection, and turn logic remain the same.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/0/code.py:18:#   1) Original `_has_corridor` and straight-step logic assumed that only bg and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/0/code.py:20:#      must also count as traversable corridor cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/0/code.py:21:#   2) `main()` still detects corridor entrances by scanning for early bg cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/0/code.