\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D20/1/code.py:118:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D20/1/code.py:130:    \"\"\"Return the first valid same-color corridor cell on row r, or None.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D20/1/code.py:194:    \"\"\"Move magenta particles along same-color corridors, including Z-shaped offsets.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D20/1/code.py:500:    \"\"\"Generate one candidate input for the D20 Z-corridor variant.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/26/code.py:72:#   preventing immediate border collisions and leaving room for the 1,1,2,3,5,8 prefix.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/1/code.py:4:# 这里改为“右上角/右下角角落调色板编码走廊优先级”；当交叉口同时存在多个合法 90° 转弯时，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/1/code.py:29:#   only available perpendicular corridor when blocked.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/1/code.py:33:# - The corridor layout stays striped: even rows are colored bar rows and odd rows\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/1/code.py:73:# - The palette colors are directly copied from corridor colors already present in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/1/code.py:74:#   the maze; no invisible numeric ordering is used.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/1/code.py:80:#   bottom edges. This keeps the symbolic cue isolated from the corridor mass.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/1/code.py:85:#   \"among simultaneously valid turns, prefer the branch whose corridor color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/1/code.py:111:def _corridor_color(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> int | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/1/code.py:112:    \"\"\"Return the corridor wall color for a legal turn cell, else None.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/1/code.py:1