ixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D12/1/code.py:107:    \"\"\"Return the first real-corridor entrance column for row r, or None.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D12/1/code.py:142:        if _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/1/code.py:25:#    corridor mouth when the two flanking bar cells have the same color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/1/code.py:26:#    This variant keeps that rule for true corridors, but if the unique\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/1/code.py:27:#    perpendicular mouth is corridor-shaped with two different flank colors,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/1/code.py:41:#    - Old _has_corridor assumed only same-color mouths matter.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/1/code.py:58:#    vs inequality of the two flank colors around a corridor mouth.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/1/code.py:60:#    - At any blocker, there is at most one corridor-like perpendicular mouth\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/1/code.py:70:def _corridor_kind(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> str | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/1/code.py:71:    \"\"\"Classify a corridor mouth as 'real', 'fake', or None.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/1/code.py:108:            kind = _corridor_kind(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/1/code.py:141:            if 0 <= tr < h and 0 <= tc < w and _corridor_kind(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir) == \"real\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/1/code.py:162:            if _corridor_kind(g, r, c, \"right\") == \"real\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/1/code.py:181:    \"\"\"Move particles through real corridors; fake mouths trap at the entrance.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D11/1/code.py:3:# Change: 严格条纹布局——偶数行为条行，奇数行为通道行/背景行；输出与输入同尺寸。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D11/1/code.py:25:#     - 原 `_has_corridor(..., left/right)` 依赖 `r-1` / `r+1` 恰好是条行；在本变体中失效，必须搜索最近条行。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D11/1/code.py:86:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D11/1/code.py:116:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D11/1/code.py:150:    \"\"\"Move magenta particles through irregular-height corridors.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D11/1/code.py:265:    \"\"\"Quantify whether generated samples really use irregular-height corridors.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/8/code.py:66:#       which regions of the maze actually grow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/8/code.py:323:    Grow the spiral maze from only two selected tips of a teal T/L source.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/8/code.py:338:      from active endpoints. A T exposes 3 tips but only 2 actually seed the maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/2/code.py:25:# - _has_corridor 原先要求两侧颜色相同；本变体里该前提失效，必须改成“相邻两侧都是彩色即可”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/2/code.py:33:# - 行布局由单行 bar 与宽度为 1/2 的 corridor 交替组成，天然不越界。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/2/code.py:44:# - 假走廊通过“更宽的缺口/更高的通道”制造干扰，但不会和真走廊重叠到难以辨认。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/2/code.py:96:def _has_true_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/2/code.py:97:    \"\"\"True iff (r,c) lies in a 1-cell-wide corridor perpendicular to direction.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/2/code.py:126:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_true_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/2/code.py:143:    \"\"\"Move each magenta particle along aligned narrow corridors.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/2/code.py:154:            if _has_true_corridor(g, r, c, \"right\"):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/2/code.py:524:        \"true_corridors\": true_rows,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/2/code.py:525:        \"fake_corridors\": fake_rows,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D12/2/code.py:15:   - The striped corridor geometry stays the same: even rows are colored bars, odd rows are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D12/2/code.py:26:     corridor crossing cell. In the original one-phase logic that crossing is plain BG, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D12/2/code.py:35:     remaining particles still use the original straight / one-turn corridor vocabulary so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D12/2/code.py:39:   - Original `_has_corridor()` and `_trace()` treat `PARTICLE` as passable everywhere.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D12/2/code.py:74:   - The phase solver assumes starts remain in column 0 and corridor entrances still begin at\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D12/2/code.py:100:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str, passable: set[int]) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D12/2/code.py:117:    \"\"\"Trace one particle through the corridor system using phase-local passability.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D12/2/code.py:133:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir, passable):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D12/2/code.py:157:    \"\"\"Start rows must have a particle in col 0 and an original-style corridor entrance.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D12/2/code.py:233:    \"\"\"Reserve a 3-column window for a vertical corridor and return the wall column.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/2/code.py:8:#    - 原题的交叉行本质上是“一个水平转接槽穿过若干竖直通道”；5 只是视觉提示，solver 几乎不读取它。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/2/code.py:14:#      因而同一条水平槽上红蓝序列会改变通道排列，输入/输出里能直接看到颜色-行为映射。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/2/code.py:25:#    - 通道列间距维持 4-5，保证 marker 对 (c-1,c+1) 不会与相邻交叉重叠。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/24/code.py:139:    - One visible quantity in the input drives two geometric effects at once. Arm length first pushes the launch point farther away from the cross, then also sets how thick the allowed spiral shell is, so the output becomes \"inner spokes + outer finite rings\" instead of a border-filling maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/0/code.py:10:#      corridors exactly as in the base task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/0/code.py:34:#    - The generator keeps the original corridor construction, so trace legality and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/0/code.py:44:#      out from corridor bars. It is also simpler and cleaner than a 3x3 filled square.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/0/code.py:51:#      same-color real corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/0/code.py:68:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/0/code.py:107:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/0/code.py:117:    \"\"\"Return the first valid horizontal corridor cell for row r, if any.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/0/code.py:183:    \"\"\"Move magenta particles along corridors formed by parallel colored bars.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/0/code.py:186:    - bg=7. Particles=6 in col 0. Colored bars on even rows form corridors on odd rows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/0/code.py:211:_N_EXTRA_COLORS = 4                         # corridor/decorator colors (+ BG + PARTICLE = 6)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/0/code.py:224:_VCOL_LEFT_PAD = 4                          # min offset from bar_start for vertical corridors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/0/code.py:240:    \"\"\"Reserve a 3-column window for a vertical corridor and return the wall column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/0/code.py:242:    Returns c_v such that c_v-1 (corridor), c_v (wall), c_v+1 (flank) are all free,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/0/code.py:416:    direction 'up': turn cell at (top, c_v-1); vertical corridor extends up\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/0/code.py:418:    direction 'down': turn cell at (bot, c_v-1); vertical corridor extends down\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/0/code.py:435:    # Carve vertical corridor gaps in bar rows beyond the turn\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/0/code.py:452:    Carves a vertical corridor at c_v-1, places a wall at (row, c_v), and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/0/code.py:27:- Input is a striped corridor field. Particles (color 6) sit in column 0.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/0/code.py:28:- A movable particle starts on a real odd-row corridor, travels through background\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/0/code.py:29:  cells, optionally turns into same-color perpendicular corridors, and stops at an\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/0/code.py:35:- Keep the same input objects, same corridor legality, same turn rule, same stop rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/0/code.py:44:- Suppose row r has a real corridor, the particle moves\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/0/code.py:58:  still about understanding corridor following and 90-degree turns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/0/code.py:68:- _has_corridor(): assumes a traversable corridor cell is currently BG or PARTICLE.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/0/code.py:78:- Entrance detection and the \"start only from genuine real corridors\" filter still\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/0/code.py:83:- The generator keeps the original corridor construction. Vertical corridors still\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/0/code.py:94:  corridor route, including turns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/0/code.py:100:- Trail cells occupy only the 1-cell-wide corridor background, so they do not cover\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/0/code.py:101:  corridor walls or decorative bars.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/0/code.py:125:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/0/code.py:159:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/0/code.py:170:    \"\"\"Move particles through the same corridors, but paint the whole trail.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/0/code.py:241:    \"\"\"Reserve a 3-column window for a vertical corridor and return the wall column.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/1/code.py:40:#       交叉口封口方式都合法。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/1/code.py:67:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/1/code.py:84:    \"\"\"Find the nearest valid launch corridor around a boundary particle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/1/code.py:87:    The initial direction is the unique direction whose first valid corridor cell is closest.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/1/code.py:102:            if _has_corridor(grid, rr, cc, direction):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/1/code.py:130:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/1/code.py:144:    \"\"\"Move boundary particles into the nearest valid corridor entrance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/1/code.py:147:    - Each magenta boundary particle locally searches for the nearest valid corridor entrance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/1/code.py:149:    - Once inside the corridor system, it follows the original task's movement rule unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/1/code.py:205:    \"\"\"Reserve a 3-column window for a vertical corridor and return the wall column.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:9:#   define real corridors, mismatched bar pairs define fake corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:11:# - Variant output logic is: erase start cell -> write the color of the endpoint corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:13:#   input channel color 4 runs right, then turns upward through a vertical color-4 corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:21:# - The variant stays close to the source task: path tracing, ambiguity checks, fake corridors,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:24:#   would recolor to the same corridor color. This is a minimal observability adjustment, not a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:29:#   color was constant (6). In the variant, that is no longer enough because the endpoint corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:32:#   wrong under D7 and must be replaced by corridor-color lookup on the original grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:33:# - The corridor lookup must read from `g`, not `out`, because earlier particles may already have\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:37:# - The generator still uses the original corridor construction, so no new overlaps are introduced.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:38:# - Endpoint recolor is always legal because the traced endpoint is a BG cell inside a real corridor;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:39:#   writing the corridor color there only changes one output pixel and cannot affect tracing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:43:#   terminal corridor rather than staying magenta. This cue is local and directly visible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:49:#   harmonized with its corridor, which is visually cleaner than the original magenta endpoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:53:#   structure: the matched same-color bar pair flanking the particle's final corridor cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:72:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:88:def _corridor_color(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> int:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:89:    \"\"\"Return the bar-pair color of the corridor containing the endpoint cell.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:110:    assert len(set(candidates)) == 1, \"final position is not on a unique real corridor\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:115:    \"\"\"Find the first valid real-corridor entrance for row r, or None.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:157:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:167:    \"\"\"Collect endpoint corridor colors for all particles that actually move.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:179:        colors.append(_corridor_color(g, end_r, end_c, end_dir))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:184:    \"\"\"Move particles along corridors and recolor each endpoint to its terminal corridor color.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:198:            out[end_r, end_c] = _corridor_color(g, end_r, end_c, end_dir)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/1/code.py:240:    \"\"\"Reserve a 3-column window for a vertical corridor and return the wall column.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/0/code.py:44:#      beyond the route corridor. The generator additionally rejects layouts where a channel would\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/1/code.py:46:#         the same radius the first rectangular corridors are four-ways balanced.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/1/code.py:52:#         mirrored side, so the occupied corridors in the left quadrants are not just\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/1/code.py:76:#       nudge before joining the rectangular corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/1/code.py:92:#       corridor systems rather than tiny dead-ends or near-solid blocks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/1/code.py:296:    Key insight: Two mappings must be fused at once: arm-pair length sets the starting radius and available corridor space, while endpoint orientation decides which mirrored spiral family that tip belongs to.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:11:#   start in column 0 and move through same-color corridors. The output now keeps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:13:#   corridor segment currently carrying the particle, and the final cell is then\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:19:#   corridor color through open gap cells, and updates color again whenever the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:20:#   local flanking pair changes at a new corridor row. The endpoint still ends as\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:23:# - Complexity calibration: I keep the original movement rule and corridor test.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:34:#      update/persist corridor color. A cell may be open without locally exposing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:36:#      code cannot require a fresh corridor match every step; it carries forward\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:37:#      the last known corridor color until a new explicit corridor color appears.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:43:#   straight/L/U plans, so corridors remain non-overlapping, in-bounds, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:50:# - Visual cleanliness: trail colors reuse existing corridor-bar colors, so every\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:55:#   corridor. The generator limits palette size to the original regime and forces\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:60:#   2. A moved path has at least one genuine corridor cell before any color is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:82:def _corridor_color(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> int | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:83:    \"\"\"Return the flanking-pair color for a valid corridor cell, else None.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:102:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:103:    return _corridor_color(grid, r, c, direction) is not None\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:107:    \"\"\"Original entrance filter: first real horizontal corridor starting at col <= 3.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:110:        color = _corridor_color(grid, r, c, \"right\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:126:    color is refreshed when the current cell explicitly exposes a corridor pair\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:143:            step_color = _corridor_color(grid, nr, nc, direction)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:155:            turn_color = _corridor_color(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:200:    \"\"\"Move particles as before, but preserve a corridor-colored trail in output.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:257:    \"\"\"Reserve a 3-column window for a vertical corridor and return the wall column.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/3/code.py:23:#       - untouched cells remain teal, so the result looks like a carved maze on a solid field\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/3/code.py:49:#       and the mirrored internal solve has exactly the same amount of room as the base task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/3/code.py:54:#       maze curls the opposite way from the original task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:26:#    The original puzzle has a global striped corridor system and all particles sit on the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:31:#    down, etc. After the first direction is chosen, the old corridor rule is unchanged:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:33:#    perpendicular corridor continuations and turn iff exactly one continuation is valid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:36:#      horizontal corridor regardless of any visible marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:38:#      the same physical corridor after a 90° rotation, but now the start direction is read\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:42:#    corridor generator into several locally rotated sublayouts, which would change much more\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:59:#    all corridor geometry, seals, turn disambiguation and bounds remain legal automatically.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:62:#    entering from different edges; the marker sits between the particle and the corridor, so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:66:#    Using one dedicated arrow color avoids overloading corridor colors. Markers only appear\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:68:#    with bar logic or decorate fake corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:77:#      require tie-breaking beyond the original \"at most one perpendicular corridor\" rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:80:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:111:            if 0 <= tr < h and 0 <= tc < w and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:149:    \"\"\"Move particles through same-color corridors; initial direction comes from edge arrows.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:199:    \"\"\"Reserve a 3-column window for a vertical corridor and return the wall column.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:7:#   The input keeps the original striped corridor layout: even rows are colored bars,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:11:#   every corridor cell that the particle actually occupies causes its two flanking bar\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:12:#   pixels to become BG, as if the particle eats the corridor walls while moving.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:21:#   collect every occupied corridor cell's wall pair. After the trace finishes, the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:25:#   We keep the original corridor grammar and turn distribution so the task remains the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:31:#     same-color horizontal corridors whose bars start at col 2 or 3. This still holds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:35:#   * _has_corridor accepted PARTICLE/BG as passable corridor cells. We preserve that so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:37:#     corridor test of the entered cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:40:#   turns and out-of-bounds vertical corridors. New output writes only convert existing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:45:#   the traveled route. Because the corridor walls are long, repeated, and axis-aligned,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:61:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:77:def _corridor_walls(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:116:            walls = _corridor_walls(grid, r, c, direction)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:125:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:131:        walls = _corridor_walls(grid, r, c, direction)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:178:    \"\"\"Move magenta particles along corridors formed by parallel colored bars.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:181:    - bg=7. Particles=6 in col 0. Colored bars on even rows form corridors on odd rows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:187:    - Variant D7: every traversed corridor cell erases its two flanking colored wall pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:200:_N_EXTRA_COLORS = 4                         # corridor/decorator colors (+ BG + PARTICLE = 6)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:213:_VCOL_LEFT_PAD = 4                          # min offset from bar_start for vertical corridors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:229:    \"\"\"Reserve a 3-column window for a vertical corridor and return the wall column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:231:    Returns c_v such that c_v-1 (corridor), c_v (wall), c_v+1 (flank) are all free,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:403:    direction 'up': turn cell at (top, c_v-1); vertical corridor extends up\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:405:    direction 'down': turn cell at (bot, c_v-1); vertical corridor extends down\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:422:    # Carve vertical corridor gaps in bar rows beyond the turn\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:439:    Carves a vertical corridor at c_v-1, places a wall at (row, c_v), and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/30/code.py:75:#    for in-bounds validity, non-overlap, and enough future room after the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/11/code.py:24:#       replace the continuous spiral corridor with disconnected concentric\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/11/code.py:36:#       weave one connected spiral-like maze in teal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/2/code.py:24:#    horizontal bars on even rows, real corridors where opposite bars share a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/2/code.py:25:#    color, fake corridors where they do not. The path logic is also identical:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/2/code.py:28:#    corridor is available.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/2/code.py:39:#    understanding the same corridor semantics before the turn marks become\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/2/code.py:42:#    - _has_corridor previously allowed BG or PARTICLE in the traversed cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/2/code.py:48:#    - Writing marks is safe because a valid turn target is always a corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/2/code.py:52:#    The original corridor builder already guarantees non-overlapping turn\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/2/code.py:64:#    still contains uncluttered striped corridors; the output adds a small set\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/2/code.py:72:def _has_corridor(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, direction: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/2/code.py:89:    \"\"\"Return the first valid corridor entrance for row r, if any.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/2/code.py:133:            if 0 <= tr < H and 0 <= tc < W and _has_corridor(grid, tr, tc, turn_dir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/2/code.py:221:    \"\"\"Reserve a 3-column window for a vertical corridor and return the wall column.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/37/code.py:21:#    input, and the output spirals leave larger corridors than the base task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/37/code.py:42:#    is visible in the output as wider or narrower rectangular corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D5/0/code.py:27:#    wall sprite in the radiate corridor and rejects placements where the collision stop would be visually inert.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D5/0/code.py:44:#    new stop condition under shadow artifacts. The blocker is aligned in the radiate corridor so the interaction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/12/code.py:28:#    and a right spatial group using the widest horizontal empty corridor between component bboxes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/12/code.py:59:#    The human-visible cues are explicit: a blank vertical corridor reveals the two groups, both\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/12/code.py:199:    - The objects form two horizontal clusters separated by the widest empty vertical corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/42/code.py:44:#         then cross 1, then cross 2. Earlier phases can seal corridors before later phases\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/42/code.py:73:#       corridors; the generator explicitly rejects layouts where sequential activation would\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/0/code.py:33:#    - 迷宫只使用 2-4 条横向墙带，每条 1 个缺口，控制自由度，保证最短路规则能从少量样例归纳。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/0/code.py:272:# --------------- generator (shortest_path_anchor_maze) ---------------\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/35/code.py:39:#       corridor family. The combo therefore keeps a short-arm special case: after the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/35/code.py:52:#       launch side and in the visible offset of the first corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/35/code.py:78:#     - Fill is kept in a mid-density band so the result remains a clean corridor system\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/35/code.py:295:    Key insight: The fusion changes the launch geometry, not the later spacing engine. Position decides which flank each tip uses, and the forced lateral first step replaces the seed task's initial backward retreat, so the very first corridor near each tip becomes visibly rotated and asymmetric.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/29/code.py:3:# Name: 路径分叉+多起点+迷宫布局\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/29/code.py:19:     of laterally shifted bars creates a woven ladder/maze rather than a single snake.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/29/code.py:25:     interlock into a dense maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/29/code.py:33:     D10 change visible: the obstacle field is dense and corridor-like, not just a sparse set of bars.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/29/code.py:53:     overlap vertically. The generator biases this gap toward the minimum, producing the intended maze\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/29/code.py:62:     two-sided enclosure; the bars are packed tightly enough that the green rails look maze-like.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/29/code.py:72:     is mandatory so the obstacle stack reads as a dense corridor system instead of a trivial ladder.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/29/code.py:84:     Large values indicate the intended maze density rather than a sparse fallback.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/29/code.py:85:   - `maze_shift`: `max(bar_lefts) - min(bar_lefts)`. If this is too small, the layout has collapsed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/29/code.py:262:    maze_shift = max(bar_lefts) - min(bar_lefts)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/29/code.py:275:        \"maze_shift\": maze_shift,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/29/code.py:288:    Grow a multi-source green network across a dense bar maze by splitting around every obstacle on both sides.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/29/code.py:303:    each bar forces a full two-sided enclosure, so dense laterally shifted bars turn the output into a woven maze of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/29/code.py:327:        assert current_row <= top, \"bars must leave room for the incoming trunks\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/29/code.py:560:        if metrics[\"maze_shift\"] < 2:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/32/code.py:18:#      全图织成一条单像素宽迷宫路径。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/32/code.py:26:#    - 例：arm=2 时，输入端点围出 5x5 框。原题会在 5x5 框外继续长成一条 maze；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/32/code.py:61:#    - 1 像素框 + 1 像素黑间隔使不同圈层不会糊在一起；十字只占中心十字形通道，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/3/code.py:10:#    - 这个变体把“保持方向”变成不可靠：主通道列改为整列贯通，因此在发生换道的行上，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/3/code.py:12:#      如果还沿用原 solver 的 greedy-straight，就会在这些点继续向下/向上，走错通道。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/3/code.py:23:#    - 一个具体小例子：假设某颜色 token 从第 2 列通道要被送到第 4 列通道。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/3/code.py:40:#      这些在新变体中都不成立，因为主通道列是连续竖线。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/3/code.py:52:#    - 主通道列全部贯通，横向 crossover row 之间至少隔 2 行；这样对角箭头装饰不会压到另一条横线。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/25/code.py:53:#    That leaves one-cell breathing room between neighboring diagonals and avoids\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/26/code.py:52:#      halos leave a guaranteed corridor between bars and between the first bar and the start.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/38/code.py:65:#    - The chosen center makes the spiral solver deterministic and leaves enough local room that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/31/code.py:35:#      main axis must leave room for a 3-row obstacle body plus its Manhattan halo.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/31/code.py:43:#      - leaves a legal open corridor wider than the decoded radius on the non-wall side,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/31/code.py:212:        assert stem_hi >= stem_lo, \"bar stem must leave room for guide pixels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/31/code.py:334:    Key insight: Blue no longer carries one scalar by counting; the cap shape gives a coarse size class, the stem-pair spacing refines it, and the stem-pair location selects which legal corridor the path should occupy.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:3:# Change: NxN空心正方形(N=4)，角为背景色，内部为背景色，四条边各为一种不同颜色，位于网格中心附近... → 十字形hub\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D3/0/code.py:19:#         9: 矩形通道块；变体中不再始终保留 9，而是按 token 在块内的实际穿越条带被染色\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D3/0/code.py:35:#     - 保留 4-5 个通道、非恒等置换、0-3 个 9-rect，使样例中有重复证据支持“彩色轨迹就是路由”\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/39/code.py:36:#    - Because the 8 launch cells are packed more tightly than later corridors, movement checks must\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/39/code.py:48:#        1. the output contains diagonal teal chains everywhere, not just orthogonal corridors;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/39/code.py:55:#      so parallel corridors keep a 1-cell orthogonal gap even while diagonal runs appear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/39/code.py:460:      corridors, except for the other 7 launch seeds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D8/2/code.py:19:#       corridor between two invisible rays. Here the solver first computes exactly that same corridor, then paints the two\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D8/2/code.py:213:    - Flood-fill from the seed through the cavity and outward through the opening, using the endpoint-derived rays as the corridor boundaries.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/27/code.py:521:    - Blue pixels are not just static danger widths: in this fused variant they are consumed bar by bar, so later route segments may reuse corridor cells that were forbidden earlier, while still being steered by the explicit second green endpoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/20/code.py:31:#    immediately dead-end or run out of room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D8/0/code.py:570:                    pass  # skip distractor if no room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D1/1/code.py:18:- The wall stays the dominant non-background object, but it becomes a thin rectangular room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D1/1/code.py:20:- A fill-colored seed blob is placed inside the room. The solver first fills the room interior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D1/1/code.py:21:- After the room is filled, each opening emits its own straight beam outward to the grid edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D1/1/code.py:22:  Example: if the room has a top opening and a left opening, the old single-opening logic would\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D1/1/code.py:40:  first inside the room bbox, then each opening ray is processed independently.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D1/1/code.py:51:- The key clue is structural, not color-id-based: one room clearly has several side gaps, and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D1/1/code.py:56:- Only one room is generated, with exactly two openings and at most five singleton obstacles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D1/1/code.py:72:- The solver assumes the seed is inside the room bbox interior. The generator places it there.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D1/1/code.py:212:    room_mask = np.zeros_like(comp_mask, dtype=bool)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D1/1/code.py:214:        room_mask[r0 + 1:r1, c0 + 1:c1] = True\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D1/1/code.py:215:    passable_room = room_mask & (~comp_mask) & ((g == bg) | (g == fill))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D1/1/code.py:217:    q = [p for p in fill_pos if passable_room[p[0], p[1]]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D1/1/code.py:218:    seen = np.zeros_like(passable_room, dtype=bool)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D1/1/code.py:224:            if 0 <= rr < h and 0 <= cc < w and passable_room[rr, cc] and not seen[rr, cc]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D1/1/code.py:249:    Fill a room-like enclosure and send the fill outward through every visible opening.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D1/1/code.py:257:    - First flood-fill the room interior reachable from the seed inside the enclosure.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/44/code.py:31:#   exist, orthogonal spacing is sufficient, and parity-specific border patches repair the maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/44/code.py:120:    - Once the plus-cross assumptions are replaced by a diagonal X and an 8-direction heading system, the same clockwise wall-following rhythm yields a clean octagonal / diamond spiral maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/24/code.py:206:        assert bottom_row < h, \"bars must leave room below for the route to clear them\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/2/code.py:18:#    - Output still occupies the same family of 1-cell-gap rectangular spiral corridors, but two\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/2/code.py:27:#        corridor in teal; when that corridor turns south, the turning step and following southward\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D1/3/code.py:313:    - Compute the same reachable region as the original task: the wall and endpoint rays define the corridor, and obstacles cast shadows along the radiate direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/33/code.py:15:#    corridor on that bar's open side, so the answer is a wide strip rather than\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/33/code.py:21:#    green area occupies those two open-side corridors plus the thin turn rows\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/33/code.py:27:#    design sits between those extremes: bar-side corridors become visibly wide,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/33/code.py:37:#    enforce corridor widths > 1 or the fused behavior would degenerate back to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/33/code.py:42:#    border start pixel. It additionally enforces a minimum open-corridor width\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/33/code.py:53:#    The band occupies one corridor at a time and uses the original turn rows as\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/33/code.py:62:#    which corridor opens, and the answer simply re-encodes that recovered route\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/33/code.py:228:            corridor = (c1 + radius + 1, w - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/33/code.py:230:            corridor = (0, c0 - radius - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/33/code.py:232:        assert 0 <= corridor[0] <= corridor[1] < w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/33/code.py:241:                \"corridor\": corridor,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/33/code.py:273:        c0, c1 = map(int, bar[\"corridor\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/33/code.py:327:    - Instead of leaving that route as a 1-pixel polyline, expand each detour leg into the whole safe corridor on the bar's open side; the turn rows stay as the thin connectors between those widened strips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/33/code.py:330:    Key insight: The obstacle geometry is only used to infer which open-side corridor the original path would choose; once that corridor chain is known, the answer is just its binary mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D12/0/code.py:3:# Change: 混合输入——大部分通道以实心3x3块作为输入token，0-2个通道以X形作为输入token；X形通道的远端约67%留空... → 全部实心输入\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D1/1/code.py:64:# - True sprites are scattered only in side-specific corridors:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D1/1/code.py:70:#   so they do not satisfy any side corridor test and are safely ignored by the solver.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D1/1/code.py:80:# - Side corridors and corner distractor regions keep objects visually separated.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D1/1/code.py:95:# - Solver assumption: intended sprites lie in exactly one of the four side corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D1/1/code.py:97:# - Solver assumption: ignored components either fall in no corridor or are smaller than\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D1/1/code.py:99:#   corner regions, so they fall in no corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D12/3/code.py:3:# Change: 混合输入——大部分通道以实心3x3块作为输入token，0-2个通道以X形作为输入token；X形通道的远端约67%留空... → 不完整token（残缺3x3块）\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D12/3/code.py:11:#   - X token 保持原样，仍然是 0-2 个通道出现的对角线+中心形状；它们的远端仍可为空或预放 diamond。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D12/3/code.py:45:#   - 每个非 X 通道都使用残缺 solid，而不是偶尔仍给完整 solid；这样 2-4 个样例中一定能看到变体。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/10/code.py:38:#    original size formula, every such center leaves enough room for the single\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/11/code.py:21:# enough room for the D12 stage-by-stage processing to actually occur.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/11/code.py:251:            assert goal_row < h, \"generator must leave room below every bar keep-out\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/11/code.py:334:    \"\"\"Minimum main-axis size with room below every bar's keep-out zone.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D12/2/code.py:3:# Change: 混合输入——大部分通道以实心3x3块作为输入token，0-2个通道以X形作为输入token；X形通道的远端约67%留空... → 双端部分形状输入\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/21/code.py:48:#           to close the same corridor in the same round, both fronts terminate and a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/21/code.py:86:#     - the output seam is geometric, not hidden-id-based: black corridors appear exactly\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/37/code.py:40:#    - Rows are spaced by at least 2, guaranteeing enough room for the `down -> sideways -> down`\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/19/code.py:33:#       already-established corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/19/code.py:437:    - The output is no longer a uniform full tiling. Border contact acts as the activation trigger, so earlier spirals carve out territory first and later spirals visibly terminate against those pre-existing corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D4/0/code.py:3:# Change: 分解（decomposition）——实心3x3块被分解为十字形（中心+4个正交邻居，留在原位）和四角星形（4个对角角，... → 反向分解（对角留、正交走）\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D4/0/code.py:24:#    - 保留原题的 4-5 条通道、非恒等置换、0-3 个 9-矩形、0-2 个 X 输入，避免变体退化成简单的\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D4/0/code.py:25:#      单边复制题。多数通道仍使用 solid 输入，因此“solid -> 原地 X / 远端 diamond”会在每个样本里重复出现。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D4/0/code.py:36:#      或在 X 输入通道里预放一个 diamond（与原题同类的“远端已补全”情况）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D4/0/code.py:38:#    - 关键可见差异是：实心块在输出里不再变成 diamond，而是变成 X。因为每题至少有 2 条 solid 通道，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D4/0/code.py:40:#    - 不使用颜色 id 做任何排序或变换；颜色只沿原通道对应传递。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D4/0/code.py:42:#    - 沿用原题的纵向通道和 sparse token 摆放；变体只交换 token 形状角色，不增加新叠层。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D4/0/code.py:48:#    - 假设 solid 通道的远端默认没有与待发射 diamond 冲突的同色残片；generator 对 solid 通道不预放远端图元。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D4/0/code.py:49:#    - 假设 X 通道若预放远端 diamond，也只是“已经完成的目标形状”，不会需要再次识别成源 token；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D14/0/code.py:48:        that corridor empty.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/4/code.py:14:#      之后直行步长推广为 3/2（即 spacing+1 / spacing），于是同心矩形通道之间始终隔 2 格；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/4/code.py:24:#      第一条侧向通道会离十字主横/主竖条过近，无法满足“留白=L”的新规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/4/code.py:29:#    - 人类可以直接从样例里同时读出两件事：靠近中心的首条横/竖通道与十字之间的空隙就是 L；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/4/code.py:107:    Key insight: The arm length has a double role. The same L that measures the input cross also sets the corridor spacing and the number of rings, so solvers must infer one quantity and apply it twice.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D12/3/code.py:106:    room_mask = np.zeros_like(comp_mask, dtype=bool)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D12/3/code.py:108:        room_mask[r0 + 1:r1, c0 + 1:c1] = True\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D12/3/code.py:109:    passable_room = room_mask & (~comp_mask) & ((g == bg) | (g == fill))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D12/3/code.py:112:    seen = _flood(passable_room, fill_pos)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D12/3/code.py:182:    Solve nested open-frame rooms from the innermost level outward.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D12/3/code.py:184:    The current fill first expands inside the nearest room, then leaks through that room's gap\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D12/3/code.py:185:    until it reaches the next enclosing room. Repeating that stage over all same-colored wall\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D12/3/code.py:186:    components turns nested rooms into a sequential inner-to-outer expansion task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D4/3/code.py:3:# Change: 分解（decomposition）——实心3x3块被分解为十字形（中心+4个正交邻居，留在原位）和四角星形（4个对角角，... → L形分解\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/0/code.py:318:    - with room for at least one non-reference segment to be longer than ref_len.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/5/code.py:22:#    corridor, the agent now walks on a coarse lattice and leaves visible 2-pixel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/5/code.py:26:#    Only two spatial parameters change at once: the corridor widens from 1 to 2,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/5/code.py:34:#      corridor blocks the launch immediately. The fused rule therefore treats the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/5/code.py:208:    - Every new segment must keep a 2-pixel orthogonal corridor from previously\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D10/1/code.py:15:#     - 新逻辑中，假设两个都向右开口的 sprite 共享同一条辐射通道：右侧 sprite 离右边界更近，先填满自己的扇区；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D10/1/code.py:30:#     - 两者始终朝同一方向开口，并沿该方向设置不同的边界距离；同时在垂直方向保持部分重叠，确保后者会与前者争夺同一填充通道。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D4/2/code.py:3:# Change: 分解（decomposition）——实心3x3块被分解为十字形（中心+4个正交邻居，留在原位）和四角星形（4个对角角，... → 镜像对称分解\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/28/code.py:67:#    maze-like appearance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/28/code.py:363:    Key insight: The final maze is not controlled by one cue anymore. You must read the border legend for global handedness, read each arm marker for its local start offset, and then follow the colored obstacle cells that inject left/right turns along the route.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/17/code.py:16:#      into a shrinking corridor and later exits it, producing a dense zigzag.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/17/code.py:25:#      leave a traversable corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/17/code.py:42:#      chamber width explicitly and reserves room for every remaining suffix.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/34/code.py:65:#      room to make multiple turns, and the slot-phased round-robin coloring differs measurably from the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D7/0/code.py:41:#      are monotone and hug a single large sprite instead of arbitrary mazes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/36/code.py:41:#    arms and rectangles fit inside the grid, stay disjoint, and leave open corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/36/code.py:48:#    overlays near the cross center and keeps each corridor leg readable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/36/code.py:200:    the output becomes a set of corridor-limited zigzags instead of nested spirals.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/1/code.py:21:#     entire pipe maze. The variant still computes those same token results, but returns only the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/1/code.py:22:#     rows `[top-1:top+2]` and `[bottom-1:bottom+2]`, so the maze rows vanish.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/1/code.py:37:#     token bands are separated by the omitted wire corridor. The crop must be endpoint-aware.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/1/code.py:44:#   - Across samples, inputs remain large pipe mazes while outputs are always compact 6xW strips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/1/code.py:386:    - After computing that full result, discard the entire wire corridor and keep only the 3-row\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1818057f/D9/3/code.py:30:#      humans to infer: mostly 3xL and Lx3 fg corridors plus a few isolated distractors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1818057f/D9/3/code.py:45:#    - A human can see that a longer corridor contains several local plus opportunities,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1818057f/D9/3/code.py:47:#      vertical corridors exposes both parts of the scan order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1818057f/D9/3/code.py:54:#      candidate survives inside a corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1818057f/D9/3/code.py:115:    - This is an in-place process rather than a simultaneous one. In corridor-like blobs with multiple overlapping '+' candidates, only the candidates that appear earliest in scan order survive to be recolored.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/23/code.py:20:#      into a maze-like spiral\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/23/code.py:42:#      post-processing all assumed self-avoiding orthogonal corridors that try to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/23/code.py:231:    - The fusion keeps the original \"start from the four tips\" scaffold, but replaces the spiral with a single unturned ray and replaces the 90-degree launch with a 45-degree clockwise launch. That turns the output from a maze-like orthogonal fill into a clean X-like overlay around the cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/3/code.py:376:    \"\"\"Find all (t0, anchor_mode, capacity_list) where segments can be placed with room for length variation.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/22/code.py:30:#   drawing, because visible blanks would incorrectly open corridors. The fix is to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/20/code.py:51:#    - The grid remains sparse and axis-aligned. Distractors live in the open corridor instead of intersecting other\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/20/code.py:67:#      distractors in safe, non-touching corridor segments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/2/code.py:327:    \"\"\"Find all (t0, anchor_mode, capacity_list) where segments can be placed with room for length variation.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/41/code.py:21:#       replace the original connected spiral corridor with closed rectangular\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/41/code.py:38:#       lengthen segments to build one outward spiral maze\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/2/code.py:19:#      Under this combo the second bar pushes the corridor much farther away, and BFS must find the shortest path through\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/2/code.py:41:#      and trailing gap >= 1. This prevents halo overlap from sealing the corridor unless the solver check rejects it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D13/0/code.py:3:# Change: 单步变换——每个token独立执行一次分解和传输操作，各通道之间没有顺序依赖... → 链式反应传播\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/30/code.py:13:#      \"2-pixel corridor\" variant, the same right-hand turtle logic is kept but all nonzero moves\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/30/code.py:27:#    - The active-axis rule uses one visually legible cue: which axis has more room to the border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/30/code.py:42:#      roomier axis, and the resulting corridors are much wider than in the source task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/30/code.py:303:    Grow a sparse pair of clockwise rectangular spirals from the roomier opposing tips of a teal cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/30/code.py:309:    - Compare the cross's two axes by visible tip-to-border clearance; only the axis with more room is active,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/30/code.py:317:    Key insight: This is not a dense four-source tiling anymore. Solving requires identifying the roomier axis,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/14/code.py:38:#   cross remains fully in-bounds and the spiral still has room to develop without overlaps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D13/1/code.py:3:# Change: 单步变换——每个token独立执行一次分解和传输操作，各通道之间没有顺序依赖... → 按管道长度排序处理\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/10/code.py:378:    \"\"\"Pick 2..4 nearby start columns that leave room for every loop side rail.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1818057f/D8/3/code.py:39:#    - 解题者在 2-4 组样例里应能看到：十字形都变 teal，方块都变 orange，其余黄块不变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:62:#       Chosen away from the border for the center point, with enough room for the short tick.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D13/2/code.py:3:# Change: 单步变换——每个token独立执行一次分解和传输操作，各通道之间没有顺序依赖... → 先拆分后路由两步\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:19:#      only open side of a bar, it fills the whole free corridor on that side until the next\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:29:#        right corridor cols [9, 15] from the turn row above the bar to the exit row below it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:36:#      corridor of width >= 4, so the Chebyshev square keepout and the wide-fill effect are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:45:#      we now solve the route as ordered corridor switches and paint full slabs, not just\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:48:#      wall-attached alternating bars and full-corridor painting, the canonical geometry is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:54:#    - Consecutive bars alternate walls, guaranteeing that each currently filled corridor is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:59:#      open width >= 4, so filled corridors are legal and visually broad.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:63:#      no-go rectangles, and the green output occupies whole side corridors rather than a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:71:#    - Because the filled areas are monotone rectangles/corridors aligned to bar keepouts,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:78:#      corridor intersects each next bar keepout.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:183:def _corridor_after_bar(bar: dict[str, int], width: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:184:    \"\"\"Return the full open-side corridor interval after clearing one bar.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:191:    assert 0 <= lo <= hi < width, \"bar must leave a non-empty open corridor\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:196:    \"\"\"Solve one canonical top-start instance using Chebyshev keepouts + corridor filling.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:225:        # If the current filled corridor hits the keepout columns, the route must switch sides here.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:226:        assert not (cur_hi < left or cur_lo > right), \"current corridor must intersect each next bar keepout\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:232:        # Continue straight down in the current corridor until just above the keepout.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:235:        new_lo, new_hi = _corridor_after_bar(bar, w)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:237:        # Turn above the keepout, crossing from the old corridor into the new one.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:242:        # D17/2: fill the whole open corridor alongside and just beyond this keepout.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:255:    Route a border-start path around side-attached bars, using square Chebyshev keepouts and filling the full bypass corridor in green.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:264:    - Move from the start edge toward the opposite edge, and whenever the current corridor intersects a bar's keepout, switch to the only open side above that keepout.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:265:    - Instead of painting a 1-pixel route, fill the entire open corridor used to bypass that keepout, producing broad green slabs. After all bypasses are drawn, convert blue pixels to red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:267:    Key insight: Blue pixels still encode how much clearance each bar demands, but under the fused rule that clearance is read in Chebyshev geometry and the solver must paint the whole safe side corridor around the resulting rectangular keepout, not just a thin shortest path.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:306:    \"\"\"Allowed bar lengths that preserve a visibly wide open-side corridor.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:409:    corridor_widths = [(_corridor_after_bar(bar, canonical_inp.shape[1])[1] - _corridor_after_bar(bar, canonical_inp.shape[1])[0] + 1) for bar in bars]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/21/code.py:410:    return extra_green >= 12 and max(corridor_widths) >= OPEN_WIDTH_STRONG\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D14/1/code.py:330:    \"\"\"Find all (t0, anchor_mode, capacity_list) where segments can be placed with room for length variation.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D6/3/code.py:67:#      room\" with \"what blocks the beam\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D10/0/code.py:346:    \"\"\"Find all (t0, anchor_mode, capacity_list) where segments can be placed with room for length variation.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:53:#   bounds and leave room for the existing crossover network.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1818057f/D1/4/code.py:199:        corridors: list[list[tuple[int, int]]] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1818057f/D1/4/code.py:212:                corridors.append(cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1818057f/D1/4/code.py:213:        if not corridors:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1818057f/D1/4/code.py:216:        n_ext = int(rng.integers(1, min(2, len(corridors)) + 1))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1818057f/D1/4/code.py:217:        chosen_ids = rng.choice(len(corridors), size=n_ext, replace=False)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1818057f/D1/4/code.py:220:            corridor = corridors[int(idx)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1818057f/D1/4/code.py:221:            max_len = min(3, len(corridor))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1818057f/D1/4/code.py:223:            cells = corridor[:ext_len]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D6/2/code.py:3:# Change: 半包围区域由U形或C形边框围成，有一个明确的开口方向（上/下/左/右）... → 包围区域带有瓶颈通道\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D6/2/code.py:10:#     to: \"内部腔室只通过固定长度的窄颈通道连接外部；填充必须先穿过通道，再在外侧扇形扩散\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D6/2/code.py:15:#       - 窄颈长度固定为 3 像素，这样 solver 可以把“通道长度”和“外扩模式”分开识别，避免几何歧义。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D6/2/code.py:25:#     - 变体里，端点先是颈部出口，不代表腔室立刻张开；solver 需要先承认“出口前面是一条窄通道”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D6/2/code.py:26:#     - 因为通道两侧是墙，所以 flood fill 会被强制挤过 1-2 像素的瓶颈。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D6/2/code.py:29:#     - 只增加一个核心自由度: 通道宽度 1 或 2。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D6/2/code.py:30:#     - 通道长度固定为 3，避免样例过少时人类无法判断“哪些直行像素属于通道，哪些属于 1:2 斜率模式”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D6/2/code.py:34:#       在瓶颈变体中这个假设失效，因为端点附近先是直通道，不是张开边。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D6/2/code.py:35:#     - 原 solver 用端点近邻推断 1:2 模式；现在改为读取“通道后的第一步”，因为前 3 步固定属于通道。\n/home/lixinyu/sna