叠。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/1/code.py:41:#     - 为避免 solid 目标槽与 X 目标槽碰撞，只把 X 通道选成 `perm` 的整条 cycle 的并集；于是 solid 通道的 `perm` 像与 X 通道的 identity 槽天然不相交。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b3084d4/D8/2/code.py:3:# Change: 交叉分割（十字形）\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D5/1/code.py:22:#     sort the real frame colors by enclosed-room count as before.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D5/1/code.py:23:#     For a frame with N rooms, output an N x N solid square of that frame color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D5/1/code.py:27:#     original encoding for room counts [2, 4] was a 2x4 grid:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D5/1/code.py:33:#     The only changed stage is the final target rendering; room detection and ordering\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D5/1/code.py:38:#     room counts 1-6, so the stacked output remains compact and unambiguous.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D5/1/code.py:42:#     - The original `width = max(rooms)` still works as the new square side cap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D5/1/code.py:44:#       may need multiple rows. Replace it with `sum(rooms)`.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D5/1/code.py:45:#     - The original fill `out[r, :rooms] = color` assumed exactly one row per object.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D5/1/code.py:46:#       In the variant it must fill a rooms-by-rooms block, otherwise only the first\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D5/1/code.py:54:#     a human can now see that larger room counts occupy taller blocks, not just longer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D5/1/code.py:115:def _room_count_for_color(g: np.ndarray, color: int) -> int:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D5/1/code.py:139:    above: dict[int, set[int]] = {color: set() for color, _rooms, _walls in group}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D5/1/code.py:140:    indegree: dict[int, int] = {color: 0