ver encloses a room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D4/3/code.py:23:#      frame walls, but it still has no closed cycle, so its room count stays zero.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D4/3/code.py:26:#        cropping that color, `_reconstruct_walls` finds no usable closed grid, so rooms = 0.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D4/3/code.py:29:#        open mask instead of inventing a rectangular frame, and rooms = 0.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D4/3/code.py:30:#      * Difference: the zero-room color is now a structured line object that competes for\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D4/3/code.py:37:#    - Real frames remain 3-5 colors with 1-6 rooms, and at most one room-count tie pair is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D4/3/code.py:42:#    - `_room_count_for_color(...)`: originally safe because scattered noise never formed rooms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D4/3/code.py:45:#    - `drawings = ... if rooms > 0`: unchanged meaning; valid frames are exactly those whose\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D4/3/code.py:48:#      extra open-line color and no real frame degenerating to zero rooms after overlaps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D4/3/code.py:66:#      recognizable room structure.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D4/3/code.py:69:#      it is the single line-set color whose reconstructed walls enclose zero rooms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D4/3/code.py:142:    above: dict[int, set[int]] = {color: set() for color, _rooms, _walls in group}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D4/3/code.py:143:    indegree: dict[int, int] = {color: 0 for color, _rooms, _walls in group}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D4/3/code.py:184:    - Colors with at least one enclosed region are the real frames; the unique zero-room color is the distractor and also the output padding color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/89565ca0/D4/3/