ht_w), dtype=bool)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D16/2/code.py:336:    base[2, left_w : left_w + corridor_len] = True\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D16/2/code.py:337:    base[:, left_w + corridor_len :] = True\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/0/code.py:301:def _corridor_rects(long: int, thick: int, count: int, dots: int) -> list[tuple[int, int, int, int, bool]] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/0/code.py:528:    canon = _corridor_rects(long, thick, total - dots, dots)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D12/2/code.py:63:#     corridor clean via the original forbidden mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/1/code.py:307:def _corridor_rects(long: int, thick: int, count: int, dots: int) -> list[tuple[int, int, int, int, bool]] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/1/code.py:500:    canon = _corridor_rects(long, thick, total - dots, dots)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D5/1/code.py:3:# Change: 同尺寸红色实心方块位于通道末端（接触网格边缘），可达时方块覆盖目标位置... → 距离编码终点\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D5/1/code.py:10:#     - A blue winding river is still the only traversable corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D5/1/code.py:43:#       corridor without branches in placement space.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D5/1/code.py:66:#     - Only one mixed-color object exists, and it is isolated at the corridor end, so the grid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D5/1/code.py:278:    - bg dominates the corners, and a river color forms a winding corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D5/1/code.py:285:    - Move that many placement steps toward the corridor end, capped by the farthest reachable point.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/3/code.py:306:def _corridor_rects(long: int, thick: int, count: int, dots: int) -> list[tuple[int, int, int, int, bool]] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/3/code.py:539:    canon = _corridor_rects(long, thick, total - dots, dots)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D3/1/code.py:17:the region's inner boundary track. The region is still an enclosed irregular room, but the yellow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D3/1/code.py:25:  - Original: a yellow at the top edge of a room with a right-pointing legend moves horizontally\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D3/1/code.py:27:  - Variant: the same room with a clockwise legend makes the yellow stay on the wall-adjacent\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D3/1/code.py:54:The generator keeps the original closed-room construction and legend/wall non-overlap rules, then\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D3/1/code.py:57:1-cell corridors) are rejected. This guarantees:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D3/1/code.py:64:  - start on the room perimeter\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D5/2/code.py:3:# Change: 同尺寸红色实心方块位于通道末端（接触网格边缘），可达时方块覆盖目标位置... → 堆叠终点\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D5/2/code.py:43:#    mover and destination never overlap, and the slot is part of the river corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D5/2/code.py:49:#    The reachable endpoint is a full n×n parking bay contiguous with the corridor, so the output\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D5/2/code.py:178:    - bg fills most of the canvas. A river-colored corridor forms a winding route.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D15/2/code.py:309:def _corridor_rects(long: int, thick: int, count: int) -> list[tuple[int, int, int, int]] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D15/2/code.py:480:    rects_long = _corridor_rects(long, thick, total)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D3/3/code.py:22:#       topology: enclosed irregular rooms formed by 1-cell-thick colored walls\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D3/3/code.py:23:#       passable: only bg/yellow cells inside a bounded room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D3/3/code.py:26:#       - each yellow moved in a single fixed direction until the next step would leave the room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D3/3/code.py:40:#     - suppose a yellow starts at (6,6) with direction (+1,+1) in a room whose southeast corner is close\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D3/3/code.py:42:#     - variant: it moves cell-by-cell; on touching the southeast wall it bounces to (-1,-1) and spends the remaining budget moving back across the room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D3/3/code.py:43:#     - visible effect: output yellows are no longer always packed against the far wall; many end mid-room after one or more rebounds\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D3/3/code.py:50:#     - room detection still assumes passable cells are bg/yellow enclosed by non-bg walls; generator preserves this\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D3/3/code.py:51:#     - border color lookup still uses majority adjacent wall color; generator keeps one wall color per room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D3/3/code.py:56:#     - grown rooms remain enclosed and disjoint\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D3/3/code.py:57:#     - yellow start cells are accepted only if the shared simulator keeps them inside the room and produces distinct final cells under the same processing order used by `main`\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D12/0/code.py:26:  idea from collision_stop: obstacles are hard blockers, not a general maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D9/0/code.py:17:# - The blue corridor is no longer a single start-to-end river. It is a tree:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D9/1/code.py:232:    - The corners reveal the background color. A river color forms a connected corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D12/1/code.py:30:#     - Output keeps the walls, because the final state is a frame of the same maze\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D12/1/code.py:78:  - Edge bites are only 1 cell deep, avoiding hidden background pockets that would create misleading extra rooms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/7/code.py:225:      slots, and the number of chosen slots is capped by remaining room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D2/1/code.py:2:# Dimension: D2 — 通道宽度约束 (path)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D2/1/code.py:3:# Change: 通道宽度>=n时可通过，<n时形成阻塞点（chokepoint），方块被卡住... → 渐变宽度约束\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D2/1/code.py:21:# - It slides one cell at a time through the blue corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D2/1/code.py:71:#   corridor that becomes narrower away from the start. The output then shows\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D2/1/code.py:75:#   size difference, border contact, and corridor width.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D2/1/code.py:212:    - Late corridor sections can be narrower than the starting square because the mover may have already shrunk enough by the time it reaches them.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/32/code.py:276:    assert placed == n_new, \"expected enough room for all transferred sprites\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D8/0/code.py:96:    - A dominant background surrounds one river-like corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D8/0/code.py:97:    - Two same-sized solid squares sit on that corridor, but their colors no longer encode\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D4/2/code.py:31:#    Small traced example on a 1-cell-high corridor moving right:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D8/1/code.py:15:#     - 若通道中存在宽度 < mover 尺寸的卡口，则 mover 停在最远可达放置位，并且同样只显示\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/58490d8a/D14/1/code.py:34:#    - Right alignment needs a parity-compatible anchor column near the right edge; the generator guarantees enough room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D8/3/code.py:10:#     river: blue 1, still a single winding corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D8/3/code.py:72:    - The corner-majority color is the background, and a blue corridor snakes through it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D8/3/code.py:77:    - Move the interior square along the corridor using unit 4-neighbor shifts of its full NxN footprint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/abc82100/D8/2/code.py:48:#    Legend examples are placed only inside a dedicated top strip, with enough room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/abc82100/D10/0/code.py:360:            border_room = min(anchor[0], h - 1 - anchor[0], anchor[1], w - 1 - anchor[1])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/abc82100/D10/0/code.py:361:            score = (spread, len(ring), border_room)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D1/0/code.py:2:# Dimension: D1 — 通道导航方式 (path)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D1/0/code.py:3:# Change: 沿蓝色水道走廊（corridor_following），方块在宽度>=n的通道内BFS搜索可行放置位置... → 重力流动导航\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D1/0/code.py:53:#     - \"reachable cases end on the bottom shelf, so the output reads as a gravity-driven descent rather than arbitrary corridor traversal\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D1/0/code.py:270:            raise AssertionError(\"not enough vertical room for shelves\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/2/code.py:221:    assert placed == n_new, \"expected enough room to place all transferred sprites\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D1/1/code.py:2:# Dimension: D1 — 通道导航方式 (path)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D1/1/code.py:3:# Change: 沿蓝色水道走廊（corridor_following），方块在宽度>=n的通道内BFS搜索可行放置位置... → 直线射线导航\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D1/1/code.py:27:#     from: corridor_following\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D1/1/code.py:44:#       - step-BFS can walk cell-by-cell along a horizontal corridor to the T-junction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D1/1/code.py:52:#     - the visual river is still a winding corridor rather than a trivial open room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D1/1/code.py:155:    Key insight: Unlike the original free BFS through the corridor, interior cells of a straight run are pass-through only; turns are possible only at places where a slide naturally stops.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D1/4/code.py:4:# Dimension: D1 — 通道导航方式 (path)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D1/4/code.py:5:# Change: 沿蓝色水道走廊（corridor_following），方块在宽度>=n的通道内BFS搜索可行放置位置... → 管道跟踪导航\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D1/4/code.py:10:#     - 仍然保留绿色背景、蓝色通道、黑色移动方块、红色目标方块。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D1/4/code.py:14:#     - 方块大小仍为 n×n，蓝色通道也按这个 n 渲染，因此 solver 仍要先恢复“哪些 top-left 位置能放下整个 n×n 方块”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D1/4/code.py:29:#     - 原题允许通道只是连通即可；新题还隐含要求 mover 的 placement 节点是叶子、分叉结点的度数为 3，生成器负责保证。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D16/0/code.py:3:# Change: 无符号编码——角色由固定颜色值隐式编码（黑=移动体，红=目标，蓝=通道，绿=背景）... → 图例区域编码\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D16/1/code.py:3:# Change: 无符号编码——角色由固定颜色值隐式编码（黑=移动体，红=目标，蓝=通道，绿=背景）... → 控制像素编码方向\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D16/1/code.py:20:#      a blue corridor and either reaches the other square or stops at the farthest feasible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D16/1/code.py:57:#    - The existing corridor construction and chokepoint checks are retained, so the n x n\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D16/1/code.py:71:#      distinguish from the squares and corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D16/1/code.py:123:    - bg dominates the corners; a river color forms the corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D16/2/code.py:3:# Change: 无符号编码——角色由固定颜色值隐式编码（黑=移动体，红=目标，蓝=通道，绿=背景）... → 目标方块内编码\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D20/1/code.py:3:# Change: 不同颜色墙壁可以4-邻接形成连通的迷宫结构，区域之间通过共享墙壁相邻或由空间隔开... → 区域串联（一个区域的输出边是另一个的输入边）\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D20/1/code.py:31:- `components_mask(passable, connectivity=4)`: in the original task this found one isolated room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D20/1/code.py:34:- Border-color majority vote: originally it identified a single room's wall color. In the variant\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D3/0/code.py:149:    - A dominant background color fills the corners, with a blue river corridor running through it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D5/3/code.py:366:    # 2. Canvas size (must fit frame grid + room for sprites).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D3/2/code.py:27:#       river remains a single winding corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D3/2/code.py:85:#     - trail uses only mover color and only on the river corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D3/2/code.py:282:    - The corner-majority background surrounds one blue river corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D3/2/code.py:283:    - Two same-sized solid squares sit on that corridor: the mover is inside the grid, while the destination touches an edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/97d7923e/D5/3/code.py:275:        room = WIDTH_MAX - width_needed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/97d7923e/D5/3/code.py:277:        if room > 0 and adjustable:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a25697e4/D5/2/code.py:3:# Change: 阶梯形（staircase/upper-triangular）凹槽，1-3个像素，由间隙行/列与notch组合形成... → T形或十字形凹槽\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a25697e4/D5/2/code.py:5:# - The visible rule change is shifted from \"阶梯形（staircase/upper-triangular）凹槽，1-3个像素，由间隙行/列与notch组合形成\" to \"T形或十字形凹槽\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a25697e4/D5/2/code.py:7:# - Variant detail: 凹槽呈T形或十字形，plug也为对应形状。这类对称性更强的形状在旋转下的匹配更微妙——某些旋转角度看似吻合但实际不对齐。增加空间推理精度要求。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/45a5af55/D2/1/code.py:3:# Change: 构建正方形嵌套框架（每层为等厚方形环）... → 构建十字形嵌套框架\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D6/2/code.py:38:#       - gunit is limited to {2, 3, 4}. This is visibly variable, but still leaves enough room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/22/code.py:186:    assert placed == n_new, \"expected enough room to place all transferred sprites\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:24:    - Concrete look: a colored outer wall encloses a room; inside the room there are black floor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:31:      new main() treats the enclosed room as the union of passable cells plus obstacle cells,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:37:      if the legend says \"right\", a vertical green bar inside the room blocks the row of the yellow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:51:    - `passable = (g == bg) | (g == mover)` assumed the entire enclosed room was exactly the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:52:      passable component. This fails once obstacle cells sit inside the room, because the room would\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:64:    - Regions are placed as closed rectangular rooms with a 1-cell exterior buffer so rooms and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:66:    - Obstacle bars are placed strictly inside the room, never on the outer wall, and the generator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:68:    - Each room is guaranteed to have at least one yellow start whose chosen shortest route contains\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:74:      enough to infer \"move through the room toward that side while avoiding green obstacles\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:82:    - Using rectangular rooms here is intentional: it reduces clutter so the D21 change is the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:92:    - The solver assumes each enclosed room is one bounded component in the meta-mask\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:313:    - A room interior may contain obstacle color 3 in addition to black floor and yellow movers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:315:    - A yellow seeks the farthest reachable cell in the legend direction within its room, routing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:317:      are treated as blockers for later yellows in the same room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:326:    room_mask = (g == bg) | (g == MOVER) | (g == OBSTACLE)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:329:    for pts in components_mask(room_mask, connectivity=4):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:333:        room = {(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in pts}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:334:        passable = {p for p in room if int(g[p]) in (bg, MOVER)}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:340:        for r, c in room:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:344:                if (nr, nc) in room:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:430:def _room_wall_cells(r0: int, c0: int, h_out: int, w_out: int) -> set[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:518:def _sample_room(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:562:        walls = _room_wall_cells(r0, c0, h_out, w_out)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:569:            \"room\": passable | obstacles,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:592:        reg = _sample_room(rng, occupied, color, color_dir[color], total_regions)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:644:    expected = [reg[\"room\"] for reg in regions]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/0/code.py:2:# Dimension: D12 — 背景与通道的颜色关系 (meta)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/0/code.py:3:# Change: 固定配色：背景=绿色(3)，通道=蓝色(1)，移动体=黑色(0)，目标=红色(2)... → 可变配色方案\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/0/code.py:9:#     - A single winding corridor still connects the two square regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/0/code.py:21:#     - A second color forms one connected winding corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/0/code.py:22:#     - Two other colors form solid equal-sized squares sitting on the corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/0/code.py:42:#       corridor color, one interior square, one border-touching square.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/0/code.py:53:#       valid because the corridor occupies more cells than either square and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/0/code.py:56:#     - Squares are painted only onto corridor cells and never overlap each other.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/0/code.py:57:#     - The destination is extended to a boundary but still lies on the corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/0/code.py:60:#     - Chokepoints only erase corridor cells to background and are verified not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/0/code.py:64:#       corners and largest empty area, the corridor is the long connected path,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/0/code.py:154:    Slide one inferred square through a color-shuffled corridor until it reaches the matching-size border square.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/0/code.py:158:    - A second color forms a single winding corridor through the background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/0/code.py:159:    - Two other colors form equal-sized solid squares on that corridor: one interior square and one edge-touching square.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/0/code.py:163:    - Move the mover through all n x n placements whose full area lies inside corridor-or-square cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/0/code.py:165:    - Repaint the mover's starting area with the corridor color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/0/code.py:168:    - The palette is shuffled from puzzle to puzzle, so color ids are unreliable; the stable cues are corner-majority background, the connected corridor, and the fact that only the destination square touches the boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/2/code.py:2:# Dimension: D12 — 背景与通道的颜色关系 (meta)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/2/code.py:3:# Change: 固定配色：背景=绿色(3)，通道=蓝色(1)，移动体=黑色(0)，目标=红色(2)... → 多色通道分段\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/2/code.py:16:#    The river is no longer a single-color corridor. Each input contains a main\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/2/code.py:17:#    corridor plus extra segments in a second river color. The mover may slide\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/2/code.py:23:#    corridor later continues in teal, the old logic would still regard the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/2/code.py:24:#    whole corridor as open if teal were chosen as the global river. The new\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/2/code.py:29:#    Reachable cases keep the whole main corridor in the mover's water color and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/2/code.py:31:#    of the main corridor, so the color rule actively determines the stop point.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/2/code.py:46:#    corridor, extends the destination to the border, then adds a second-color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/2/code.py:61:#    stuck samples show the mover halting exactly when the corridor changes to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/2/code.py:211:    - The corner-majority background surrounds a winding corridor made from two river colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/2/code.py:212:    - Two same-sized solid squares sit on that corridor: an interior mover and a border-touching destination.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D12/2/code.py:221:    The second river color is a visual decoy: even a wide corridor segment becomes impassable when its color does not match the mover's starting water.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D7/2/code.py:3:# Change: 1-2种墙壁颜色，每种形成1-3个封闭区域，总计不超过4个区域；不同颜色墙壁可4-邻接形成迷宫结构... → 共享墙壁（两个区域共用一面墙）\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D4/0/code.py:3:# Change: 黑色实心n*n正方形，尺寸n=1~4，位于通道内部但不接触网格边缘... → 矩形移动体\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D4/0/code.py:33:       horizontal corridor only has to be 2 pixels tall, but a vertical corridor must\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D4/0/code.py:82:   - River is still a single clean corridor; no extra markers or labels are added.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D4/0/code.py:96:  stuck rule: at least one corridor segment is narrowed below the needed cross-section\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D4/0/code.py:142:    - The corner-majority background surrounds one blue winding corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D4/0/code.py:143:    - Two solid same-sized rectangles lie on the corridor: an interior black mover and a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D4/0/code.py:147:    - The black rectangle keeps its orientation and slides along the corridor toward the red one.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D4/0/code.py:154:    - Horizontal motion is limited by corridor height, while vertical motion is limited by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D4/0/code.py:155:      corridor width, so non-square rectangles are blocked by direction-specific chokepoints.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/97d7923e/D8/1/code.py:206:    \"\"\"Pick distinct fill lengths; the first one must leave room for the embedded legend.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D5/0/code.py:46:#   network rather than a single corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D4/3/code.py:3:# Change: 黑色实心n*n正方形，尺寸n=1~4，位于通道内部但不接触网格边缘... → 多色方块移动体\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D4/3/code.py:53:# - 河道、目标、移动体三层语义清晰：绿色背景，蓝色通道，红色终点，多色 mover。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D4/3/code.py:130:    - The corner-majority color is the background, and one dominant non-background color forms a river-like corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D4/3/code.py:131:    - On that corridor sit two same-sized square objects: an interior multicolor mover and a boundary-touching solid target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D4/3/code.py:134:    - Treat the mover as one rigid n*n patch and slide it through the corridor without changing its internal colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9aaea919/D8/2/code.py:44:#     - Greying a lane can no longer happen only for red markers. Bridge lanes must be greyed after their own transfer step, and the generator must leave enough room for their temporary enlargement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D5/1/code.py:743:#   placement checks enforce a clear corridor from every emitter set to its next\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D4/2/code.py:3:# Change: 黑色实心n*n正方形，尺寸n=1~4，位于通道内部但不接触网格边缘... → 粒子像素移动体\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D4/2/code.py:14:  closed gate. Those gate pixels are visible as part of the corridor drawing but are not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D15/0/code.py:25:#   corridor, so the visual difference comes from comparing \"distance along the channel\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D15/0/code.py:355:    - The corner-majority background surrounds one blue river corridor and one detached yellow straight bar.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D19/2/code.py:60:#       straight corridor to the intended blob and outgoing rays still avoid other blobs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D15/1/code.py:3:# Change: 通过BFS在可行放置位置空间上搜索，判断目标位置是否在起点的连通分量内... → 单向通道可达性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D15/1/code.py:227:    - The corner-majority background surrounds a connected water corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D15/1/code.py:228:    - Two same-sized solid squares lie on the corridor: an interior mover square and an edge-touching destination square.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D15/1/code.py:229:    - Some straight corridor segments are recolored as cyan strips with a yellow tip; those strips are one-way, pointing from cyan toward yellow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D15/2/code.py:30:#        Source logic: previously occupied blue pixels stay blue, so the whole corridor remains.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D15/2/code.py:37:#    - The river remains a long winding corridor with repeated straight segments and several\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D15/2/code.py:237:    - The background is the corner-majority color, and a blue corridor forms the only route.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D15/2/code.py:238:    - Two same-sized solid squares sit on that corridor: a black mover near an edge and a red\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/97d7923e/D14/0/code.py:260:    \"\"\"Largest fill length that still leaves room for the bottom cap.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D13/1/code.py:4:#   → 方块尺寸由通道编码；黑/红对象本身不再显示 n，而是由其所在端点水垫可容纳的最大正方形边长给出\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D13/1/code.py:16:#   - 标记始终是 1×1，颜色仍固定为黑/红，河道仍是单一蓝色连通通道，因此视觉差异集中在“物体尺寸来自河道，而不是来自物体自身”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/97d7923e/D12/2/code.py:215:    The anchor bar (the leftmost / legend-sharing column) must leave room for a future legend of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/0/code.py:52:#      river itself connected, so the visual corridor stays coherent and the BFS still has a well-\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/0/code.py:62:#    - Keep the original single winding corridor and two solid squares; no extra markings are added.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/0/code.py:191:    - The corner-majority color is background, and a blue river carves a connected corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/0/code.py:192:    - Two solid same-sized squares lie on that corridor: an interior mover and a border-touching\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/1/code.py:46:#    - Both squares stay within the river corridor footprint used by the placement BFS.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/1/code.py:91:    Slide a solid square through a river corridor toward a same-sized dock square.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/1/code.py:99:    - Move the black square through the blue corridor using only placements where its full n×n body fits.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9aaea919/D11/1/code.py:145:    Move marked source-lane sprites into the marked destination lane until that lane runs out of room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/3/code.py:52:#    - Generator still builds one connected river corridor, places exactly two same-sized\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/3/code.py:87:    - The corner-dominant background surrounds one blue river corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/3/code.py:88:    - Two same-sized solid squares sit on that corridor: an interior mover and a border-touching destination.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9aaea919/D12/0/code.py:180:    assert placed == n_new, \"expected enough room to place all transferred sprites\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/2/code.py:44:#    - The inward merge slot is kept blue in the input, so the solver can reach it if and only if the corridor is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/2/code.py:152:    - The corner-majority background surrounds a blue river corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/2/code.py:153:    - Two same-sized solid squares sit on that corridor: one square touches exactly one border, and the other\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D15/0/code.py:403:    roomy_lb = max(side_lb, CANVAS_MAX - 5)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D15/0/code.py:404:    H = random.randint(roomy_lb, CANVAS_MAX)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D15/0/code.py:405:    W = random.randint(roomy_lb, CANVAS_MAX)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D10/0/code.py:64:#    The template is a sparse tree rather than a dense maze. Objects do not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2ba387bc/D3/2/code.py:3:# Change: 所有对象均为固定的4x4正方形，框架为1像素宽边框+2x2背景内部，实心为全色填充... → 三种类型的方块（框架、实心、十字形）\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D10/1/code.py:3:# Change: 不可达时（stuck）方块停在BFS可达的最远位置（距起点最远的可行放置点），目标方块保持不变... → 阻塞时标记通道\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D10/1/code.py:60:    - 通道仍保持单连通，避免出现多处碎片化标记。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D10/1/code.py:252:    - The corner-majority color is background. A blue river forms one connected corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D10/3/code.py:26:#    The rule change is only in the stuck branch. Objects, colors, corridor geometry,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D10/3/code.py:184:    - A dominant background color fills the corners, and one river color forms a single corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D10/3/code.py:185:    - Two same-sized solid squares lie on that corridor: the interior one is the mover, and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D12/2/code.py:32:#    chains, so the task remains legible and does not become a dense maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D10/2/code.py:239:    Move a solid square along a blue corridor toward a same-sized red endpoint, shrinking when blocked.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D10/2/code.py:247:    - The black square slides through the blue corridor using 4-neighbor top-left placements.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D6/2/code.py:62:#     - candidate next blobs must intersect that fixed ray corridor, stay within bounds, and keep\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D6/2/code.py:73:#     - the next chain blob is the only blob intersecting that ray corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D18/2/code.py:22:#      background corridor 1-2 cells inward from that gap. This produces a boundary-connected\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D18/2/code.py:24:#    - Example: a 7x7 frame may have a top-edge gap at (0,3) and an inward corridor at (1,3).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D18/2/code.py:25:#      Original logic on inner = region[1:-1,1:-1] would count that corridor as one \"hole\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D18/2/code.py:27:#      any component that touches the outer boundary. The open corridor is therefore not a hole.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D18/2/code.py:34:#    - The inward corridor is narrow (width 1, depth 1-2) so the frame remains easy to recognize\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D18/2/code.py:42:#      boundary-connected corridor can enter the interior through a border gap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D18/2/code.py:52:#      corridor, ensuring the intended enclosed-hole count is exact.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D18/2/code.py:61:#    - Each frame has only one short gap segment and one thin inward corridor, avoiding clutter.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D18/2/code.py:188:    \"\"\"Create a boundary-connected bg notch: 1-2 border-gap cells + 1-2 inward corridor cells.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D11/0/code.py:2:# Dimension: D11 — 通道结构复杂度 (obstacle)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D11/0/code.py:3:# Change: 单条蜿蜒走廊，>=3个转弯，无分叉，通过粗粒度Hamiltonian walk生成... → 带分叉通道\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D11/0/code.py:18:#    - 输入仍是方形网格，绿色背景上有蓝色通道，黑色 mover 与红色 destination\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D11/0/code.py:20:#    - 关键变化不再是“单一走廊”，而是“树形通道”：从 mover 出发先经过一段蜿蜒主干，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D11/0/code.py:28:#    - 保留 2 个同尺寸实心块与 1 个蓝色连通通道，不增加额外标记物。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D11/0/code.py:33:#    - 原 solver 假设通道是否可达由 BFS 自然决定，这在变体里仍成立；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D11/0/code.py:47:#    - 只允许一个主要分叉点，避免多个交叉口形成杂乱蓝块。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D11/0/code.py:50:#    - 颜色语义不变：蓝色是通道，黑色是被移动方块，红色是目标方块，绿色是背景。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D11/0/code.py:55:# - 通道颜色是除背景和这两个方块颜色外的主要剩余颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D6/0/code.py:339:    # 2. Canvas size (must fit frame grid + room for sprites).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D11/1/code.py:2:# Dimension: D11 — 通道结构复杂度 (obstacle)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D11/1/code.py:3:# Change: 单条蜿蜒走廊，>=3个转弯，无分叉，通过粗粒度Hamiltonian walk生成... → 环形通道\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D11/1/code.py:26:- The visible change is that the channel is no longer a single corridor. It contains one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D11/1/code.py:50:  general maze search problem.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D11/2/code.py:2:# Dimension: D11 — 通道结构复杂度 (obstacle)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D11/2/code.py:3:# Change: 单条蜿蜒走廊，>=3个转弯，无分叉，通过粗粒度Hamiltonian walk生成... → 带障碍物通道\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D11/2/code.py:19:# - 变化点是：蓝色河道不再是“只有宽窄变化的一条空走廊”，而是宽一些的通道，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D11/2/code.py:64:# - 通道由单条蜿蜒 placement 主路径膨胀得到，因此整体仍像一条主河道，而不是满屏噪声。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D1/0/code.py:66:#   - Regions are at least 3x3, so each spiral has enough room for a visible entrance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D1/2/code.py:26:#   - 例：一个 7x7 房间，左上角有红种子，右下角有绿种子。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D1/2/code.py:29:#     中间出现一条楼梯状分界线，而不是围绕房间边界的矩形环。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D1/2/code.py:42:#   - 区域仍由递归矩形切分得到，因此每个 bbox 就是真实房间，可直接在 bbox 的模板位置放种子。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D1/2/code.py:108:    Flood each wall-bounded room outward from its colored seed pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D1/2/code.py:111:    - The grid is partitioned into rooms by one wall color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D1/2/code.py:112:    - Inside each room, most cells share one base color, with a few isolated marker pixels of other colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D1/2/code.py:115:    - Treat every non-base pixel in a room as a seed and launch a simultaneous 4-neighbor BFS from all seeds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D1/2/code.py:119:    Key insight: The marker pixels are no longer entries in a boundary-depth palette; they are competing sources whose Manhattan-distance wavefronts carve the room into Voronoi-like territories.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D1/2/code.py:186:MARKER_COUNT_WEIGHTS = [1, 2, 4, 5]   # 0/1/2/3 seeds; still allows empty rooms, but favors competition\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2ba387bc/D11/2/code.py:43:#    padding to 2 so there is room to add adjacent noise without touching another\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/25/code.py:18:#    - Motion is no longer \"ray until collision\". The particle advances one corridor cell at a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/25/code.py:19:#      time. If the corridor only offers one forward continuation (including a forced bend), it\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/25/code.py:44:#      corridor topology on every step.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/25/code.py:51:#    - Template blocks stay in rows 1-3 and cols 1/4/7/10, while the corridor network starts\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/25/code.py:210:        assert path_neighbors >= 1, f\"target at ({r},{c}) must touch the corridor network\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/25/code.py:314:    # The marker first launches into the corridor using the original R,D,L,U\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/25/code.py:404:    Repaint corridor traces on a road-grid path until they reach explicit finish pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/25/code.py:408:    - Left edge: one or two isolated marker pixels in the first cycle color sit inside a col-0 corridor segment.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/25/code.py:409:    - Path area: a thin network of horizontal and vertical corridors with visible intersections.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/25/code.py:410:    - Finish cue: one removable 2x2 legend block of a distinct color plus isolated pixels of that same color embedded on the corridor network.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/25/code.py:414:    - The particle advances one corridor cell at a time. If the corridor forces a bend, it follows the bend automatically.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/25/code.py:415:    - At a junction with multiple forward continuations, the particle prefers alternating side branches: first eligible choice takes the left branch, next eligible choice takes the right branch, then left again, and so on. If the scheduled side branch does not exist, it keeps following the available corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/25/code.py:418:    Key insight: The route is determined by local corridor topology, not by ray collisions. The solver must read crossroads as decision points and use the alternating left/right side preference to pick a path through the grid toward the explicit target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/8/code.py:26:#    - Generator uses a dependency corridor:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/8/code.py:42:#      orthogonal corridors. This keeps the rule legible and avoids hidden\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/8/code.py:56:#      corridor is placed lower and farther right, so template blocks never\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/8/code.py:67:#      markers, dependency corridor, and end block. Overlap happens only where\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/8/code.py:354:        raise ValueError(\"grid too narrow for dependency corridor\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/8/code.py:370:    # Lower marker corridor and bypass around its marker cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D5/3/code.py:254:def _next_segment_room_ok(H: int, W: int, r: int, c: int, dr: int, dc: int, future_bounces: int) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D5/3/code.py:358:                    if _next_segment_room_ok(H, W, cur_r, cur_c, -cur_dr, cur_dc, bounces_left - 1):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D5/3/code.py:362:                        if _next_segment_room_ok(H, W, cur_r, cur_c, -cur_dr, cur_dc, bounces_left - 1):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D5/3/code.py:368:                    if _next_segment_room_ok(H, W, cur_r, cur_c, cur_dr, -cur_dc, bounces_left - 1):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D5/3/code.py:372:                        if _next_segment_room_ok(H, W, cur_r, cur_c, cur_dr, -cur_dc, bounces_left - 1):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D5/2/code.py:17:#    or 3-column corridor between them. Variant: paint only the center row/center column of that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D5/2/code.py:18:#    corridor, still using the starting frame's inner color. Example: two horizontally aligned\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D5/2/code.py:257:    # Force a visible bridge-width change: original would have a 3-cell-thick corridor here.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D8/2/code.py:212:_SEG_LEN_RANGE = (7, 16)        # longer minimum leaves room for pair/lone layouts\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D5/4/code.py:52:#   two bridges cannot visually share the same corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D5/4/code.py:56:#   color ids or any hidden ordering. Because only the interior of the bridge corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/11/code.py:28:#    Small trace on the generated corridor tree:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/11/code.py:75:#    The corridor tree is intentionally sparse. Unused short spurs get isolated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/11/code.py:440:    - The combo couples two stateful effects: greedy branch choice decides which local corridor survives each collision, and consumed path cells make those choices irreversible across later relaunchs from the same source.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/11/code.py:486:            ((rs, 1), (rs, cA)),          # launch corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D9/0/code.py:72:   - Only three visual layers coexist: framed squares, empty bridge corridors, and the control row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/7/code.py:44:#    recolored prefix stops early while the path corridor continues. No rule uses\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/7/code.py:48:#    dash pattern is legible inside the existing corridor. Collision marks stay\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D9/2/code.py:47:  frames, so bridges can occupy only the gap corridors and never overwrite borders.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/17/code.py:28:#     range, while two-marker scenes use a dedicated 15x15 staircase corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/17/code.py:41:#     this means `(r,1)` must be path, so every marker row belongs to the corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/17/code.py:303:    Trace alternating-turn particles through a compact thin anti-diagonal corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D2/2/code.py:45:        然后只检查“沿上方这条通道是否存在可进入的 socket”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D7/0/code.py:25:#       visible_effect: 十字形正交射线\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D3/3/code.py:59:#       room already proven by the segment endpoints.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D7/2/code.py:34:#    - Segments reserve their entire diagonal corridor, not only the drawn cells. This prevents distractors from appearing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D15/1/code.py:52:#   and that aligned frame pairs leave enough room for the bridge interval\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D8/3/code.py:178:# enough bar-side room to contain pairs like (2,4) and enough extension room to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D2/2/code.py:73:  pile of intersecting corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D17/0/code.py:105:    assert w > _LEGEND_W, \"grid must leave room for a main field\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D15/2/code.py:22:#   therefore a monotone staircase corridor made from small axis-aligned blocks instead of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D15/2/code.py:47:#   with overlap on the orthogonal axis) and whose staircase corridor is valid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D15/2/code.py:55:#   not overlap and every bridge has enough empty space for a k-thick staircase corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D1/1/code.py:20:#     - 每个已匹配结构的通道上还会放一个更近的错形红诱饵；旧题的射线规则会先撞到它，新规则必须忽略它。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D1/1/code.py:40:#     - 结构之间保留 >=4 格间隔；红诱饵只占据滑行通道，不引入额外颜色或覆盖层级。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/9/code.py:3:# Name: 碰撞十字形标记+path含内部障碍物\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/9/code.py:18:#      anti-diagonal corridor; a 2x2 end block sits in the opposite bg region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/9/code.py:19:#    - Add 1-2 internal obstacle pixels of one extra color inside the corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/9/code.py:38:#      flooding the corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/9/code.py:516:    The useful state is not just the path boundary anymore: foreign-colored pixels inside the corridor are also hard walls, and every collision leaves a visibly enlarged local mark, so obstacle-triggered turns become part of the observable output pattern.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D8/1/code.py:38:- 每条桥的通道都要求非空、在网格内、且不覆盖任何框或控制行；只允许桥与桥之间相交。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D8/3/code.py:18:#   “狗腿形”折线：先离开原通道，绕到阻挡桥的外侧 1 像素，再回到目标方块。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D8/3/code.py:31:#   单像素偏移通道都不可用，就直接丢弃该样本。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D8/3/code.py:46:# - 若后续桥梁需要绕行，则其原通道两侧至少有一侧是纯背景；生成器通过顺序模拟保证。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D10/2/code.py:47:#   marker cells stay in-bounds, never touch walls, and leave room for visible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D1/2/code.py:60:#       side and never occupy the sliding corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D13/2/code.py:20:#    in the straight corridor. The bridge therefore cannot be a raw rectangle any more. Instead it starts from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D13/2/code.py:30:#    A full arbitrary maze would be too hard to infer from 2-4 ARC examples. To keep the new behavior visible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D13/2/code.py:40:#        rectangle derived from bbox endpoints; this fails once another framed square occupies the corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D13/2/code.py:63:#    The fixed pitch leaves two blank cells between adjacent frame boxes, which is enough room for neat U-turns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D13/2/code.py:71:#    A sample is considered to exercise D13 if at least one consecutive pair has a blocked direct corridor,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D13/2/code.py:72:#    forcing the planned path to be longer than the direct Manhattan corridor between its two ports. The test\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:50:#     - 新 main() 假设 path 更接近单通道拓扑：前方通则直走，前方堵则只在左右 90 度中选。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:289:    Recolor particles as they thread through a narrow corridor, using alternating turn priority with a backup turn.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:294:    - The path itself is a thin 1-2 cell corridor, and a separate 2x2 block of another color sits in a distant background pocket.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:298:    - Because the path is a narrow corridor, the particle keeps moving straight until the corridor wall blocks its next cell; that blocked wall cell is marked with the end color if it is background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:300:    - If the preferred 90-degree turn is blocked, try the other 90-degree direction as a backup; stop only when neither side leads back into the corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:303:    - The template still only controls color order; the new challenge is topological. The path is now a forced corridor, so the important reasoning is which bend survives each wall hit, especially when the scheduled alternating turn fails and the backup side keeps the particle alive.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:322:def _corridor_is_clean(mask: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:323:    \"\"\"Reject local rooms so the path reads as a narrow 1-2 cell corridor.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:347:def _build_corridor(H: int, W: int) -> tuple[np.ndarray, int] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:348:    \"\"\"Build a single narrow serpentine corridor that guarantees an early fallback turn.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:388:    # At most one gentle width-2 bulge keeps the corridor visibly narrow instead of turning it into a room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:415:                if _corridor_is_clean(trial):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:422:    if not _corridor_is_clean(mask):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:439:    built = _build_corridor(H, W)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/13/code.py:281:    Follow a visible spiral corridor and recolor it by Manhattan distance from the start marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D6/2/code.py:44:#    Because bridges only connect lattice-adjacent path steps, the painted corridor spans only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D1/3/code.py:52:#      Dots never overlap borders or bridges in the input, and bridges only fill inter-frame corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/291dc1e1/D14/0/code.py:32:  detached, 4-connected, non-rectangular noise blobs in the background corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/291dc1e1/D14/0/code.py:86:- Noise is placed in dedicated empty corridors above, between, or below rectangle bands.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D4/3/code.py:26:#       only paint a thin strip. After docking, we instead flood the entire socket-width corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D4/3/code.py:32:#     - Variant output paints a 3-column black rectangle below it, because corridor width is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D4/3/code.py:42:#     - The corridor-width rule no longer comes from the red bbox. The solver must recover the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D4/3/code.py:46:#     - Output-first generation remains valid because the new black corridor stays inside the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D4/3/code.py:51:#     - Black only appears in opening corridors; structures keep a single non-red color; distractors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D4/3/code.py:91:def _flood_corridor_bounds(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D4/3/code.py:132:    Dock outside red blocks into the hollow sockets of large comb structures and paint a filled corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D4/3/code.py:281:        corridor = _flood_corridor_bounds((or0, oc0, or1, oc1), final_bbox, socket_cells, (dr, dc))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D4/3/code.py:282:        _paint_rect(out, corridor, black)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D4/3/code.py:291:# --------------- generator (D4 flood-corridor variant) ---------------\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D4/3/code.py:300:# Matched structures use teeth 2 or 3 so the flood corridor is visibly thicker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D4/3/code.py:586:    raise RuntimeError(\"failed to generate a valid input for 8b9c3697 D4 flood-corridor variant\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/23/code.py:71:# - In the output, some shared corridor cells continue with the lower marker's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/23/code.py:391:    - The local particle dynamics are unchanged; the new inference burden is to notice that the two left-edge markers now occupy one shared corridor with no separator, so intersections are resolved by visible later-overwrites-earlier paint rather than by forbidding overlap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D1/2/code.py:46:#    corridor between neighboring lattice squares. This keeps frames, bridges, and controls\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D14/0/code.py:32:#   The generator still constructs a self-avoiding path on a lattice, computes full-band bridge corridors,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D14/0/code.py:33:#   and rejects any scene where those corridors overlap or hit non-background cells. Thin bridges are a subset\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D14/0/code.py:34:#   of those legal corridors, so they are automatically legal once the full corridor is legal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D14/0/code.py:43:#   output still contains at most one bridge corridor per path edge. This keeps the scene readable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D15/1/code.py:129:    - The sprite shape still encodes the shot direction, but the board is no longer square, so correct reasoning must respect separate height and width limits instead of assuming symmetric edge room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D10/0/code.py:36:#    corridors of the active path, and forbids distractor frames from occupying those corridors. That\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D10/0/code.py:56:#    - Distractor frames never occupy reserved active bridge corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/12/code.py:29:#           shared corridor, so both stop before that tick is applied.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/12/code.py:75:#      * the final shared corridor is cut short because the two active particles\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/12/code.py:595:    - The puzzle is no longer independent path tracing. The decisive cue is the combination of three visible effects: bridge-style chain reactions at dead ends, later-overwrites-earlier crossings on reused trails, and a final shared-corridor truncation where the two live particles meet and freeze together.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/12/code.py:778:    \"\"\"Blend a bridge-friendly gap with a later shared corridor when possible.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D10/2/code.py:30:#    - All frames are built around 1x1 inner cells on a 4x4 inner lattice with fixed 6-cell empty corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D10/2/code.py:34:#      inside the real bridge corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D12/0/code.py:35:#    - Left and right widths are each constrained to at least 4 cells, keeping room for\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D3/2/code.py:56:element overlaps a frame, another control bar, or a bridge corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c36