n = int(rng.integers(cor_lo, cor_hi + 1))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D4/1/code.py:320:    tail_margin = int(rem - corridor_len)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D4/1/code.py:321:    return bar_side_len, corridor_len, tail_margin\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D4/1/code.py:348:    bar_side_len, corridor_len, tail_margin = layout\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D4/1/code.py:353:        target_col = sep_col + 1 + corridor_len\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D4/1/code.py:358:        target_col = sep_col - 1 - corridor_len\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D6/1/code.py:3:# Change: 两组之间完全交换颜色模式（A组获得B组的颜色，B组获得A组的颜色），同时保持尺度不变... → 颜色通道轮换\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D12/1/code.py:54:- Groups are packed using their full occupied bbox (frames plus bridge corridors), so different groups do not intersect.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D15/1/code.py:219:    row_room = (H - 1 - r) // step_len if dr == 1 else r // step_len\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D15/1/code.py:220:    col_room = (W - 1 - c) // step_len if dc == 1 else c // step_len\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D15/1/code.py:221:    return int(min(row_room, col_room))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D7/1/code.py:10:#    2. 对每一对相邻颜色，仍然在两个方块之间的对齐通道里画出同色桥梁。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D7/1/code.py:35:#    - 每段桥梁所在通道不与已有方块、桥梁冲突；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D14/1/code.py:161:        assert c0 <= c1, \"horizontal pair must have a positive corridor\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D14/1/code.py:173:        assert r0 <= r1, \"vertical pair must have a positive corridor\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D14/1/code.py:195:    - Pair the two sprites that share a scale, then fill the empty corridor between them with a two-color trail that shows the exchanged transfer colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D14/1/code.py:198:    - The same color-1 anchor box that stabilizes scale/alignment also gives a stable corridor band for the new trail; once same-scale A/B pairs are recovered, D14 is just “original swap + draw the transfer band between the paired anchors”.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:26:#       corridor cells and an outer source region. Consecutive square shells would touch and different opening positions would\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:32:#       The first annulus is a left/right corridor, the second annulus is a top/bottom corridor (or the rotated version),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:57:#     - The generator explicitly alternates between 2-layer and 3-layer templates, and between wide/tall corridor layouts, so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:58:#       the review should treat frame-depth and corridor-orientation as intentional branches even when the final 3x3 fill count\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D5/3/code.py:33:#         if both eventually use the same corridor, each keeps painting until it\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D5/3/code.py:39:#       - Visual difference: the merged corridor is only partially painted; one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D5/3/code.py:473:    Key insight: the template still explains the color cycle, but the decisive new cue is the shared corridor where one trail catches the other and truncates both traces at once.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D1/0/code.py:43:#     - 原 solver 把 `passable={floor,9}`，意味着 maroon 也可作为通道；变体中 maroon 反而应该终止视线，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D1/0/code.py:179:    - Reachability is no longer about turning through corridors. A maroon pixel can be topologically connected through the floor yet still remain untouched if it is not the first thing seen on a straight ray from the green block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/0/code.py:230:    \"\"\"Build wall barrier around dest with corridor openings, extending outward.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/1/code.py:190:    - Orange floor surrounds a fixed green 3×3 destination with one red center, and magenta walls may carve corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D3/1/code.py:191:    - Maroon pixels sit on floor cells; some are connected to the destination through open corridors and some may be trapped elsewhere.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D9/3/code.py:42:#      corridor rounds, so each launch still includes multiple collision-driven\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D9/3/code.py:46:#      a clean corridor network with one fresh outgoing branch at each stop.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dfadab01/D3/4/code.py:3:# Change: 散布在网格中的单像素标记，使用字形字典中的颜色（2、3、5、8），标记位置即字形放置的左上角... → 十字形标记编码字形类型\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D14/1/code.py:3:# Change: 每个周期位置涂1个像素——涂点是单个格子... → 涂色扩展为十字形\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D14/1/code.py:41:# - 十字形落色只发生在扩展侧，且对每个候选格单独做边界检查与背景检查，因此不会越界，也不会覆盖\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D14/1/code.py:43:# - 生成器仍采用 output-first：先放条形，再按 solver 同步的顺序模拟十字形扩展，最后清空扩展侧\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D14/1/code.py:57:#   “十字形会往上下多染 1 格”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D9/2/code.py:25:#    - Generator builds a shared elbow corridor:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D9/2/code.py:64:#      corridor, never color id.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D6/0/code.py:50:#       The new generator must instead leave spare room before the boundary and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/0/code.py:23:#   so the task is still \"collect nearest reachable maroons through corridors\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/0/code.py:104:    Key insight: The hard part is still the flood-fill reachability through wall-made corridors, but once the valid maroons are chosen, the destination path is a mirrored fill that grows from bottom-right toward top-left.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/1/code.py:31:#     corridors. The only branch we expose is the fill path, and it has exactly two\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/1/code.py:162:    - Maroon source pixels are scattered on floor cells outside the target, with some reachable through corridor openings and others potentially trapped as distractors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D2/0/code.py:28:#    corridor could zig-zag. Here the first two valid turns are Left then Left,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D2/0/code.py:29:#    so the same corridor bends into a spiral-like walk. Example: if a marker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/2/code.py:59:#     - the surrounding corridor / wall geometry remains as in the original task, avoiding clutter\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/2/code.py:108:    - Orange floor cells hold scattered maroon tokens, and magenta walls may carve corridors around the target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/2/code.py:275:    \"\"\"Build wall barrier around dest with corridor openings, extending outward.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D2/3/code.py:32:#      or enter a shorter corridor. The new solver must compare both branches\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D2/3/code.py:33:#      and choose the 6-cell corridor, producing a visibly different painted\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D2/3/code.py:59:#    The variant is observable because the changed rule alters which corridor is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D2/3/code.py:65:#    corridor gets painted, so the I/O remains readable: template in the top\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D2/3/code.py:74:#      the candidate corridors. The band generator keeps turns orthogonal and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D2/3/code.py:379:    - The hard part is no longer turn parity but local branch comparison: the solver must evaluate both candidate corridors at each collision and greedily commit to the longer straight run.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D3/0/code.py:3:# Change: 拼合后形成一个紧凑的矩形复合体，所有碎片无间隙无重叠地拼成完整矩形... → 拼合成十字形或L形\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D15/1/code.py:41:#    bridge corridors, and uses fjords/islands inside the path band as the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D2/2/code.py:37:#    - Old template placement stride 3 left no room for side symbols; generator must\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D2/4/code.py:26:#         new: 先检查向上失败，再检查向下成功，于是继续存活并沿下方通道前进。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D2/4/code.py:295:    - The visible novelty is not a new object type but the extra survival rule: failed preferred turns no longer kill the particle immediately, so some trajectories bend into a backup corridor and continue much farther.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:35:#    - Walls/corridors remain from the original task so reachability still\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:47:#      5x5 fit inside the 11x11 canvas with room for wall rings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:37:      style: optional local wall rings around each block with 2-4 corridor gaps and short outward arms\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:64:      - more containers on 11x11 would make wall corridors and fills cluttered\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D8/3/code.py:48:# - The chosen corner cell leaves room for both the rectangle and the two marker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D3/0/code.py:42:#      regular dash-gap rhythm along the same corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D5/3/code.py:324:    \"\"\"Choose a divider layout that leaves enough vertical room for ordinal legends.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D8/2/code.py:3:# Change: 红色像素的几何形态决定反射类型：单个像素=点反射中心，同行排列=水平轴，同列排列=垂直轴... → 十字形标记定义四折对称\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/247ef758/D1/0/code.py:350:    # Fixed roomy geometry is more reliable than resampling many incompatible sizes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D5/2/code.py:66:#    - Holes are rectangular and separated by at least one fg corridor, so multiple markings inside\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D8/2/code.py:4:#   → 十字形标记指示中心\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:19:#    Example: if a source token sits two corridor steps away from a destination opening, the original\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:21:#    two corridor floor cells teal, so the transport path is visible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:25:#    always builds wall-bounded corridor trees, so each reachable token has a unique route to the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:40:#    corridor tree at exactly one 4-neighbor so no loops are created. Distractor maroons are placed in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:41:#    isolated one-cell floor pockets that are not 4-adjacent to the reachable corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:43:#    The new color 8 is used only for transport trails. Because reachable tokens sit on leaf corridors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:47:#    Trails occupy narrow corridors outside the destination block and do not overlap the destination or\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:157:    - Floor openings beside the target connect into corridors; only maroons reachable through those corridors participate.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D17/0/code.py:15:  wall embedded in the corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D10/0/code.py:11:#     it is the corridor geometry: narrow rows, tighter overlaps, and more\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D10/0/code.py:26:#     2-3-cell corridor it becomes either visually muddy or topologically fragile.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D10/0/code.py:53:#     inside an already narrow corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D10/0/code.py:298:    - The motion rule is unchanged from the original task, but the thin 2-3-cell corridor makes the alternating wall-bounce pattern visible much more often than in a broad band.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b5ca7ac4/D4/1/code.py:35:#      22x22 canvas need more room for both valid scattering and non-overlapping output lanes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D2/2/code.py:44:#      This guarantees no overlap, no out-of-bounds writes, and enough room for the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D1/2/code.py:60:#      there is room. Seeing both orientations across examples makes the rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D10/2/code.py:20:#      Each obstacle sits strictly inside the corridor: it is off the grid border\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/1/code.py:43:#       path upward before it joins the rectangular corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/2/code.py:19:# the innermost corridor following the original clockwise spiral, the next ring using\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/2/code.py:30:# corridors in one color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D16/1/code.py:52:      - 任意两个红标记4连通接触，导致合并成L形/十字形歧义组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D17/0/code.py:16:#      difference is not just a preserved red dot: the nearby teal corridor bends or truncates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D13/0/code.py:519:    assert 2 <= split <= cols - 2, \"canvas must have room for both background zones\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D4/3/code.py:3:# Change: 青色十字形（中心点 + 四个方向各延伸等长臂），四个端点作为螺旋发射源... → T形或L形源（部分端点缺失）\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D4/3/code.py:23:#       - because some launchers are absent, the maze becomes visibly asymmetric\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D4/3/code.py:320:FILL_LO, FILL_HI = 0.40, 0.52          # keep the output dense enough to read as a maze\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D13/1/code.py:60:#       the corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D13/1/code.py:287:    - The local spiral rule is unchanged, but multiple visible source holes create a deterministic multi-source packing process where reading-order priority decides which spiral owns a contested corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D6/1/code.py:26:#       original: one connected clockwise spiral corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D6/1/code.py:65:#     the output shows nested boxes with black gaps, not one continuous maze\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D14/0/code.py:30:#     - generator still uses the original size formula and tip-to-border gap rule, so spirals have enough room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/64efde09/D5/1/code.py:43:#    - Marker hosts are chosen only from ports whose entire boundary corridor is clear, and each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/0/code.py:83:#    - `main()` assumes enough free room exists in the reserved strip for the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/64efde09/D5/3/code.py:390:def _clear_corridor_specs(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/64efde09/D5/3/code.py:428:        specs = _clear_corridor_specs(grid, sprite_placements, tid, stop_offset)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:62:#       - Connector corridors are kept free of other sprites, so drawing lines after\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:80:#       corridor reservation during placement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:232:def _corridor_cells(a: tuple[int, int], b: tuple[int, int]) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:243:    cells1 = _corridor_cells(a, elbow)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:244:    cells2 = _corridor_cells(elbow, b)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:249:    for r, c in _corridor_cells(a, b):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:689:def _corridor_clear(occupied: np.ndarray, line_blocked: np.ndarray, corridor: list[tuple[int, int]], sprite_port: tuple[int, int]) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:690:    for r, c in corridor:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:738:                corridor = _corridor_cells(port, sprite_port)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:739:                if _corridor_clear(occupied, line_blocked, corridor, sprite_port):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:762:                corridor = _corridor_cells(port, sprite_port)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:763:                if _corridor_clear(occupied, line_blocked, corridor, sprite_port):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:819:        for rr, cc in _corridor_cells(info[\"port\"], sprite_port):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D11/0/code.py:21:# meet already-painted corridors and must bend or terminate around them. The original\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/64efde09/D4/1/code.py:56:#     labeled port has room for an interior marker plus visible background before the boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/64efde09/D4/1/code.py:58:#     and visible from their owning active-edge cell through a clear background corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/fc7cae8d/D1/1/code.py:273:def _choose_segment_offset(room: int) -> int:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/fc7cae8d/D1/1/code.py:274:    return random.randint(0, int(room))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D7/0/code.py:24:#         - 因而螺旋只形成 2 层同心矩形通道，外圈之外保留整片黑色留白。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/64efde09/D4/3/code.py:67:      the boundary, with a clear bg-only corridor back to that edge and with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D7/2/code.py:33:#         new cells in adjacent positions across a one-pixel corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D7/2/code.py:39:#         The corridor remains as the arm boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D7/2/code.py:73:#     the change is visible as unfinished corridors and mirrored stopping fronts. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/64efde09/D16/2/code.py:49:#   - Sprites still need clear outward corridors to the boundary for their chosen\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/64efde09/D16/2/code.py:137:    - Isolated single-pixel markers sit on boundary cells, each aligned with an outward corridor from some sprite's dominant long edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/64efde09/D16/2/code.py:141:    - First move each boundary marker inward along its corridor until it lands on the nearest active-edge cell; that attached sprite cell now carries the marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D11/1/code.py:46:#    The split is visible from the blank vertical corridor between clusters, not from hidden ids.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D11/1/code.py:152:    - The components form two horizontal clusters separated by the widest empty vertical corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b0280bc/D13/0/code.py:66:#   the two highlighted routes legible instead of collapsing into one tangled shared corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/64efde09/D3/0/code.py:43:#    - Sprites still cannot overlap and still need clear boundary-facing corridors so markers are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/64efde09/D3/0/code.py:48:#    - The dashed rule is visible in every training sample because each emitted corridor contains\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/64efde09/D3/0/code.py:58:#      same-color dashed corridors in multiple places per example.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/64efde09/D3/0/code.py:231:# - Every labeled corridor must keep the marker as the first non-bg cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b0280bc/D6/1/code.py:55:#     - New marker drawing assumes enough room for distinct dots. Generator enforces 3x3 nodes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/3/code.py:272:    - The bar geometry still determines the legal corridor, but now the second green border pixel removes the old freedom to stop at any opposite-edge cell, so the route must continue until it reaches the explicit endpoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/71e489b6/D1/0/code.py:3:# Change: 方形光晕 -> 十字形标记\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a32d8b75/D6/2/code.py:279:    - Decode the marker pixel as a relative offset instead of a three-way anchor: its row/col inside the 5x5 interior specify quarter-step percentages of the remaining vertical and horizontal travel room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D14/1/code.py:21:#     the inversion obvious while preserving enough room for nontrivial sliding.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D22/1/code.py:236:    assert valid, \"emitter needs room for a hole and two walls\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D2/0/code.py:52:# - The widened right pane gives diagonal rays room without changing the left-side fitting logic.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D7/0/code.py:163:        assert stop_col >= sep + 2, f\"target on row {r} must leave room for a visible ray\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D2/3/code.py:247:        assert current_row <= top, \"bars must leave room for the incoming trunk\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D1/1/code.py:389:        assert r0 >= 1, \"output sprites must leave room for upward unsliding\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D1/1/code.py:408:        assert r0 >= 1, \"rendered sprites must have room to move upward\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D18/1/code.py:188:    assert cur_r < h - 1, \"path must still have room to reach the opposite edge\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D6/0/code.py:44:# - The generator reserves extra main-axis room after the last bar so there is at least\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:250:    \"\"\"Minimum main-axis size so blue-tip halos do not choke the corridor.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:280:    \"\"\"Valid bar length range given a blue tip and required open-side corridor.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D3/0/code.py:14:#     the visible change is that the path now hugs blue-heavy bars more closely and gives red-heavy bars more room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D3/0/code.py:33:#     cross-axis open gap is enforced as at least red_count + 1, guaranteeing a legal corridor around each bar.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D10/2/code.py:18:#      enters a progressively narrower corridor and draws nested rectangular\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D10/2/code.py:29:#      floating inner bar and a stronger \"concentric corridor\" cue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D10/2/code.py:44:#      overlap that would seal the corridor completely.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D10/2/code.py:54:#      the remaining suffix of bars, so later bars never run out of room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D10/2/code.py:71:#      leaves a traversable corridor. The helper functions below enforce both.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/71e489b6/_shared.py:18:    \"D1/0\": \"十字形标记替代方形光晕\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D4/3/code.py:61:   - Straight corridors remain azure, so green marks do not mask large regions of the board.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D17/0/code.py:57:#     and the extra vertical room required by the thicker strip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:3:# Change: 单一矩形灰色框架，框架线条均匀，内部为操作区域... → 框架为非矩形（L形或十字形）\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:50:#    - The interior support mask is built from broad bars, not thin corridors, so clipped\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D14/0/code.py:68:#     - The legend always fits because crop height is at least 8, leaving room for four legend rows inside the framed canvas.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
